ment on the acclaimed director, her former comedy partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roughly six decades after she teamed with Mike Nichols to form one of comedy’s most influential duos, Elaine May has again signed on for a Nichols project. Ms. May will direct an “American Masters” documentary about the acclaimed director, who died in November 2014 at 83. The film will debut on PBS on Jan. 29 to kick off the 30th season of “American Masters.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elaine May to Direct Mike Nichols Documentary for PBS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elaine May to Direct Mike Nichols Documentary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Elaine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nichols, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'AMERICAN MASTERS (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-01T17:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01d2e80a-854b-5da3-987a-6b02848e1228', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01d2e80a-854b-5da3-987a-6b02848e1228'}, {'abstract': 'The three Republican presidential debates have failed to provide enough information about how any of the candidates would govern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/02/us/politics/gop-debates-fail-to-give-voters-basic-details.html', 'snippet': 'The three Republican presidential debates have failed to provide enough information about how any of the candidates would govern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Republican presidential candidates’ three debates have been sometimes compelling, often contentious and always amusing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Debates Fail to Give Voters Basic Details', 'kicker': 'Letter From Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debates Fail to Give Voters Basic Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inheritance and Estate Taxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-01T17:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Albert R. Hunt | Bloomberg View', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Albert', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cc56d08-62f6-520b-88b5-edcc374e6319', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cc56d08-62f6-520b-88b5-edcc374e6319'}, {'abstract': 'The coming trials of Sheldon Silver and Dean G. Skelos will focus attention on the crisis of corruption in the state capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/02/nyregion/in-two-corruption-cases-the-culture-of-albany-will-go-on-trial.html', 'snippet': 'The coming trials of Sheldon Silver and Dean G. Skelos will focus attention on the crisis of corruption in the state capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In separate federal courthouses in Lower Manhattan this month, two of the most powerful men in New York are about to go on trial, an extraordinary spectacle centering on allegations of corruption, bribery and nepotism in the state’s highest chambers of political power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/nyregion/02ALBANY1/02ALBANY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Two Corruption Cases, the Culture of Albany Will Go on Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Albany Culture Is Put on Trial in Graft Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skelos, Dean G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-01T17:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum and Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5ab33a-f828-554a-b9b0-bb1b7c0feac1', 'word_count': 1968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5ab33a-f828-554a-b9b0-bb1b7c0feac1'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/01/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:20 P.M. THE LUNCHBOX (2014) Food from (and for) the heart: A neglected Mumbai housewife sends a home-cooked meal to her husband — and ends up pen pals with a widowed office worker after it goes astray. The great Irrfan Khan stars. It’s not a new conceit, but “the idea of two lonely souls connecting in a vast, modern metropolis, and remaining strangers even as their intimacy grows, has a durable charm,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. (Starz Cinema) (Image: Mr. Khan)', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-01T17:08:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d59a788-3033-5bb4-aca4-8e9bc80f1696', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d59a788-3033-5bb4-aca4-8e9bc80f1696'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees star continues his surprisingly strong season, only now as a World Series analyst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/02/sports/baseball/alex-rodriguez-is-an-october-surprise.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees star continues his surprisingly strong season, only now as a World Series analyst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Rodriguez, the Fox pregame-show version of himself, was sitting on a black couch in a trailer outside Citi Field on Friday night talking about the World Series. This is a new role for Rodriguez, an unexpected diversion in a journey of athletic greatness tainted by performance-enhancing drugs, and one he is excelling at. So he looked happy to be talking about baseball as he peered into his interviewer’s eyes, answered some questions, avoided some others and posed a few of his own. He discussed his love of preparation, his note-taking, his working with Pete Rose (“When it comes to baseball, he has an Ivy League mind”) and his admiration of Keith Hernandez.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 1784, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/02/sports/02SANDOMIRweb/02SANDOMIRweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Rodriguez Is an October Surprise', 'kicker': 'TV Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'October Surprise: Rodriguez Excels on Different Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': Non