: 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By TONY CENICOLA and ERIK PIEPENBURG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CENICOLA', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PIEPENBURG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7ec1014a-a141-59fa-93c5-ca5dbed30a91', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7ec1014a-a141-59fa-93c5-ca5dbed30a91'}, {'abstract': 'The publisher and activist Paige Powell shares intimate snapshots from her personal archives, which remained untouched for almost 40 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/02/t-magazine/madonna-basquiat-warhol-rare-photos.html', 'snippet': 'The publisher and activist Paige Powell shares intimate snapshots from her personal archives, which remained untouched for almost 40 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some It-girls of the ’80s may regret that their youthful glory predated social media, but Interview magazine’s former associate publisher Paige Powell doesn’t have to. Powell arrived in New York in 1980 from the Pacific Northwest, looking like a granola version of Edie Sedgwick and armed with the work ethic of Mary Tyler Moore. She was soon swept up in Interview’s bid to be a more serious publication — “At first it was more for friends, like, Fran Lebowitz drove the delivery truck to drop off issues at different newsstands,” she remembers — and Andy Warhol’s select social whirlwind of downtown clubbing, midtown shopping and uptown lunches. “Andy always said, ‘Work is fun and fun is work,’” Powell says. “It was just the way I thought New York City was, all the time, for everyone — exuberant.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Never-Before-Seen Photos of Madonna, Warhol, Basquiat and More', 'kicker': 'Art Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madonna, Warhol, Basquiat and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Art Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basquiat, Jean-Michel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haring, Keith', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warhol, Andy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-02T21:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathay Che', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Che', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9758894f-0ebd-5416-a88b-09c7df3f7bf6', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9758894f-0ebd-5416-a88b-09c7df3f7bf6'}, {'abstract': 'A scene from A. R. Gurney’s comedy about a man and his feisty new dog, on Broadway at the Cort Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/theater/in-performance-matthew-broderick-and-annaleigh-ashford-of-sylvia.html', 'snippet': 'A scene from A. R. Gurney’s comedy about a man and his feisty new dog, on Broadway at the Cort Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest In Performance video features the Tony Award-winning actors Matthew Broderick and Annaleigh Ashford in a scene from A. R. Gurney’s comedy “Sylvia,” which opened last week on Broadway at the Cort Theater. In the play, Greg (Mr. Broderick), hoping to curtail a downer of a midlife crisis, takes home a dog (Ms. Ashford) he finds wandering around Central Park one day. An unconventional love triangle — among Greg, his wife (played by Julie White) and the dog,named Sylvia — ensues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Matthew Broderick and Annaleigh Ashford of ‘Sylvia’', 'kicker': 'In Performance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sylvia (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashford, Annaleigh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broderick, Matthew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurney, A R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-02T21:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa9130d5-0513-57b1-ac91-87b5183fc574', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa9130d5-0513-57b1-ac91-87b5183fc574'}, {'abstract': 'Credit facilities can signal a transition point for a start-up as it moves to a stage with a more nuanced capital structure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/business/dealbook/wework-said-to-seek-750-million-credit-facility.html', 'snippet': 'Credit facilities can signal a transition point for a start-up as it moves to a stage with a more nuanced capital structure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WeWork, which rents out offices and desks to freelancers and budding companies, has been on a fund-raising tear.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'