enjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dornford-May, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "A Midsummer Night's Dream (Opera)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-02T21:49:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ca0d76f-dad0-58fc-86b0-c44f542131c8', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ca0d76f-dad0-58fc-86b0-c44f542131c8'}, {'abstract': 'The law would not, as opponents contend, empower sexual predators or make public restrooms less safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/opinion/support-houstons-equal-rights-ordinance.html', 'snippet': 'The law would not, as opponents contend, empower sexual predators or make public restrooms less safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, Houston voters will be asked if they want to keep or repeal the city’s strong and enlightened equal rights ordinance, which was approved by the City Council last year and put on hold pending this week’s vote. Opponents of the law have perversely turned a broad, sensible measure  that protects people from discrimination in employment, city services, housing and public accommodations, among other things, into a debate about sexual predators in women’s restrooms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/opinion/03tue3web/03tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl