 concessions game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sports stadiums across America are upping the ante on their culinary offerings. At Seattle’s CenturyLink Field, Seahawks fans are feasting on fries with crab sauce and locally sourced sausages from the Pike Place Market butcher shop Uli’s. At Portland’s Moda Center, home of the N.B.A.’s Trail Blazers, on draft is Widmer Brothers’ Upheaval IPA (the arena pours 70 percent craft beers), which pairs well with Bunk Sandwiches’ New Orleans-style muffuletta. At Philadelphia’s Lincoln Financial Field, Eagles enthusiasts are eating gourmet pizzas by the James Beard Award-winner Marc Vetri. But leading the pack is the 49ers’ new $1.3 billion Levi’s Stadium in Santa Clara, Calif. About 75 percent of the food is local, and 26 vegan items are on offer, including a vegetarian take on a pulled pork sandwich with smoked jackfruit.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-stadium-t/04tmag-stadium-t-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-stadium-t/04tmag-stadium-t-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-stadium-t/04tmag-stadium-t-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-stadium-t/04tmag-stadium-t-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-mag