', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04WILESJP1/04WILESJP1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04WILESJP1/04WILESJP1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'BalletNext and Abraham.In.Motion Experiment With Jazz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Ballet Asks Jazz to Dance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiles, Michele', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kyle Abraham/Abraham.In.Motion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Next Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T18:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b88e88-cc96-5d60-aa6d-314ba8fb0d0c', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b88e88-cc96-5d60-aa6d-314ba8fb0d0c'}, {'abstract': 'Also: Dominique Bistro opens in the West Village; Chelsea Market adds kiosks; and I Trulli eliminates tipping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/04/dining/cassette-greenpoint-french-catalonian-flavor.html', 'snippet': 'Also: Dominique Bistro opens in the West Village; Chelsea Market adds kiosks; and I Trulli eliminates tipping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cassette In their new venture, Henry Rich and the chef Joe Pasqualetto move from the rustic Italian they feature at Rucola in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn, to southwestern French, with some Catalonian flavors. Vegetables dominate in dishes like roasted peppers with white anchovies, potatoes with salsa verde, roasted acorn squash with red rice, and pasta with tomatoes, toasted garlic and salt cod. Desserts include crème Catalan, the Spanish take on crème brûlée. The wines of the region are well represented and well priced, with about a dozen under $50. Perry Chen, a founder of Kickstarter, which happens to be just around the corner, is also a partner. Unlike the cozy, cluttered Rucola, this restaurant is airy and spacious, with big windows: 113 Franklin Street (Kent Street), Greenpoint, Brooklyn, 347-682-4111, cassettebk.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/dining/04OFF/04OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cassette Brings French-Catalonian Flavors to Greenpoint', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cassette (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dominique Bistro (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T18:55:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b0ba9d4-2847-5850-afe0-29911e378783', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b0ba9d4-2847-5850-afe0-29911e378783'}, {'abstract': 'The population of little penguins on an island in Australia has bounced back thanks to the vigilance of a few sheepdogs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/world/australia/australia-penguins-sheepdogs-foxes-swampy-marsh-farmer-middle-island.html', 'snippet': 'The population of little penguins on an island in Australia has bounced back thanks to the vigilance of a few sheepdogs.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Massacred,” read the banner headline in the local newspaper — just the single word, as if describing an act of war. Below it was a photo of dead penguins and other birds, the latest casualties in Australia’s long history of imported species’ decimating native wildlife.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/world/australia/05penguins01/05penguins01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia Deploys Sheepdogs to Save a Penguin Colony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guard Dogs Help a Penguin Colony Back From the Brink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Penguins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Oddball (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Australia', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/783a6dc8-5ec9-5643-af4d-3a10d459e8fb', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/783a6dc8-5ec9-5643-af4d-3a10d459e8fb'}, {'abstract': 'The indie brand Calico Wallpaper has teamed up with Print All Over Me and the Brooklyn concept store Swords-Smith on an inaugural capsule collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/t-magazine/clothes-wallpaper-williamsburg-sword-smith.html', 'snippet': 'The indie brand Calico Wallpaper has teamed up with Print All Over Me and the Brooklyn concept store Swords-Smith on an inaugural capsule collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comparing someone’s outfit to wallpaper isn’t normally a compliment — but that may change today, as Calico Wallpaper launches a collaboration. With the custom clothier Print All Over Me, the cultish indie brand’s stylish, nature-inspired patterns have been translated into a limited-edition capsule collection, sold exclusively by the Brooklyn concept shop Swords-Smith. It’s the second time Calico and Print All Over Me have teamed up, though it’s the first with any fanfare: As Nick Cope, the co-founder of Calico alongside his wife Rachel, explains, “We had them unofficially design our tradeshow uniforms that harmonized with our booth” at this year’s Design Week NYC back in May. And as for Swords-Smith, the shop isn’t just shilling the goods; its founders (also a married couple, Briana Swords and R Smith) were integral in developing the concept. “I loved Calico’s wallpaper,” Swords says. “Every time I saw it, I thought to myself, ‘I would love this on a dress.’”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-calico/03tmag-calico-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-mag