ities exhumed the bodies of Czar Nicholas II and Empress Alexandra for new DNA tests. Last week, the Russians said the body of the czar’s father, Alexander III, would be dug up for testing, too.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/world/04romania/04romania-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romania Places the Heart of a Queen in Her Castle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Royal Resting Place for Romanian Queen’s Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marie, Queen of Romania (1875-1938)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palaces and Castles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Victoria, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T19:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Gillet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6412a04f-1cce-5026-b036-965192dba8bd', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6412a04f-1cce-5026-b036-965192dba8bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Education Department has said that requiring a transgender student to change behind a curtain violates Title IX. How are bathrooms, locker rooms and showers used at your child’s school? What are the rules set around bathrooms and locker rooms, and how have the conversations around that gone where you live?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/what-is-the-locker-room-policy-for-transgender-students-at-your-childs-school/', 'snippet': 'The Education Department has said that requiring a transgender student to change behind a curtain violates Title IX. How are bathrooms, locker rooms and showers used at your child’s school? What are the rules set around bathrooms and locker rooms,...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal education authorities found Monday that an Illinois school district violated antidiscrimination laws when it did not allow a transgender student who identifies as a girl and participates on a girls’ sports team to change and shower in the girls’ locker room without restrictions. Instead, the student, who identifies as female but was born male, is required to change beyond privacy curtains in the girls’ locker room and to shower separately.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 1935, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/locker-promo/locker-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is the Locker-Room Policy for Transgender Students at Your Child’s School?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T19:38:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd6cc1b2-1c00-5bb5-9dbe-754b5719af56', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd6cc1b2-1c00-5bb5-9dbe-754b5719af56'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cohn, the company’s president, said Goldman Sachs had evolved from private partnership to bank holding company and would find new ways to work in the shifting environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/04/business/dealbook/gary-cohn-says-goldman-sachs-will-adapt-to-survive.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cohn, the company’s president, said Goldman Sachs had evolved from private partnership to bank holding company and would find new ways to work in the shifting environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Challenges have sprung up across Wall Street, making life more difficult for the industry’s big banks. But the president of Goldman Sachs, Gary D. Cohn, insists that the company will adapt and survive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04conference-cohn-web2/04conference-cohn-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04conference-cohn-web2/04conference-cohn-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non