 through is the better part of valor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, with my latest broadside on matters Catholics\xa0filed and published, I drove with my family up into northwestern Connecticut\xa0— just for the drive, no particular destination in mind. We ended up stopping for mass at a shrine near Litchfield, built in imitation and honor of Lourdes, that I’d visited occasionally many years earlier with my parents. The place was mostly unchanged: A big expanse of land, gray and somewhat forbidding on a cloudy day with the trees half-gone toward winter; a grotto where they have outdoor masses in warmer weather; a long stations of the cross ascending a wooded hill to a lifesize Calvary; and various gift shops and outbuildings scattered around the grounds. One of the outbuildings doubles as a chapel, and that’s where the All Saints Day mass was held: In a crowded, close, carpeted space, with a mostly-gray haired congregation (we were some of the youngest people there) dressed in suburban- Catholic casual and packed into too-small chairs\xa0on three sides of the altar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catholicism For the Time Being', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crosses and Crucifixes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilgrimages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John Paul II', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Litchfield (Conn)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Medjugorje (Bosnia and Herzegovina)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T20:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fda8348-ceba-5f53-bedb-940700f6e7d1', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fda8348-ceba-5f53-bedb-940700f6e7d1'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Earnest, the White House press secretary, suggested that politics had driven the request by TransCanada to suspend the review of the proposed Keystone XL pipeline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000004016336/white-house-on-keystone-project.html', 'snippet': 'Josh Earnest, the White House press secretary, suggested that politics had driven the request by TransCanada to suspend the review of the proposed Keystone XL pipeline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Earnest, the White House press secretary, suggested that politics had driven the request by TransCanada to suspend the review of the proposed Keystone XL pipeline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/multimedia/keystone/keystone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/multimedia/keystone/keystone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/multimedia/keystone/keystone-jumbo.jpg', 'he