e', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7c855ff3-8e91-5369-9b02-bed71e2805c6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7c855ff3-8e91-5369-9b02-bed71e2805c6'}, {'abstract': 'The company said it had underreported the carbon dioxide emitted by 800,000 diesel- and some gasoline-powered cars, and would set aside $2.2 billion to cover the cost of the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/04/business/vw-discloses-new-emissions-problem-involving-carbon-dioxide.html', 'snippet': 'The company said it had underreported the carbon dioxide emitted by 800,000 diesel- and some gasoline-powered cars, and would set aside $2.2 billion to cover the cost of the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Volkswagen’s pollution problems took a costly new turn on Tuesday when the company said it had understated emissions of carbon dioxide, a greenhouse gas, for about 800,000 of its vehicles sold in Europe, and overstated the cars’ fuel economy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/business/04vwcarbon-web3/04vwcarbon-web3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'VW Reveals It Misstated Emissions of Gas Cars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'VW Reveals It Misstated Emissions of Gas Cars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowley, Graham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diesel Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Emissions (Transportation)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T21:32:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea35ec18-315e-52bc-9d4a-aa440d97403a', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea35ec18-315e-52bc-9d4a-aa440d97403a'}, {'abstract': 'Paintings in a new show of Troy Brauntuch’s early work come on loan from the collections of Larry Gagosian, Robert Longo and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/03/t-magazine/troy-brauntuch-petzel-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Paintings in a new show of Troy Brauntuch’s early work come on loan from the collections of Larry Gagosian, Robert Longo and more.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’re in, you’re out, you’re up, you’re down,” the painter Troy Brauntuch says, with his trademark disarming self-deprecation. “Privately, one always goes on.” Nearly 40 years ago, Brauntuch had a flash of big-shot fame: he was one of five artists (alongside Jack Goldstein, Sherrie Levine, Robert Longo and Philip Smith) included in the influential 1977 group show “Pictures,” curated at Artists Space by Douglas Crimp. The show came to represent the brewing movement of image-based artists — those who “had a broader perspective of how we read images, and really entered the picture again, and what that means,” Brauntuch says. “Pictures” operated as a bellwether, in stark contrast to then-fashionable Minimalism and abstraction. “We came out of a time when ‘art’ was not what we were doing, which is why we were doing what we were doing.” His years in New York in the late ’70s and 1980s were spent running up the ladder alongside his friends, like Cindy Sherman, Matt Mullican, David Salle, Goldstein and Longo, whose careers exploded onto the superstar level. He counted Richard Prince and Dike Blair among his golfing buddies, too. “We played religiously,” Brauntuch says. “We also played in a poker game for decades.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Influential, Late-’70s Paintings, Revisited', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T21:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225f9580-a467-585b-b814-5dfc33aea156', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225f9580-a467-585b-b814-5dfc33aea156'}, {'abstract': 'Greece and Elsewhere: Pictures of the Day', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/11/03/blogs/pictures-of-the-day-greece-and-elsewhere.html', 'snippet': 'Greece and Elsewhere: Pictures of the Day', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greece and Elsewhere: Pictures of the Day', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/blogs/20151103pod-slide-KDUY/20151103pod-slide-KDUY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/blogs/20151103pod-slide-KDUY/20151103pod-slide-KDUY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/blogs/20151103pod-slide-KDUY/20151103pod-