roft.html', 'snippet': 'For a new collaboration with yoox.com, the performance artist and photographer Vanessa Beecroft mined inspiration from Walter Benjamin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1936, the German critic Walter Benjamin published “The Work of Art in the Age of Mechanical Reproduction,” a seminal essay that’s arguably even more influential in 2015 than it was eight decades ago. Now, Benjamin’s observations on authorship, authenticity and capital have found their way into Vanessa Beecroft’s photographic series for yoox.com, the Italian e-commerce retailer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/t-magazine/03tmag-beecroft1/03tmag-beecroft1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artistic Homage to a Classic Work of Philosophy', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yoox Group SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T22:57:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8233d236-ab91-5602-8588-eab24757dbeb', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8233d236-ab91-5602-8588-eab24757dbeb'}, {'abstract': 'In this novel, set in 2022, an Islamic party sweeps into power and the country undergoes a radical transformation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/04/books/review-michel-houellebecqs-submission-imagines-france-as-a-muslim-state.html', 'snippet': 'In this novel, set in 2022, an Islamic party sweeps into power and the country undergoes a radical transformation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Published in France on Jan. 7, the day of the terrorist attacks on the satirical magazine Charlie Hebdo, Michel Houellebecq’s new book, “Submission” — a novel set in 2022 in which an Islamic party sweeps into power in France and Islamic law is embraced — became an instant best seller there and the center of a heated debate over the lines between satire and Islamophobia, free-expression and hate-mongering.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 920, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 920}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1337, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-cover/04BOOKHOUELLEBECQ-1446578216926-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Michel Houellebecq’s ‘Submission’ Imagines France as a Muslim State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Radical  Conversion  in France   ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houellebecq, Michel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Submission (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-03T22:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/57f50b36-53d8-52c5-97ad-fe6d94d980b5', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57f50b36-53d8-52c5-97ad-fe6d94d980b5'}, {'abstract': 'Frederick Wiseman’s documentary about this Queens neighborhood advances the idea that it is people — in streets and stores, in barbershops and laundromats — who make a city great.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/04/movies/review-in-jackson-heights-an-ode-to-the-immigrant-experience.html', 'snippet': 'Frederick Wiseman’s documentary about this Queens neighborhood advances the idea that it is people — in streets and stores, in barbershops and laundromats — who make a city great.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All of creation converges in “In Jackson Heights,” a thrilling, transporting love letter from Frederick Wiseman to New York and its multi-everything glory. Set in the Queens neighborhood of its title — where people from across the globe are staking a claim on America while speaking Spanish, Tibetan and Punjabi — Mr. Wiseman’s latest documentary is a movingly principled, political look at a dynamic neighborhood in which older waves of pioneers make room for new, amid creeping gentrification. It’s an immigration story, so it goes without saying that it is also about New York and the United States — that “teeming nation of nations,” to steal a phrase from Walt Whitman.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 318}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1070, 'width': 2019, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/arts/04INJACK/04INJACK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘In Jackson Heights,’ an Ode to the Immigrant Experience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kaleidoscopic Ode to an Immigrant Neighborhood     ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiseman, Frederi