ion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/world/europe/romania-victor-ponta-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'Already under indictment for graft, Victor Ponta was stepping down after more than 20,000 people marched in Bucharest, the capital, to demand his resignation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUCHAREST, Romania — Huge protests, some of the largest since the fall of communism, toppled the government of Romania on Wednesday, five days after a fire at a nightclub killed 32 people and set off a wave of outrage over corruption and ineptitude.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victor Ponta, Romania’s Premier, Steps Down After Outcry Over Corruption', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yielding to Outcry Over Corruption, Romanian Prime Minister Steps Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponta, Victor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bucharest (Romania)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T10:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Gillet and Palko Karasz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname'