nt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastert, J Dennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T11:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67814091-613e-5b87-b525-b865ae72f2e9', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67814091-613e-5b87-b525-b865ae72f2e9'}, {'abstract': 'The House schedule for next year will contain just 25 full four-day or five-day work weeks, and the Senate will have a similarly abridged schedule, largely because of time off for political conventions and campaigning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/04/2016-legislative-calendars-leave-plenty-of-room-for-campaigning/', 'snippet': 'The House schedule for next year will contain just 25 full four-day or five-day work weeks, and the Senate will have a similarly abridged schedule, largely because of time off for political conventions and campaigning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rank-and-file House Republicans have been demanding a greater role in legislating — and more amendments — which means longer debates and workdays at the Capitol. And Speaker Paul D. Ryan seems prepared to oblige. But election years also present their own special scheduling imperatives, given the need for lawmakers to defend their seats. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/03/us/03firstdraftnl-schedule2/03firstdraftnl-schedu