y much including alcohol. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heartland of Darkness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T14:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26ea61d0-5873-590f-a512-165c311e5a9e', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ea61d0-5873-590f-a512-165c311e5a9e'}, {'abstract': 'The WhatsApp site offers instructions for emailing the contents of a conversation in a file to yourself — which could then be printed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/technology/personaltech/an-easy-way-to-use-whatsapp.html', 'snippet': 'The WhatsApp site offers instructions for emailing the contents of a conversation in a file to yourself — which could then be printed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. My daughter has been living in South America for the last year and we communicate daily via WhatsApp on our iPhones. Our text history is a wonderful diary of her experiences there and I would like to be able to save them to my computer and print them out for us to enjoy in the future. Is there a simple way to do this?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/05/technology/05askk-web/05askk-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/05/technology/05askk-web/05askk-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty