 Phillips and Juliette Binoche, deep underground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the first day of shooting “The 33,” the Mexican director Patricia Riggen sat in her chair in the cave that served as the movie’s set. “And bicckk! A stone falls on top of my head,” she recalled. “Fortunately, I had my hard hat on. But it makes me realize where I am and what it means to be there.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT1/1108SNAPSHOT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patricia Riggen, Director of ‘The 33,’ on Shooting in a Mine', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watch for Falling Rocks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riggen, Patricia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The 33 (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T16:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/938eb375-39a2-50fe-906a-ccb7f5dcb71c', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/938eb375-39a2-50fe-906a-ccb7f5dcb71c'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Redford and Zero Mostel are among the cast members in this 1972 caper comedy screening at Film Forum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/08/movies/in-the-hot-rock-gems-on-view-before-their-time.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Redford and Zero Mostel are among the cast members in this 1972 caper comedy screening at Film Forum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s never been clear why “The Hot Rock,” the New York caper comedy directed by Peter Yates, didn’t get more love at its 1972 release. (Maybe because the city was simply an unfunny tableau of urban decline, not yet the object of nostalgic affection it would become.) Even so, the film, about unpolished jewel thieves trying to snatch a spectacular diamond for an interested buyer, is an embarrassment of riches: It featured William Goldman’s script, adapted from the Donald E. Westlake novel, as well as a top-shelf cast — Robert Redford playing straight man to George Segal, Paul Sand and Ron Leibman, all eclipsed by vintage late-period Zero Mostel. And the city was virtually a featured character itself.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1492, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD4/08WEEKAHEAD4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘The Hot Rock,’ Gems on View Before Their Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film; A Cast of Gems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Forum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yates, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Hot Rock (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T16:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68df60b9-7b49-5e1e-95cb-afba98b0c484', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68df60b9-7b49-5e1e-95cb-afba98b0c484'}, {'abstract': 'The troupe is known for its fiery mix of ballet, flamenco, cha-cha, rumba, bolero and salsa dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/08/arts/dance/lizt-alfonso-dance-cuba-blends-dance-traditions.html', 'snippet': 'The troupe is known for its fiery mix of ballet, flamenco, cha-cha, rumba, bolero and salsa dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s always a hot night in Havana wherever and whenever Lizt Alfonso Dance Cuba performs. In her “Cuba Vibra!,” Ms. Alfonso’s Havana-based company, in only 95 minutes, will celebrate the development of Cuban music and dance from the 1950s to the present with the aid of 18 dancers and an onstage big band. The troupe, founded by Ms. Alfonso in 1991 as an all-female group, now includes men.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD3