ing for an in-the-meantime nibble, Isaac’s has developed an unexpected following among those unaware of or indifferent to the laws of kashrut.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Brooklyn Bakery Appeals to Observant Jews and Pizza Fans ', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Observant Jews and Fidgety Pizza Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koenig, Leah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Isaac's Bake Shop (Brooklyn, NY, Bakery)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midwood (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kosher Foods and Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T16:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Koenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1b28191-5ab4-5ce6-8cf4-8dfdecbc95ca', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1b28191-5ab4-5ce6-8cf4-8dfdecbc95ca'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gerhaher and his pianist, Gerold Huber, will perform Haydn, Beethoven and Schoenberg on Nov. 10, the same night as Ms. Bullock’s museum recital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/08/arts/music/christian-gerhaher-at-park-avenue-armory-and-julia-bullock-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gerhaher and his pianist, Gerold Huber, will perform Haydn, Beethoven and Schoenberg on Nov. 10, the same night as Ms. Bullock’s museum recital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among chamber music fans, the baritone Christian Gerhaher is considered the uncontested heir to Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau at the helm of the German lied tradition. On Tuesday, Nov. 10, he and his longtime pianist, Gerold Huber, return to the elegant Board of Officers Room at the Park Avenue Armory, which they inaugurated with an all-Schumann recital two years ago. This time, they bring their probing musicianship to the Viennese tradition with a program spanning songs by Haydn, Beethoven, Schoenberg and Berg. (7:30 p.m., parkavenuearmory.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/arts/08WEEKAHEAD2/08WEEKAHEAD2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 15