11/05/business/dealbook/time-warner-may-have-left-door-ajar-for-a-fox-return.html', 'snippet': 'Time Warner’s stock trades below the 2014 offer price from 21st Century Fox and at a discount to peers, making it vulnerable to a fresh takeover approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time Warner may have left its henhouse gate open to Fox. Its chief executive, Jeffrey L. Bewkes, last year thwarted an $80 billion takeover bid from Rupert Murdoch’s rival media company with some bold projections. Mr. Bewkes is now backing down from those claims and could be vulnerable to a fresh approach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time Warner May Have Left Door Ajar for a Fox Return', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '21st Century Fox', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bewkes, Jeffrey L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T20:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saba', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saba', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c951f625-5377-5c78-aac9-8a5d8b4a7e0f', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c951f625-5377-5c78-aac9-8a5d8b4a7e0f'}, {'abstract': 'Ruling that individuals should have the right to grow and distribute marijuana for personal use, the court waded into the debate on the war on drugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.c