 same moment as the\xa0“Charlie Hebdo”\xa0massacre\xa0— that the dystopia is the Islamicized France, that Houellebecq is trying to do for Islamism or “Eurabia” what Orwell once did for Stalinism. But if you’ve read the keener reviews\xa0(or Houellebecq’s previous novels) you probably understand that no, actually, the dystopia is the contemporary West, and\xa0the Islamified future that Houellebecq’s story ushers in\xa0is portrayed as a kind of civilizational step forward, or if you prefer a necessary regression back to health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Houellebecq’s Islam, Houellebecq’s West', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houellebecq, Michel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Front (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T20:31:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62cf383-5d84-5433-b20f-67e7c7113175', 'word_count': 1765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62cf383-5d84-5433-b20f-67e7c7113175'}, {'abstract': 'A federal complaint charges Pagedale, Mo., near Ferguson, with turning its municipal court into a revenue-generating machine by issuing housing code violations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/us/lawsuit-accuses-missouri-city-of-fining-homeowners-to-raise-revenue.html', 'snippet': 'A federal complaint charges Pagedale, Mo., near Ferguson, with turning its municipal court into a revenue-generating machine by issuing housing code violations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PAGEDALE, Mo. — This spring, officials in this tiny city near St. Louis ordered Valarie Whitner to replace her siding; repaint her gutters, downspout and foundation; and put up screens or storm covers outside every window and blinds or curtains on the inside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/04/us/05pagedale-web1/05pagedale-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna