GELES — Music-themed documentaries made their mark as the International Documentary Association announced nominees, and some winners, for its annual documentary awards, to be presented in Los Angeles on Dec. 5.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Amy’ Among Nominees for Documentary Film Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gracia, Chad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Stanley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Notaro, Tig', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppenheimer, Joshua', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riley, Stevan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Documentary Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T21:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e57e8220-93b7-5d1f-aa39-9346f251a899', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e57e8220-93b7-5d1f-aa39-9346f251a899'}, {'abstract': 'Some academics say managing a company based on the immediate need to meet shareholder expectations can be perilous, but others say it can discourage complacency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/business/dealbook/the-risks-and-rewards-of-short-termism.html', 'snippet': 'Some academics say managing a company based on the immediate need to meet shareholder expectations can be perilous, but others say it can discourage complacency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debate has been raging in various forms for the last 30 years — whether corporate short-termism is a problem and, if it is, is it hurting American businesses and the economy? Short-termism is exactly what it sounds like: companies managed for the short term, with decisions driven by the need to meet shareholder expectations about quarterly earnings and stock prices.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Risks and Rewards of Short-Termism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Risk and Reward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-04T21:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c9a3bd6-1f34-5ebd-b1bc-6969a65705aa', 'word_count': 1408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c9a3bd6-1f34-5ebd-b1bc-6969a65705aa'}, {'abstract': 'The company, propelled by its enormous user base, said mobile advertising now accounts for 78 percent of ad revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/technology/facebook