tary wants that work to continue,” John Kirby, the department spokesman, said, referring to Secretary of State John Kerry. In a letter to Mr. Kerry, TransCanada said a delay would allow time for a review by Nebraska. Environmental groups said the request is a bid to avert President Obama’s expected rejection of the pipeline. TransCanada said on Wednesday that it respected the State Department’s decision and would continue pressing to show that the pipeline is “in the national interest of the United States.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Dept. Denies Request for Delay on Pipeline Review', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Dept. Denies Request for Delay on Pipeline Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirby, John F', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T01:24:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a530c62f-73ae