: 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5a493c-756b-56a4-bbd3-0e057c0a9cc5', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5a493c-756b-56a4-bbd3-0e057c0a9cc5'}, {'abstract': 'International transmission of failure.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/currency-wars-at-the-zlb/', 'snippet': 'International transmission of failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ricardo Caballero, Emmanuel Farhi, and Pierre-Olivier Gourinchas have a new theoretical paper on how to think about a worldwide liquidity trap. I’m still working through the analytics, but it’s clearly consistent with the kind of thing I’ve been saying for years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Currency Wars at the ZLB', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T13:59:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e84c2af-fc28-575d-8728-4c6ce10ea016', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e84c2af-fc28-575d-8728-4c6ce10ea016'}, {'abstract': 'Thom Browne, Francisco Costa and more pick works for an auction sponsored by the CFDA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/t-magazine/cfda-paddle-eight-auction.html', 'snippet': 'Thom Browne, Francisco Costa and more pick works for an auction sponsored by the CFDA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art and fashion are famously symbiotic — but a new auction shows just how much designers have drawn influences from works of art. For a new sale on the site Paddle8, 20 American designers — including Michael Kors, Thom Browne, Francisco Costa and Diane von Furstenberg — have each picked one piece of art that has influenced their work; the proceeds of the sale will go to benefit the CFDA and its programs. (The Alice + Olivia designer Stacey Bendet Eisner has even donated a Francesco Clemente painting.) Click through the slide show here to see the work that inspires each designer — and why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twenty Designers on the Art That Inspires Them', 'kicker': 'Fashion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Fashion Designers of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paddle8 Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08b06a74-16d2-5485-a7b8-eb04f83efa48', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08b06a74-16d2-5485-a7b8-eb04f83efa48'}, {'abstract': 'An online campaign by the French designer Olivier Rousteing brought out his fans, and the limited collection sold out in Paris in less than three hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/fashion/release-of-hm-x-balmain-collection-creates-chaos-in-london.html', 'snippet': 'An online campaign by the French designer Olivier Rousteing brought out his fans, and the limited collection sold out in Paris in less than three hours.', 'lead_paragrap