'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T16:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. A. Hanks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Hanks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c0bf55-8547-56d2-8449-ade4055d9905', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c0bf55-8547-56d2-8449-ade4055d9905'}, {'abstract': 'A box of chocolates or some hand towels are nice, but if your hosts enjoy wine, what better gift than a well-chosen bottle?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/dining/wine-gift-thanksgiving-2015.html', 'snippet': 'A box of chocolates or some hand towels are nice, but if your hosts enjoy wine, what better gift than a well-chosen bottle?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A good Thanksgiving guest has one responsibility and one elective. The responsibility is to carry out with good will whatever tasks, if any, have been assigned. The elective (and let’s face it, good manners would call this a responsibility, too) is to bring a little something for the hosts.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 580}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1978, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/dining/11POUR/11POUR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wine Gift Options Abound for Thanksgiving', 'kicker': 'The Pour', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '... And to Bring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T16:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/940348d3-1637-5c60-bd0e-3de34aee12ed', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/940348d3-1637-5c60-bd0e-3de34aee12ed'}, {'abstract': 'The juror was dismissed after she complained that her employer had said she would be paid for only her first 10 days of service in what is expected to be a six-week trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/1