tps://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/world/europe/migrants-germany.html', 'snippet': 'With some 758,400 newly arrived asylum seekers, Germany faces the daunting task of trying to integrate people from vastly different cultures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — How to get along in Germany: Follow its laws, including showing respect for all religions, especially in the case of Jews, to whom the country has a historical obligation. Don’t be late. Do shake hands. And learn a few basic phrases, from “Cheers” to “I don’t eat pork.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany 101: Refugees Get Guidebook to Their New Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany Gives Migrants Guide to a New Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Adenauer, Konrad, Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T19:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aa562b0-c58e-53fe-a443-a5717444feaf', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aa562b0-c58e-53fe-a443-a5717444feaf'}, {'abstract': 'But the hype machine of Silicon Valley has reasons for wanting you to think so.', '