236d-5319-908d-3a8586d0294a'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Ayumi Tanaka’s careful, nostalgic compositions are inspired by half-remembered moments from her childhood in a Japanese village.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/05/t-magazine/japanese-photo-collages-ayumi-tanaka.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Ayumi Tanaka’s careful, nostalgic compositions are inspired by half-remembered moments from her childhood in a Japanese village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Encountering the photographer Ayumi Tanaka’s series “Wish You Were Here” feels like stepping into her subconscious: Though the images and themes might not be yours, the feelings they evoke are familiar. Tanaka constructs three-dimensional dioramas, composed of overlapping multiple layers of photo collages, assembled and photographed to illustrate the “landscapes of my memory,” as she puts it: images that might serve as jumping-off points for all sorts of fairy-tales. The artist constructs her collages with family photos taken when she was growing up in a small village in the mountains of Japan; more recent personal snapshots; self-portraits; and pictures of everyday objects taken from the Internet that become symbols evocative of her childhood memories. The artist herself takes on a poetic tone when discussing her work. “At times in my day-to-day life, I find myself stumbling over reminders of days gone by. Partly formed memories rise up from a forgotten abyss within, surrounding me like a powerful fragrance and rocking my emotions to the core,” she says. “In these moments, I am seized with the desire to gather and collect, to retrieve what has been lost and weave it into something whole.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreamlike Photo Collages, Created From Memory', 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T21:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Hirsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6372af1-b417-5bac-8cfe-403083d97c50', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6372af1-b417-5bac-8cfe-403083d97c50'}, {'abstract': 'A day earlier, a former Federal Reserve Bank of New York employee pleaded guilty to an identical charge in the same case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/business/dealbook/former-goldman-employee-pleads-guilty-in-leak-case.html', 'snippet': 'A day earlier, a former Federal Reserve Bank of New York employee pleaded guilty to an identical charge in the same case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Highlighting the hazards of Wall Street’s revolving door with regulatory agencies, a former employee of Goldman Sachs pleaded guilty on Thursday for obtaining documents leaked to him by a former colleague at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Goldman Employee Pleads Guilty in Leak Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bansal, Rohit', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '201