D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 903, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 903}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/science/10obs-poppy/10obs-poppy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientists Engineer a Plant to Reject Its Own Pollen', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Botany: Engineering a Plant to Reject Its Own Pollen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poppies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Birmingham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-05T21:24:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caeb06ce-4d14-531b-a01c-c8a0ffaad73f', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caeb06ce-4d14-531b-a01c-c8a0ffaad73f'}, {'abstract': 'HSBC caused an uproar by suggesting it might move its headquarters to Hong Kong. But it makes more sense for its London-based peer Barclays to move to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/business/dealbook/why-barclays-may-want-to-mull-a-move-to-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'HSBC caused an uproar by suggesting it might move its headquarters to Hong Kong. But it makes more sense for its London-based peer Barclays to move to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HSBC has caused a scene by suggesting it might move its headquarters from London. But it is rival Barclays that really ought to consider a domicile switch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Barclays May Want to Mull a Move to the U.S.', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'gl