, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de43ce36-d73a-5fe0-9cf5-646db9247053', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de43ce36-d73a-5fe0-9cf5-646db9247053'}, {'abstract': 'A Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum show features 26 paintings by this Venice-born artist who devoted his talents mostly to religious commissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/arts/design/carlo-crivelli-an-overlooked-renaissance-master-in-boston.html', 'snippet': 'A Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum show features 26 paintings by this Venice-born artist who devoted his talents mostly to religious commissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — If your admiration for Italian Renaissance painting is more culturally received than deeply felt, “Ornament and Illusion: Carlo Crivelli of Venice” at the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum is the show to see. It is the first exhibition in an American museum devoted to Crivelli, a great but neglected Early Renaissance master, and his fabulously fraught panel paintings, with their charged emotional moods, exquisitely detailed and richly appointed settings, gleaming trompe l’oeil jewels and tracts of gold gilt. There are only 26 paintings here, but they form a thrilling, seductive and edifying experience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06CRIVELLIJP6/06CRIVELLIJP6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06CRIVELLIJP6/06CRIVELLIJP6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 870}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06CRIVELLIJP6/06CRIVELLIJP6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 707, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'cr