nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e66d792-dd27-5ab4-ab50-3ff4077ac7d3', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e66d792-dd27-5ab4-ab50-3ff4077ac7d3'}, {'abstract': 'The title of Corin Hardy’s horror film refers not to a place, but to the vicious supernatural beings who inhabit a forest paradise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/movies/review-in-the-hallow-evil-lurks-in-the-irish-woods.html', 'snippet': 'The title of Corin Hardy’s horror film refers not to a place, but to the vicious supernatural beings who inhabit a forest paradise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of “The Hallow” refers not to a place, but to the vicious supernatural beings who inhabit a lush Irish forest. Into this initially peaceful paradise come Adam and Claire (Joseph Mawle and Bojana Novakovic) and their new baby, following the money offered to Adam, a tree expert, by a logging company wishing to survey its latest acquisition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06HALLOW/06HALLOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06HALLOW/06HALLOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06HALLOW/06HALLOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/arts/06HALLOW/06HALLOW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1091, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/0