aders of Burundi are using language that recalls the run-up to the genocide in Rwanda next door. The international community needs to act urgently to avert what may be a humanitarian catastrophe.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/mass-atrocities-looming-in-burundi/', 'snippet': 'Leaders of Burundi are using language that recalls the run-up to the genocide in Rwanda next door. The international community needs to act urgently to avert what may be a humanitarian catastrophe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s evidence that we may be on the brink of a humanitarian calamity in Burundi, a small central African nation that has seen waves of killings in its history. It has been unstable for months, but now the authorities are using language that recalls the run-up to the 1994 genocide in Rwanda, right next door. A few officials are blowing the whistle — including Samantha Power, who chronicled genocide in her brilliant book and yesterday as ambassador to the U.N. put out a statement on the crisis. But we need a much stronger reaction, immediately, from top U.N. officials including Ban Ki-moon and from African leaders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mass Atrocities Looming in Burundi?', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Power, Samantha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Crisis Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Burundi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-06T16:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'arti