e', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-06T17:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/849dce41-82d9-542b-b03d-a5a018b87319', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/849dce41-82d9-542b-b03d-a5a018b87319'}, {'abstract': 'Public libraries in New York have one hour to defend the city’s title as home to “the world’s fastest library-sorting system” and to break a 2-2 tie with a team from Seattle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/08/nyregion/new-york-public-library-seattle-book-sorting-system.html', 'snippet': 'Public libraries in New York have one hour to defend the city’s title as home to “the world’s fastest library-sorting system” and to break a 2-2 tie with a team from Seattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, Salvatore Magaddino will crank up the “Rocky” theme song and deliver a pep talk. His crew will then have one hour to defend the city’s title as home to “the world’s fastest library-sorting system” (at least according to the trophy) and to break its 2-2 tie with a squad from the King County Library System, which serves the area around Seattle. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/nyregion/08LIBRARYss-slide-2XBR/08LIBRARYss-slide-2XBR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/08/nyregion/08LIBRARYss-slide-2XBR/08LIBRARY