 book suspended from a high school’s English curriculum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friends and family congratulated me, book sales bounced a little and a 10-year-old title was suddenly under discussion by people who had never read it. I had been awarded literary recognition of a peculiar kind, one that brought me no euphoria. Along with six other books opposed by conservative parents in a wealthy school district near Dallas, my book “The Working Poor: Invisible in America,” a nonideological portrayal of lives near the bottom, was suspended from the English curriculum at Highland Park High School, where it had been used in advanced placement classes.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '49', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/books/review/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/08/books/review/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 665}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/books/review/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/books/review/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1504, 'width': 1358, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/08/books/review/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote/1108-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy'