ormation about the world by a means that’s now all but obsolete: encyclopedias. “There were so many inaccuracies, and there were so many things left out, because the process of creating encyclopedias is all about editing and curating, really,” Strachan says. He became fascinated by the figures forgotten by history — like Matthew Alexander Henson, the African-American explorer who led Robert Peary to the North Pole in 1909. (Strachan took inspiration from Henson when he represented the Bahamas at the Venice Biennale in 2013.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1143, 'width': 2038, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-strachan-1/06tmag-strachan-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '