, 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27624700-d652-5687-be24-84758726fa71'}, {'abstract': 'Funny about that private sector.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/06/obama-the-job-killer-redux/', 'snippet': 'Funny about that private sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philip Bump at the WaPo makes the same point I made a couple of days ago about the Obama job record: private sector job creation under the “job-killing” president has far outpaced anything that happened under Bush, while public-sector employment has declined. This doesn’t mean that Obama’s record is great. It does, however, mean that Republican claims that Obama’s left-wing policies, or something, are the big problem are very much at odds with the evidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama the Job Killer Redux', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-06T19:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab19ecd-2523-51ed-af20-1bd79799a3ba', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab19ecd-2523-51ed-af20-1bd79799a3ba'}, {'abstract': 'Over half of all passing yards this season have come from quarterbacks who are on the “wrong” side of 30.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/07/sports/football/older-quarterbacks-form-a-new-story-in-the-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Over half of all passing yards this season have come from quarterbacks who are on the “wrong” side of 30.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2011 and 2012, the landscape of the N.F.L. appeared to be changing, with the game turning into one dominated by the young quarterbacks who had just entered the league. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1443, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/07/sports/07LIONS1/07LIONS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Older Quarterbacks Form a New Story in the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Youth Must Be Served? Not This Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-0