e had been exhibiting under the pseudonym Tao Hongjing for the past decade, his assumed identity hasn’t helped him that profoundly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, a French artist living in Shanghai named Alexandre Ouairy received a wave of press attention for revealing that he had been exhibiting under the Chinese pseudonym Tao Hongjing for the past decade. According to news reports, he had assumed the pseudonym a decade ago, based on a suggestion by his gallerist, in order to cash in on the market there for Chinese contemporary art, a goldmine unavailable to an artist of French descent living in China. Now, on the eve of two solo shows — at Red Gate Gallery in Beijing and Shun Gallery in Shanghai — Mr. Ouairy was finally coming clean, acknowledging that the whole masquerade had been a “conceptual art project.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Artist Kills Off Chinese Alter Ego, but Some Knew of Ruse', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Counterfeit Merchandise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudson, Michael Derrick (Yi-Fen Chou)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alter Ego', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cohan, James, Gallery', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moganshan (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-08T20:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae72295a-f9c8-5005-b046-e8b05e05cf29', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae72295a-f9c8-5005-b046-e8b05e05cf29'}, {'abstract': '“I think there’s a growing body of intelligence and evidence that this was a bomb,” Representative Adam B. Schiff of California said on “This Week.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/09/us/politics/egypt-russia-plane-crash-bomb.html', 'snippet': '“I think there’s a growing body of intelligence and evidence that this was a bomb,” Representative Adam B. Schiff of California said on “This Week.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senior House members said Sunday that there was a mounting consensus among American intelligence officials that a bomb brought down the Russian charter jet that crashed last month in the Sinai Peninsula in Egypt, killing all 224 people aboard.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consensus Grows for Bomb as Cause of Russian Jet Crash, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intelligence Consensus Grows for Bomb as Cause of Russian Crash, U.S. Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '