ture of computer technology with advances in a branch of artificial intelligence known as machine learning. Machine-learning software is trained to handle vast amounts of data, and then learns as it goes, often on its own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Offers Free Software in Bid to Gain an Edge in Machine Learning', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Open-Source Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-09T14:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bfeffad-cc5e-55b9-8b5f-f118c2c8a13b', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bfeffad-cc5e-55b9-8b5f-f118c2c8a13b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Gen. Charles de Gaulle and his troops land in Gabon in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/09/1940-de-gaulle-strikes-in-africa/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Gen. Charles de Gaulle and his troops land in Gabon in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VICHY — The situation in French Africa became more tense today [Nov. 9] as reports reached here that ‘‘Free French’’ forces headed by Gen. Charles de Gaulle and Gen. de Larminat, after conquering Lambaréné, in the interior of Gabon, French Equatorial Africa, had effected a landing near Libreville, the most important seaport of Gabon. British light naval units supported the landing, it 