-draft/2015/11/10/donald-trump-sees-a-bump-in-attention-after-s-n-l-appearance/', 'snippet': 'According to a digital marketing firm, Donald J. Trump experienced a large increase in engagement across websites, social media and video platforms the day after being on the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few candidates for president have been as deft at garnering free media attention as Donald J. Trump. His appearance on “Saturday Night Live” is the latest example.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/09/us/politics/09firstdraftnl-snl/09firstdraftnl-snl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Sees a Bump in Attention After ‘S.N.L.’ Appearance', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saturday Night Live (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T11:40:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a261bd-60df-58a2-a00b-b4dd42edf61a', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a261bd-60df-58a2-a00b-b4dd42edf61a'}, {'abstract': 'When Mr. Glass and Christopher Hampton wrote “Appomattox,” it was mostly about the Civil War. Now the second act grapples with more recent history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/arts/music/revisiting-the-opera-appomattox-in-the-course-of-human-events.html', 'snippet': 'When Mr. Glass and Christopher Hampton wrote “Appomattox,” it was mostly about the Civil War. Now the second act grapples with more recent history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Each new chapter of American history has a way of casting what came before it in a different light. So when the composer Philip Glass and the playwright Christopher Hampton decided to revive “Appomattox,” the opera about the Civil War that they wrote a decade ago, they found that the changing civil rights landscape cried out for a rewrite.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 913}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1346, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11GLASS/11GLASS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Voting Rights Under Siege, Philip Glass Rewrites an Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Opera Isn’t Spared When History Outpaces Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Philip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hampton, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington National Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Appomattox (Opera)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17141d40-3c58-57fb-bbbe-890b6be27b0a', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17141d40-3c58-57fb-bbbe-890b6be27b0a'}, {'abstract': 'Ireland is a place where milk chocolate is a source of intense pride, with respected chocolatiers like Butlers, Skelligs, Lily O’Brien’s and Cadbury.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/travel/dublin-ireland-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'Ireland is a place where milk chocolate is a source of intense pride, with respected chocolatiers like Butlers, Skelligs, Lily O’Brien’s and Cadbury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone we met in Ireland told us that our trip last year couldn’t have been better timed. We were there in early summer. The countryside was at its ripest green, the characteristic clouds and rain were nowhere to be seen, and the crowds of summer tourists hadn’t yet arrived. But never mind the weather and the sights. We were there for the chocolate. Well, actually, I was there for the milk chocolate. My husband, Mahir, who proclaims his allegiance to dark, was my grumbling recruit.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/travel/15CHOCOLATE1/15CHOCOLATE1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Ireland, Milk Chocolate Reigns', 'kicker': 'Pursuits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Happy Cows, Delectable Milk Chocolate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40637f74-9518-5ad9-a23d-c4cc8251ae8e', 'word_count': 1649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40637f74-9518-5ad9-a23d-c4cc8251ae8e'}, {'abstract': 'In American life, work is confused with play and political inexperience in a presidential candidate is considered a virtue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/magazine/the-cult-of-the-amateur.html', 'snippet': 'In American life, work is confused with play and political inexperience in a presidential candidate is considered a virtue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in October, the retired brain surgeon Ben Carson took the stage at a Christian college in Colorado and pitched himself as president. ‘‘I love it when people come up to me and they say: ‘B-b-b-b-but-but you’ve never been elected to any public office! You can’t possibly know how to do anything!’ Well, let me tell you something. The ark was built by amateurs. The Titanic was built by professionals.’’ Carson touched his fingertips together and smiled softly to himself. The crowd went nuts. Outside, one Carson supporter pinpointed the surgeon’s appeal: ‘‘People are sick of politicians.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 555}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 1532, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cult of the ‘Amateur’', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unprofessionals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hess, Amanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c592ba2-0821-5d15-8202-fc40bcb78bdd', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c592ba2-0821-5d15-8202-fc40bcb78bdd'}, {'abstract': 'Is “biohacking” just a fad? Or can data-driven diets help us become an improved, happier species?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/magazine/you-only-better.html', 'snippet': 'Is “biohacking” just a fad? Or can data-driven diets help us become an improved, happier species?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Asprey does not like infomercials. He didn’t want our conversation to feel like one, he said, raising both hands in a gesture of innocence, like a magician showing there was nothing up his sleeve. But once he planted the suggestion, it wouldn’t go away. There was the register of his voice, oscillating between breathy and enthusiastic, and the complete absence of qualifiers to soften his bold claims. And then there were the wares clustered on the table in front of him. He had laid out cups of his signature product, Bulletproof Coffee, which is made with grass-fed butter and Brain Octane, a trademarked oil extracted from coconuts. Next to the cups lay Bulletproof-branded protein bars in chocolate and vanilla. ‘‘I am not plugging my stuff,’’ he said with a semi-embarrassed laugh. ‘‘I’m just talking about how things work.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/magazine/15asprey1/15asprey1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You, Only Better', 'kicker': 'The Future Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Supplemented Self', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asprey, Dave (1969- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bulletproof Digital Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T12:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b33b4fea-d732-5511-bb28-72c17c8eb972', 'word_count': 2634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b33b4fea-d732-5511-bb28-72c17c8eb972'}, {'abstract': 'The Belgian director Ivo van Hove, Michael C. Hall and Cristin Milioti talk, and avoid talking, about this new musical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/theater/a-visit-to-the-strange-secretive-world-of-david-bowies-lazarus.html', 'snippet': 'The Belgian director Ivo van Hove, Michael C. Hall and Cristin Milioti talk, and avoid talking, about this new musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent weekday morning, the Belgian director Ivo van Hove sat at a corner table in the bar of the Standard Hotel. A bound script of “Lazarus,” his latest stage project, nestled on the table beside his Americano.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15LAZARUS1/15LAZARUS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg'