r’s spring and summer season, announced on Tuesday, also includes Dorrance Dance, the Stephen Petronio Company, Pennsylvania Ballet and a Cuba Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/10/miami-city-ballet-returns-for-joyce-season/', 'snippet': 'The Joyce Theater’s spring and summer season, announced on Tuesday, also includes Dorrance Dance, the Stephen Petronio Company, Pennsylvania Ballet and a Cuba Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Miami City Ballet will give a season in New York for the first time since 2009. Alessandra Ferri and Herman Cornejo team up for a program of contemporary ballet pieces with the pianist Bruce Levingston. These are some of the highlights of the Joyce Theater’s offerings for its spring and summer season, announced on Tuesday, which also includes the tap ensemble Dorrance Dance, the Stephen Petronio Company, Pennsylvania Ballet and a Cuba Festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami City Ballet Returns for Joyce Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miami City Ballet Is Among Joyce Offerings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami City Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petronio, Stephen, Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T15:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Suclas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suclas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/558497c7-2c12-59cc-b282-05bf2f62d27b', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/558497c7-2c12-59cc-b282-05bf2f62d27b'}, {'abstract': 'A media giant enthralls a country’s TV-addicted viewers with empty soap operas and inane commentary on the news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/opinion/international/escaping-reality-with-brazils-globo-tv.html', 'snippet': 'A media giant enthralls a country’s TV-addicted viewers with empty soap operas and inane commentary on the news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — Last year, The Economist published an article about TV Globo, Brazil’s largest broadcast network. It reported that “91 million people, just under half the population, tune in to it each day: The sort of audience that, in the United States, is to be had only once a year, and only for the one network that has won the rights that year to broadcast American football’s Super Bowl championship game.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/opinion/barbara_new/barbara_new-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/05/opinion/barbara_new/barbara_new-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/opinion/barbara_new/barbara_new-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/opinion/barbara_new/barbara_new-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/opi