ic-roinestad-ceramics.html', 'snippet': 'With his whitewashed water jugs, the Los Angeles-based ceramist Eric Roinestad nods to the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stoneware vessels crafted by the Los Angeles-based ceramist Eric Roinestad evoke the persevering elegance of water jugs pulled from the volcanic soil of Pompeii. Yet while the objects nod to the past, with their whitewashed bisque palette and smooth matte surfaces, they are clearly of their time. After giving these substantial pieces, which range between 14 and 20 inches tall, a flat wash, Roinestad fires them and then sands them to let some of the clay show through the glaze, giving the vases the feel of having been hauled, gently, from the ashes of time.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0/15tmag-12qual_thing_urns-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/t-magazine/15tmag-12qual_thing_urn