 'Mr. Church’s new album, a surprise release last week, has shades of the Allman Brothers and scraped-up Southern rock, along with bluesy country gospel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Church is the sort of singer who sings earnestly about other singers, whose songs posit music as a magical sun shower to bathe in blissfully. In his songs, music is fuel for love, for anguish and, naturally, for other music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/arts/11CHURCH/11CHURCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On ‘Mr. Misunderstood,’ Eric Church Pays Homage to His Influences', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Homage to 1970s Vinyl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Church, Eric (1977- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-10T22:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0e216a9-3b8c-57cd-884e-b2f0dc473d2a', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0e216a9-3b8c-57cd-884e-b2f0dc473d2a'}, {'abstract': "Venice's Rose Café, reopened with chef Jason Neroni, features work from the artist Craig Stecyk.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/10/t-magazine/los-angeles-rose-cafe.html', 'snippet': "Venice's Rose Café, reopened with chef Jason Neroni, features work from the artist Craig Stecyk.", 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Rose Café — a longtime artist hangout in Venice Beach — closed its doors earlier this year, many of its fans feared a big change was underway. But for its next incarnation, open now, the new owner Bill Chait wanted to honor the space’s history and reflect the neighborhood’s culture. So he called on Jeffrey Deitch, the New York-based art dealer and curator who just a few years earlier had served as the director of the Museum of Contemporary Art Los Angeles. “We talked to Ed Ruscha, and Ed Moses, and reached out at some point to John Baldessari, and ended up talking to Craig,” Chait says, referring to the artist Craig Stecyk, who decorated the new space. “Craig knew a lot of these artists and obviously had been very involved in the Venice surf and skateboard scene, and so I think what he’s doing was very sort of trying to enhance the history of the Rose.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/t-magazine/10tmag-rose/10tmag-rose-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Beloved L.A. Surf Hangout Gets a Second Act', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, '