erg kept its secrets from me for the longest time and it was worth it. I say this because it’s very easy to put your nose up in the air and critique a puzzle that has … let’s just call it “odd” fill and cluing, shall we? … but it’s a downright hoot when you find out toward the end of the solve that the oddness was deliberate and to a purpose.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Rush Participants', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T03:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b7306e3-4ad1-5537-a10a-b2de350d0a42', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b7306e3-4ad1-5537-a10a-b2de350d0a42'}, {'abstract': 'A car traveling at high speed down Gerritsen Avenue on early Monday morning crashed into the water of Shell Bank Creek and sank. It remained there for more than a day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/nyregion/fatal-crash-in-a-brooklyn-creek-seen-only-on-camera.html', 'snippet': 'A car traveling at high speed down Gerritsen Avenue on early Monday morning crashed into the water of Shell Bank Creek and sank. It remained there for more than a day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The car traveling at high speed down Gerritsen Avenue in Brooklyn early Monday morning smashed through a wood construction fence, through a yard and into thin air. It crashed into the water of Shell Bank Creek, by the Belt Parkway, and sank.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'