b0c952-6290-5525-aba6-92b37a120929', 'word_count': 1409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b0c952-6290-5525-aba6-92b37a120929'}, {'abstract': 'Raluca Iosif moved to my neighborhood from Romania harboring dreams of a typical American life; instead, she was shot to death by her ex-boyfriend.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/a-typical-american-life-a-very-american-death/', 'snippet': 'Raluca Iosif moved to my neighborhood from Romania harboring dreams of a typical American life; instead, she was shot to death by her ex-boyfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, after working a long shift at the hospital, I walked to a restaurant in my neighborhood to have dinner with a male friend. The weather was unseasonably warm, so we ate outside. As we sat talking, our conversation was interrupted by something that sounded like a car backfiring. We paused, made a joke about the crowd at the nearby grocery store, and continued our meal. On my walk home, I didn’t notice the flashing lights at the end of my street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 494}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1572, 'width': 1910, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/10kristof_blog/10kristof_blog-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Typical American Life, a Very American Death', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durham (NC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carolynn Dude', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dude', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c6bbc6-8aa4-5405-b9c2-c3770cc4340b', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c6bbc6-8aa4-5405-b9c2-c3770cc4340b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Two governments-in-exile pledge co-operation against Germany in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/1940-czechs-and-poles-drop-feuds/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Two governments-in-exile pledge co-operation against Germany in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Laying the groundwork for a possible new order in central Europe, the Polish government and the provisional government of Czecho-Slovakia buried their past quarrels and jointly declared today [Nov. 11] their intention at the end of the war to enter into a closer economic and political association. The two governments-in-exile expressed the hope that they would be joined by other countries in the same part of Europe, and that free people throughout the world would help their cause by combating the German menace to the full extent of their power.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 12, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/blogs/12iht-oldnov12-poland/12iht-oldnov12-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/blogs/12iht-oldnov12-poland/12iht-oldnov12-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 740}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/blogs/12iht-oldnov12-poland/12iht-oldnov12-poland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/blogs/12iht-oldnov12-poland/12iht-oldnov12-poland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1660, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/blogs/12iht-oldnov12-poland/12iht-oldnov12-poland