e': 'Lawyers Say Ex-Allies of Christie Didn&#8217;t Get Evidence in Lane Closings Case ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baroni, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Bridget Anne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3dfbd60-5722-5b4e-ae45-af997887b0bf', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3dfbd60-5722-5b4e-ae45-af997887b0bf'}, {'abstract': 'With four playoff spots and five power conferences, at least one is going to be left out each year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/sports/ncaafootball/rankings-indicate-big-12-could-miss-college-football-playoff-again.html', 'snippet': 'With four playoff spots and five power conferences, at least one is going to be left out each year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the release of the season’s second college football playoff rankings, the pecking order at the top continues to clarify. If No. 1 Clemson wins the Atlantic Coast Conference, No. 2 Alabama the Southeastern Conference and No. 3 Ohio State the Big Ten, and if No. 4 Notre Dame wins the rest of its independent schedule, they are likely to be the four teams in the playoff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/sports/12BIG12web1/12BIG12web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rankings Indicate Big 12 Could Miss College Football Playoff Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Football Playoff National Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big 12 Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4852139e-8870-58fe-8695-8dd2e1738db9', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4852139e-8870-58fe-8695-8dd2e1738db9'}, {'abstract': 'This play at the Signature Theater centers on a group of mostly Jewish detainees in Vichy France who struggle with denial, choices and fundamental questions of identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/theater/incident-at-vichy-a-revival-of-arthur-millers-harrowing-wartime-drama.html', 'snippet': 'This play at the Signature Theater centers on a group of mostly Jewish detainees in Vichy France who struggle with denial, choices and fundamental questions of identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guilt is as inescapable as oxygen in the works of Arthur Miller, whose centennial is being celebrated this season with a formidable assortment of revivals, including Broadway productions of “A View From the Bridge” and “The Crucible.” But seldom did he dissect the nature of moral responsibility as rigorously as he did is in his lesser-known “Incident at Vichy” (1964), which opens Sunday, Nov. 15, in a Signature Theater production. Set in France during World War II, the play centers on a group of male detainees, most of them Jewish, who have been rounded up by German and French officers for interrogation. As the men try to figure out why they have been brought together, their conversation widens to embrace the most fundamental questions of identity, both ethnic and ethical. Michael Wilson (“The Orphans’ Home Cycle”) directs a cast that includes Richard Thomas and Jonathan Hadary. (Through Dec. 13, Pershing Square Signature Center, Manhattan; 212-244-7529, signaturetheater.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Incident at Vichy,’ a Revival of Arthur Miller’s Harrowing Wartime Drama', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; War Detainees, Questioning Why', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Arthur', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Michael (1964- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Incident at Vichy (Play)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ff66fe-500c-596d-8722-0dc921cd1edc', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ff66fe-500c-596d-8722-0dc921cd1edc'}, {'abstract': 'The retailer said it would have to mark down inventory to make way for new styles, which could put pressure on other chains to follow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/business/macys-lowers-its-guidance-on-sales-slump.html', 'snippet': 'The retailer said it would have to mark down inventory to make way for new styles, which could put pressure on other chains to follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A slump in tourist spending and warmer weather hit Macy’s business in the third quarter, driving sales lower and prompting the department store chain to lower its guidance for the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Macy’s Lowers Its Guidance on Sales Slump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundgren, Terry J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5241642-2fc3-5770-b8b6-73ee5e09abaa', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5241642-2fc3-5770-b8b6-73ee5e09abaa'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Butler, a creator of “Riverdance,” performs with the cellist Neil Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/arts/dance/jean-butler-brings-her-irish-dance-to-st-marks-church.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Butler, a creator of “Riverdance,” performs with the cellist Neil Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This tale of two Irish dance stars began with a six-minute performance at the Eurovision Song Contest in Dublin in 1994. They were the central couple backed up by a rousing ensemble: Jean Butler, a poised redhead, and Michael Flatley, a flamboyant blond in a shiny teal blouse who would later become the self-proclaimed Lord of the Dance. Together, they created and starred in “Riverdance,” the international megahit spawned by that TV appearance.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE10/15GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE10/15GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 499}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUI