ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4704bdc4-b39c-5a19-ab68-b9ef589f7372', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4704bdc4-b39c-5a19-ab68-b9ef589f7372'}, {'abstract': 'Many black students say that racial tensions were already woven into the fabric of everyday life at the University of Missouri, well before the recent cascade of events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/us/university-of-missouri-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Many black students say that racial tensions were already woven into the fabric of everyday life at the University of Missouri, well before the recent cascade of events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, Mo. — At first, Briana Gray just chalked up the comments and questions from her new roommate at the University of Missouri to innocent ignorance: How do you style your hair? What do you put in it? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/us/12missouri-jp1/12missouri-jp1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At University of Missouri, Black Students See a Campus Riven by Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Students See a University Riven by Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, Timothy M (1958- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberharassment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yik Yak Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Missouri', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3704b24-7374-5805-a857-7c7bec21526a', 'word_count': 1458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3704b24-7374-5805-a857-7c7bec21526a'}, {'abstract': 'Performing at the fashionable National Sawdust space, the orchestra will take up works by Kate Soper, Adam Schoenberg and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/arts/music/a-philharmonic-menu-of-young-composers.html', 'snippet': 'Performing at the fashionable National Sawdust space, the orchestra will take up works by Kate Soper, Adam Schoenberg and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American composers 40 and under are the focus of the New York Philharmonic’s latest Contact! new-music concert, on Monday, Nov. 16. The first Contact! to be hosted at the recently opened performance space National Sawdust, in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, the event features chamber works by Kate Soper, Adam Schoenberg, Nathan Heidelberger and Caroline Mallonée. Mario Davidovsky, born in Argentina but a resident of the United States for the past half-century, represents an older generation with his sextet “Flashbacks.” (7:30 p.m., 80 North Sixth Street, 646-779-8455, nationalsawdust.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE1/15GUIDE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Philharmonic Menu of Young Composers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical; From the Young, a Gaggle of Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Juilliard Ensemble', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Sawdust (Brooklyn, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Joel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4abea657-3e5b-5997-ba07-59d85346e923', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4abea657-3e5b-5997-ba07-59d85346e923'}, {'abstract': 'This scripted series, available for streaming on Nov. 19, traces the underbelly of the art world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/arts/television/the-art-of-more-on-crackle-reveals-the-ugly-side-of-pretty-things.html', 'snippet': 'This scripted series, available for streaming on Nov. 19, traces the underbelly of the art world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sex, blood, dirty money. “Smuggled, stolen and forged art is a $10 billion business,” intones a voice more Bensonhurst than Beekman Place. “The big collectors are more than willing to look the other way.” That’s where Graham Connor (Christian Cooke) — a former soldier in Iraq turned antiquities thief who has maneuvered his way into a top Manhattan auction house — comes in. “I get them to look my way,” he says in “The Art of More,” a new series streaming Thursday, Nov. 19, on Crackle.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE9/15GUIDE9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Art of More,’ on Crackle, Reveals the Ugly Side of Pretty Things', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; The Ugly Side of Pretty Things', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crackle.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quaid, Dennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Art of More (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T15:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd870d5-fc48-5a58-869f-9f95d375b543', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd870d5-fc48-5a58-869f-9f95d375b543'}, {'abstract': 'This restored 1972 film features Jeff Bridges and Stacy Keach as boxers at different points in their careers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/movies/in-fat-city-boxing-has-a-starring-role.html', 'snippet': 'This restored 1972 film features Jeff Bridges and Stacy Keach as boxers at different points in their careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another “Rocky” movie, this one called “Creed,” is just days away from release, but before the manipulative hero-making of that franchise, there was John Huston’s “Fat City,” a whole different kind of boxing movie. A new restoration of it begins a one-week run on Friday, Nov. 20, at Film Forum, and Leonard Gardner, who wrote both the screenplay and the novel it was based on, is scheduled to be on hand at the opening night showing at 7 to introduce this 1972 movie. The film was an early showcase for Stacy Keach and Jeff Bridges, Mr. Bridges playing a young boxer just starting out, Mr. Keach a somewhat older one who tries a comeback. In his review in The New York Times, Vincent Canby had high praise for the acting and for the script, “full of the kind of dialogue that movies usually can’t afford, that defines time, place, mood and character while seemingly going nowhere.” (At 209 West Houston Street, South Village; 212-727-8110, filmforum.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE3/15GUIDE3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE3/15GUIDE3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE3/15GUIDE3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE3/15GUIDE3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1550, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/arts/15GUIDE3/15GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi