n the protests at the University of Missouri.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/a-lesson-in-journalism-at-the-university-of-missouri.html', 'snippet': 'A veteran journalist decries an ugly moment in the protests at the University of Missouri.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lesson in Journalism at the University of Missouri', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lesson in Journalism at the University of Missouri', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Missouri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T16:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/61c52516-cb95-5a96-8782-89949fa628bd', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61c52516-cb95-5a96-8782-89949fa628bd'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Rhodesia declares independence from British rule in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/1965-rhodesia-claims-independence/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Rhodesia declares independence from British rule in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALISBURY — Rhodesia today [Nov. 11] declared its independence in the most momentous defiance of Britain since America threw off colonial rule nearly 200 years ago. The white-ruled colony in the heart of Africa immediately found itself outlawed in a largely hostile world. Britain imposed economic sanctions and called for a meeting of the United Nations Security Council to recruit world-wide support. In Pretoria, South African Premier Dr. Hendrik Verwoerd declared that his country would continue normal relations with Rhodesia, thus becoming the first government to recognize the ‘‘rebel’’ nation.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 12, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Rhodesia Claims Independence', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhodesia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T16:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c70bba3a-0ab9-535b-a0f9-d9101483665a', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c70bba3a-0ab9-535b-a0f9-d9101483665a'}, {'abstract': 'Delicious recipes for dinner tonight, for celebrating Diwali and for your Thanksgiving feast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/dining/weeknight-thanksgiving-diwali-recipes.html', 'snippet': 'Delicious recipes for dinner tonight, for celebrating Diwali and for your Thanksgiving feast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Sifton emails readers of Cooking five days a week to talk about food and suggest recipes. Beginning today, that email will also appear on nytimes.com. To receive the email, register here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/dining/recipes-chickenfricassee/recipes-chickenfricassee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 