eshow/83cffc6f-9ffd-5f80-842d-e9d5cc14bfd7'}, {'abstract': 'The singer’s all-grown-up album, “Purpose,” comes out on Friday, and he’ll kick off a North American tour in March in Seattle.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/justin-bieber-announces-58-date-purpose-tour/', 'snippet': 'The singer’s all-grown-up album, “Purpose,” comes out on Friday, and he’ll kick off a North American tour in March in Seattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Bieber’s all-grown-up album, “Purpose,” comes out on Friday, and all the final pieces are falling into place for his meticulously crafted, apology-filled comeback. After a steady stream of convincing singles, including “Where Are Ü Now,” made with Diplo and Skrillex, and “What Do You Mean?”, Mr. Bieber’s first No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100, he has announced a 58-date North American tour for 2016, promoted by AEG Live.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Bieber Announces 58-Date ‘Purpose’ Tour', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bieber Hitting the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T16:52:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/715aa52f-0851-5f97-ae7a-6af41f06c15f', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/715aa52f-0851-5f97-ae7a-6af41f06c15f'}, {'abstract': 'In Malibu, Paradise Cove has million-dollar views, hip residents and a location on one of the world’s most iconic beaches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/11/t-magazine/paradise-cove-malibu-million-dollar-trailer-parks.html', 'snippet': 'In Malibu, Paradise Cove has million-dollar views, hip residents and a location on one of the world’s most iconic beaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1979, David Carter, then a 30-year-old surfer, decided to move from Maui, where he’d spent a few years chasing waves and making surfboards, to Southern California. He and his wife were in search of that real estate oxymoron: an affordable place close to the ocean where they could raise their two sons. On the advice of friends, they went to visit a curious little subdivision called Paradise Cove, a private waterfront community of 265 trailers in Malibu.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '112', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/t-magazine/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/11/t-magazine/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/t-magazine/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/t-magazine/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 1833, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/t-magazine/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A/11tmag-paradise-t-slide-LK6A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su