paper, had ended his column after he questioned editorial independence in Spain in an article in The New York Times about the growing financial and government pressures on the Spanish news media that also discussed recent newsroom tensions at El País and other publications.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'El País Columnist Says Dismissal Tied to His Criticism of Media Independence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Europe; Spain: Newspaper Cancels a Column', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aguilar, Miguel Angel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Pais', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Press Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoy, Mariano', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-11T22:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da98f6a-6a72-5921-adbb-9a75035a3dfb', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da98f6a-6a72-5921-adbb-9a75035a3dfb'}, {'abstract': 'The images of wealth and luxury seen in TV commercials are aimed mostly at those who aspire to wealthy lifestyles, not those who actually enjoy them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytime