person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2185e8b-9cb0-5711-a437-2dc16e575210', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2185e8b-9cb0-5711-a437-2dc16e575210'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Burns, who plays Gloria Estefan’s mother in “On Your Feet,” is an entertainer at ease in the place where Broadway tradition merges with Latin American pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/arts/music/review-andrea-burns-at-feinsteins-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Burns, who plays Gloria Estefan’s mother in “On Your Feet,” is an entertainer at ease in the place where Broadway tradition merges with Latin American pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrea Burns, who plays Gloria Estefan’s mother in the musical “On Your Feet!,” knows who she is: a Latina fish out of water who grew up in Miami, obsessed with Broadway. Ebullient and playful, Ms. Burns, 44, brought a breath of tropical air to Feinstein’s/54 Below on Monday evening. She compared her parents’ 46-year relationship to a union between Jerry Seinfeld and Sofia Vergara. The person onstage had a little of both. “I happen to be part Jewish,” she added. “I have the guilt.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/12BURNS/12BURNS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/12BURNS/12BURNS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/12BURNS/12BURNS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}