alue': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlotte Hornets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T03:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21a2654-a5e9-5c40-9ca2-5dc212bb7623', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21a2654-a5e9-5c40-9ca2-5dc212bb7623'}, {'abstract': 'Research into veterans’ suicide received a lift on Tuesday with Senate passage of a measure requiring an independent research program on the effects of combat service on suicide rates and other mental health issues among troops and veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/us/senate-approves-research-into-combat-effects-on-mental-health.html', 'snippet': 'Research into veterans’ suicide received a lift on Tuesday with Senate passage of a measure requiring an independent research program on the effects of combat service on suicide rates and other mental health issues among troops and veterans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Research into veterans’ suicide received a lift on Tuesday with Senate passage of a measure requiring an independent research program on the effects of combat service on suicide rates and other mental health issues among troops and veterans. A report by The New York Times in September found that monitoring of suicide was not coordinated between the Department of Veterans Affairs and Department of Defense, and many veterans fell through the cracks because the effect of combat exposure was poorly tracked. \xa0 After more than decade of war, neither department has the data to show whether troops exposed to combat have a higher risk of suicide, and how that risk changes over time. Because of this, veterans say suicide prevention programs do not fit their needs. “We simply don’t know enough about the effects of combat on mental health issues among service members and veterans both during and after service,” said the amendment’s sponsor, Senator Michael Bennet of Colorado. The measure passed as part of the Military Construction and Veterans Affairs and Related Agencies Appropriations Act for fiscal year 2016. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Approves Research Into Combat Effects on Mental Health', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Approves Research Into Combat Effects on Mental Health', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philipps, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T04:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Philipps', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Philipps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4177002c-5003-58e1-8311-9267def30b3e', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4177002c-5003-58e1-8311-9267def30b3e'}, {'abstract': 'The victory in Bihar State by opposition parties calling themselves secular was partly a response to the right-wing Hindu characte