 'uri': 'nyt://article/7578b346-6d0a-5153-899b-203a3821c0a6'}, {'abstract': 'The author of a book about capital punishment writes that we will not “see abolition until the focus is on the system.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/death-penalty-and-the-law.html', 'snippet': 'The author of a book about capital punishment writes that we will not “see abolition until the focus is on the system.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Penalty and the Law', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death Penalty and the Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eighth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T08:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/db223497-85f5-5e30-a833-59460cdbca1b', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db223497-85f5-5e30-a833-59460cdbca1b'}, {'abstract': 'Here are some crib notes from the Republican debate to consider if your Thanksgiving dinner turns political.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/campaign-stops/wow-more-terrifying-than-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Here are some crib notes from the Republican debate to consider if your Thanksgiving dinner turns political.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps you didn’t watch the Republican presidential debate this week. That in no way excuses you from having an opinion about it. It’s the last one until December, and all you’ll have to work with if you want political conversation at Thanksgiving dinner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-jumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-superJumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbLarge-v9.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wow, More Terrifying Than Trump', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wow, More Terrifying Than Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Gail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiorina, Carleton S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/409bfb54-b6ba-5169-bd5c-10c8374f58bf', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409bfb54-b6ba-5169-bd5c-10c8374f58bf'}, {'abstract': 'At Yale and Missouri, both sides are talking past each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/who-is-entitled-to-be-heard.html', 'snippet': 'At Yale and Missouri, both sides are talking past each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME of the most potent threats to free speech these days come not from our government or corporations, but from our citizenry. Pitched battles being waged at Yale and the University of Missouri pit speech versus speech in a contest of who and what is entitled to be heard. These are only the latest examples: In recent years speakers have been disinvited, campus events disrupted and activists threatened for speaking their minds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12nosselWeb/12nosselWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': ' Who Is Entitled to Be Heard?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Is Entitled to Be Heard?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nossel, Suzanne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberharassment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Missouri', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne Nossel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/42196bcd-e455-58eb-9492-57ab4261cfd2', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42196bcd-e455-58eb-9492-57ab4261cfd2'}, {'abstract': 'Will the Supreme Court reverse an appeals court decision blocking a program to shield undocumented parents of American-born children from deportation?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/judicial-energy-and-the-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'Will the Supreme Court reverse an appeals court decision blocking a program to shield undocumented parents of American-born children from deportation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terry Eastland, a Reagan-era conservative activist who now edits The Weekly Standard, wrote a book back in 1992 that he called “Energy in the Executive: The Case for the Strong Presidency.” He took to task both President Ronald Reagan, for whom he had worked in the Justice Department, and the first President Bush for having failed to use all possible levers of presidential power to advance the conservative agenda.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judicial Energy and the Supreme Court', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ab91a1-a0c3-5f1f-a218-470d1fca5472', 'word_count': 1900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ab91a1-a0c3-5f1f-a218-470d1fca5472'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Trudeau’s diverse cabinet and his youthful energy may engender a renewed public spirit and a stronger sense of national identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/opinion/an-antidote-to-cynicism-in-canada.html', 'snippet': 'Justin Trudeau’s diverse cabinet and his youthful energy may engender a renewed public spirit and a stronger sense of national identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has become common to bemoan the sorry state of politics, what with all the big money, dirty tricks, image molding, partisan gridlock and general cynicism. Yet voters seem never to cease longing for a leader who can restore pride to high office and rekindle the national spirit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12thu3web/12thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12thu3web/12thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 455}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12thu3web/12thu3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12thu3web/12thu3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1554, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12thu3web/12thu3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201