even further.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/cola-a-new-start-up-introduces-ways-to-do-more-in-text-messages/', 'snippet': 'The company is trying to make it easier to accomplish tasks inside text messaging and to give other app makers the programming hooks that allow them to expand the abilities of text messages even further.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For better or worse, text messaging is the app people spend more time using than any other on their smartphones. A new start-up, Cola, believes it can make it a bit better. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/technology/12bits-cola/12bits-cola-jumbo.png', 'height': 838, 'width': 471, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/technology/12bits-cola/12bits-cola-superJumbo.png', 'height': 838, 'width': 471, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/technology/12bits-cola/12bits-cola-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/technology/12bits-cola/12bits-cola-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/technology/12bits-cola/12bits-cola-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cola, a New Start-up, Introduces Ways to Do More in Text Messages', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Start-Up Taps Textingu2019s Potential', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cola Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T16:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7471e9cf-7486-5602-8f08-4119084ec34b', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7471e9cf-7486-5602-8f08-4119084ec34b'}, {'abstract': 'A new software initiative will enable Android smartphones to be used for large-scale medical research projects. Apple did that for iPhones earlier this year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/bringing-iphone-style-medical-research-to-the-android-world/', 'snippet': 'A new software initiative will enable Android smartphones to be used for large-scale medical research projects. Apple did that for iPhones earlier this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Apple introduced its ResearchKit software in March, scientists at leading medical schools across the country have written apps to study asthma, Parkinson’s disease, autism, epilepsy, melanoma, breast cancer and other ailments. Medical experts are hopeful that using smartphones to gather health data from millions of people, with their consent, can open a window to new insights into diseases, treatments and lifestyle effects.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/11/technology/11bit