37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb39c60-b7fa-5a9c-8cf5-3194140c73da'}, {'abstract': 'Portrayed as an accidental disclosure, the Russian news media’s reporting of a nuclear-armed drone submarine appeared to be a deliberate tactic by the Kremlin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/world/europe/russia-says-leak-of-secret-nuclear-weapon-design-was-an-accident.html', 'snippet': 'Portrayed as an accidental disclosure, the Russian news media’s reporting of a nuclear-armed drone submarine appeared to be a deliberate tactic by the Kremlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Kremlin’s chief spokesman has confirmed that a report broadcast on Russian television this week revealed the design of a secret nuclear weapon delivery system: a drone submarine that could attack coastlines.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Says Leak of Secret Nuclear Weapon Design Was an Accident', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weapon Plan Shown on TV by Accident, Russia Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Submarines and Submersibles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T16:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/408d4fd2-14eb-5d51-911b-dd1e91af7225', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/408d4fd2-14eb-5d51-911b-dd1e91af7225'}, {'abstract': 'Immigration Equality and the Legal Aid Society discuss the plight of transgender people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/opinion/transgender-and-facing-prison-or-deportation.html', 'snippet': 'Immigration Equality and the Legal Aid Society discuss the plight of transgender people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transgender, and Facing Prison or Deportation', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transgender, and Facing Prison or Deportation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legal Aid Society', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T16:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4091768-343d-5251-af68-555d3b04abcf', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4091768-343d-5251-af68-555d3b04abcf'}, {'abstract': 'Watchdog groups are calling on the speaker to suspend privately-funded foreign junkets for lawmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/paul-ryan-stays-close-to-home-while-others-junketeer/', 'snippet': 'Watchdog groups are calling on the speaker to suspend privately-funded foreign junkets for lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative\xa0Paul Ryan, the new Speaker of the House, is by now a famous homebody who emphatically prefers family life to the back slapping, nice-to-see-you routine of lawmakers, even when they travel to exotic places abroad in the name of fact finding. In the last 15 years, Mr. Ryan, unlike many colleagues, has accepted only two privately financed trips overseas. The distinction might have been encouraging \xa0for Washington’s leading ethics watchdog groups last week in their call for the speaker to suspend the increasingly controversial foreign junkets paid for by private interests intent on swaying American lawmakers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/opinion/12clinesWEB/12clinesWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Ryan Stays Close to Home While Others Junketeer', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': No