 occasionally boundary-crossing delights set up shop around the neighborhood’s Little Manila.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bonito flakes wave like tattered flags, great shreds of them over a heap of ground pork still agitated from the frying pan, riled up by fermented black beans and fish sauce. Japanese Kewpie mayonnaise brings scattered sweet high notes and a deeper tang than its Western cousins. Under it all, French fries lie in wait, with charred tips.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tito King’s Kitchen and Bago Join a Filipino Feast in the East Village', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Growth Spurt in Little Manila', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bago (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Tito King's Kitchen (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T17:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cf723cd-8943-5800-883e-c0326ada1fd0', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cf723cd-8943-5800-883e-c0326ada1fd0'}, {'abstract': 'Video of the episode showed an employee saying there were fears they might “steal something.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/business/international/an-australian-apple-store-apologizes-to-black-students-it-eject