years.html', 'snippet': 'The prisoner, Murod Juraev, had been imprisoned since Sept. 18, 1994, and was sometimes called the world’s longest-serving political prisoner by rights groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — An Uzbek detainee sometimes called the world’s longest-serving political prisoner by rights groups was released on Thursday, having spent 21 years behind bars on various pretexts and trumped-up charges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uzbekistan Releases Political Prisoner After 21 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Asia; Uzbekistan: Political Prisoner Is Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uzbekistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juraev, Murod', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-12T21:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6153e303-fa7d-588d-bf6f-51d3a64645b7', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6153e303-fa7d-588d-bf6f-51d3a64645b7'}, {'abstract': 'From the owners of Reform Gallery comes the Landing, which opens Saturday with an exhibition of work by the artist J. B. Blunk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/12/t-magazine/landing-gallery-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'From the owners of Reform Gallery comes the Landing, which opens Saturday with an exhibition of work by the artist J. B. Blunk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Running a gallery can be “a little bit like an adoption agency,” says Gerard O’Brien. “You want to find the right home for these things because they have intrinsic value.” For more than a decade, his salon-style showroom, Reform Gallery, has been an insider resource for furniture by the post-G.I. Bill generation of West Coast artists, with pieces from the wire sculptor Ruth Asawa to the potter Doyle Lane. “California has always been this incredible place for makers,” O’Brien says, sitting on a loading dock in Paul Tuttle’s iconic leather “Z” chair, which was designed in Santa Barbara and produced in-state. “It was the land where you could come dream and make those dreams come true.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-wu/12tmag-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-wu/12tmag-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-wu/12tmag-wu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-wu/12tmag-wu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-wu/12tmag-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazi