'nyt://article/cfa57195-8f23-5680-b054-c433ec64389e'}, {'abstract': 'Diane Keaton and John Goodman play a long-married couple who have big news to deliver to the family once it gathers, in Jessie Nelson’s film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/movies/review-in-love-the-coopers-a-dysfunctional-family-sits-down-to-christmas-dinner.html', 'snippet': 'Diane Keaton and John Goodman play a long-married couple who have big news to deliver to the family once it gathers, in Jessie Nelson’s film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classic Christmas movies have a magic that can’t be manufactured, but “Love the Coopers” desperately tries to do just that. It employs a familiar conceit — dysfunctional family gathers for holiday meal — and enlists recognizable actors to deliver it, but the result plays like a collection of ideas and jokes borrowed from other movies. The film is occasionally amusing but rarely feels genuine.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/13LOVECOOPERS/13LOVECOOPERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/13LOVECOOPERS/13LOVECOOPERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/13LOVECOOPERS/13LOVECOOPERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/arts/13LOVECOOPERS/13LOVECOOPERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11