rist last month was fired Wednesday, the city announced on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The plainclothes rookie Palm Beach Gardens police officer who fatally shot a stranded motorist last month was fired Wednesday, the city announced Thursday. Corey Jones, 31, a housing inspector and musician, died Oct. 18 after his car broke down in the middle of the night off Interstate 95 in Palm Beach County. Palm Beach Gardens Police officer Nouman K. Raja was working a burglary detail when he approached Mr. Jones’s car in an unmarked van. Mr. Raja told the authorities that Mr. Jones confronted him with a gun, so the officer fired six times, striking Mr. Jones three times as he fled. The officer came under criticism for failing to show his badge, and because Mr. Jones had acquired his gun legally. Mr. Raja, who joined the police department in April, was still in his probationary period, making it easier for the city to terminate his employment. The Federal Bureau of Investigation and the Palm Beach Sheriff’s Office are investigating the shooting. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Police Officer Who Killed Stranded Motorist Is Fired ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Police Officer Who Killed Stranded Motorist Is Fired ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robles, Frances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Corey (d 2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raja, Nouman K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palm Beach Gardens (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T01:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frances Robles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frances', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e7fb3d-565f-5be5-8922-960ffa9f7e2f', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e7fb3d-565f-5be5-8922-960ffa9f7e2f'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Ashton B. Carter said on Thursday that he was removing his senior military assistant, Lt. Gen. Ronald F. Lewis, over allegations of misconduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/us/defense-secretary-dismisses-a-general-on-his-staff-in-a-misconduct-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Ashton B. Carter said on Thursday that he was removing his senior military assistant, Lt. Gen. Ronald F. Lewis, over allegations of misconduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defense Secretary Ashton B. Carter said on Thursday that he was removing his senior military assistant, Lt. Gen. Ronald F. Lewis, over allegations of misconduct. A statement announcing the dismissal offered no details, saying only that the matter would be investigated by the Pentagon’s inspector general, but a senior Defense Department official, speaking on the condition of anonymity because he was not authorized to publicly discuss the matter, said the misconduct was sexual. It is rare, if not unheard-of, for a defense secretary to so publicly fire a senior officer on his staff. General Lewis, a former Army chief of public affairs who deployed to Afghanistan and Iraq, has been at Mr. Carter’s side for years, serving him in a number of posts. In the statement, Mr. Carter said: “I expect the highest possible standards of conduct from the men and women in this department, particularly from those serving in the most senior positions. There is no exception.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defense Secretary Dismisses a General on His Staff in a Misconduct Inquiry', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defense Secretary Dismisses a General on His Staff in a Misconduct Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Ronald F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T01:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ec44b99-3ae0-580c-b841-d38186fe707a', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ec44b99-3ae0-580c-b841-d38186fe707a'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/nyregion/things-to-do-in-the-hudson-valley-nov-13-to-22-2015.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to westweek@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/nyregion/15HIWE2/15HIWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, '