'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a34b5cb-6140-57f4-b325-87e805f4ed8d', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a34b5cb-6140-57f4-b325-87e805f4ed8d'}, {'abstract': 'Reviewers have recommended several books for their tone in covering the state of Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/books/review/from-all-sides.html', 'snippet': 'Reviewers have recommended several books for their tone in covering the state of Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israeli prime minister Yitzhak Rabin was assassinated 20 years ago this month. This week, Ilene Prusher reviews “Killing a King,” Dan Ephron’s account of that murder and its continuing impact in the Middle East. Over the past couple of decades, reviewers in these pages have recommended several books for their tone in covering the state of Israel.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/books/review/1115-BKS-OpenBook/1115-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 267, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/books/review/1115-BKS-OpenBook/1115-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 267}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/books/review/1115-BKS-OpenBook/1115-BKS-OpenBook-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/books/review/1115-BKS-OpenBook/1115-BKS-OpenBook-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20