', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harvey Stein has documented Midtown Manhattan — during parades, the evening rush — since the 1970s. In his new book, “Briefly Seen: New York Street Life,” he captures Midtown as theater: older women in Easter hats; a painted body on a Gay Pride float. But just as often, he does the opposite, unmasking faces, capturing the expressions of people simply trying to make their way through the crowd.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harvey Stein Captures Street Theater of Midtown Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Street Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correal, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Briefly Seen: New York Street Life (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T17:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35611de0-93c0-572e-988e-f497ea04a1e5', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35611de0-93c0-572e-988e-f497ea04a1e5'}, {'abstract': 'It was once considered unbecoming, or annoying itself, to moan publicly about trifling personal ordeals. Now we tolerate, even encourage, the microcomplaint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/fashion/the-microcomplaint-nothing