(England)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T20:32:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Photographs by DEREK RIDGERS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Photographs', 'middlename': 'Derek', 'lastname': 'RIDGERS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8e421bbc-1493-59af-9fec-0990aa272b8b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8e421bbc-1493-59af-9fec-0990aa272b8b'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Derek Ridgers shares images from his new book, “The Others.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/t-magazine/derek-ridgers-1980s-london-photography.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Derek Ridgers shares images from his new book, “The Others.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The English photographer Derek Ridgers’s latest book doesn’t really pick up where his earlier efforts, “When We Were Young” and “78-87,” left off. Instead, “The Others,” out today, gathers what these much-lauded publications left out: 100 previously unpublished snapshots (pared down from 650) that had been living in Ridgers’s hard-drive folder under the same name. He captured the kids at London hot spots like the Mud Club, Le Beat Route, Heaven, Cha-Cha and Cafe De Paris “because I was there and had the access,” he explains, “but very quickly, I realized I was documenting people who were not going to be looking like that for that long — in some cases, they were only ever going to look like that for one night.” Here, he shares with T a selection of couples caught mid-liplock. “As I felt like I needed to ask permission of my subjects, I would sometimes have to stop them kissing, ask, and then let them get on with it,” he remembers. “No one ever said no and no one ever stopped kissing. They just went right back to it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Hot and Heavy in the 1980s', 'kicker': 'Photography', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T20:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d91891ed-a4e3-5eb3-a87c-6bf5280b0bad', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d91891ed-a4e3-5eb3-a87c-6bf5280b0bad'}, {'abstract': 'Francisco A. Alsina, 23, was arrested on Thursday after the authorities tracked him to a home about 180 miles from New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/nyregion/francisco-alsina-suspect-in-midtown-manhattan-shooting-arrested-in-rhode-island.html', 'snippet': 'Francisco A. Alsina, 23, was arrested on Thursday after the authorities tracked him to a home about 180 miles from New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man the police believe fatally shot one person and injured two others at a Midtown Manhattan subway station this week has been arrested, the authorities said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/nyregion/14ARRESTweb/14ARRESTweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/