k': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anthony, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smillie, Justin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-13T21:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef01a0b1-b9d0-5afd-8166-b885fd08c61b', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef01a0b1-b9d0-5afd-8166-b885fd08c61b'}, {'abstract': 'Unclebrother, created by the art dealer Gavin Brown and the artist Rirkrit Tiravanija, is an outgrowth of Tiravanija’s 1992 performance piece “Untitled (Free).”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/t-magazine/rirkrit-tiravanija-gavin-brown-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'Unclebrother, created by the art dealer Gavin Brown and the artist Rirkrit Tiravanija, is an outgrowth of Tiravanija’s 1992 performance piece “Untitled (Free).”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1992, the art dealer Gavin Brown helped the artist Rirkrit Tiravanija transform 303 Gallery, then on Greene Street, into an operational kitchen for a part performance, part installation piece titled “Untitled (Free).” The seminal solo show, which found the artist serving up gratis curry and rice out of the converted gallery, represented a critical development in Tiravanija’s practice. It also marked the beginning of his friendship with Brown, who at the time worked as an assistant at the gallery. Now in the collection of MoMA, “Untitled (Free)” — considered a masterwork of relational aesthetics — was the first of many interactive projects realized by the twosome. Their latest scheme: a gallery-meets-kitchen in Hancock, N.Y. Lovingly referred to as Unclebrother (the name is an inside joke), the hybrid restaurant revives the generous spirit of Tiravanija and Brown’s inaugural partnership, but adds in a full-time, brick-and-mortar locale. “It’s the first time he’s had a commercial kitchen, so it’s a departure in that sense,” Brown says. “It’s a natural progression, in a way. It’s about entering into the same place but from a different direction.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/t-magazine/12tmag-rirkrit/12tmag-rirkrit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'hei