ogress,” at City Center, includes works by Akram Khan, Mats Ek, Russell Maliphant and William Forsythe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sylvie Guillem is a trailblazer, notably in the decisive way she has commandeered her ballet career, but she’s only human. After dancing for nearly four decades, she’s calling it quits. In the charming program note for her farewell performance, “Life in Progress,” Ms. Guillem writes that she gave a friend the final say, or a “license to kill,” if she remained onstage longer than she should. “Frankly,” she writes, “I’d like to spare him this task.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/14/arts/14GUILLEM/14GUILLEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/art