lan concert hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/world/europe/paris-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'People attending a show by an American group, Eagles of Death Metal, described sudden terror when gunmen burst into the Bataclan concert hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The band had been playing to the crowd at one of this city’s most popular music venues, the Bataclan, for about an hour. The 150-year-old music hall was sold out for the show by the American group Eagles of Death Metal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Scene of Carnage’ Inside Sold-Out Paris Concert Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside Sold-Out Concert Hall, a Siege and ‘a Scene of Carnage’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgins, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bataclan (Paris, France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eagles of Death Metal (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T02:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter and Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb20e6ae-5ac0-5b28-94d3-07705c859daa', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb20e6ae-5ac0-5b28-94d3-07705c859daa'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Yufe became a celebrity after he and his brother were subjects in a study of nature versus nurture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/us/jack-yufe-a-jew-whose-twin-was-a-nazi-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Yufe became a celebrity after he and his brother were subjects in a study of nature versus nurture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day in 1954, Jack Yufe, a store owner from Southern California, stepped off a train in Essen, West Germany, and began searching the crowd at the station. He was looking for someone he had not seen since he was a baby, 21 years earlier.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/us/14yufe-obit/14yufe-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/14/us/14yufe-obit/14yufe-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/us/14yufe-obit/14yufe-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/us/14yufe-obit/14yufe-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1483, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/us/14yufe-obit/14yufe-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSt