ttps://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/sports/baseball/red-sox-acquire-star-closer-craig-kimbrel.html', 'snippet': 'The San Diego Padres traded Kimbrel, who had 39 saves in 43 chances after joining the team last season from Atlanta, for four of Boston’s minor league prospects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The revival of the San Diego Padres was a flop last season, and the Boston Red Sox are the latest team to poach one of their talented players. In their first major move under baseball operations president Dave Dombrowski, the Red Sox traded four prospects Friday for Craig Kimbrel, a four-time All-Star who is only 27 years old.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Sox Acquire Star Closer Craig Kimbrel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Red Sox Acquire Kimbrel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimbrel, Craig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T03:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a36b47a-a252-536a-86c7-61508015b58b', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a36b47a-a252-536a-86c7-61508015b58b'}, {'abstract': 'Law enforcement must embrace innovations like body cameras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/opinion/more-scrutiny-better-policing.html', 'snippet': 'Law enforcement must embrace innovations like body cameras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE director of the F.B.I., James B. Comey, recently offered an explanation for a reported uptick of violent crime in some of our cities. “A chill wind,” he said, “has blown through American law enforcement over the last year” — a reference to the so-called Ferguson effect that increased scrutiny on police conduct has led to reduced law enforcement in some urban neighborhoods.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 1918, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/opinion/14adams/14adams-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Scrutiny, Better Policing', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Scrutiny, Better Policing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Eric L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T03:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric L. Adams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Adams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d686fd6-ad26-54c9-abde-e2d04cd03d40', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d686fd6-ad26-54c9-abde-e2d04cd03d40'}, {'abstract': 'If the Knick’s doctors have their way, there won’t be any diseases left for us to worry about a century later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/13/arts/television/the-knick-season-2-episode-5-rapid-progress.html', 'snippet': 'If the Knick’s doctors have their way, there won’t be any diseases left for us to worry about a century later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the small staff of the Knickerbocker Hospital has its way, there won’t be any diseases left for us to worry about a century later. In Friday night’s episode of “The Knick” alone, John Thackery was zeroing in on the causes of addiction while the former (and presumably future) Knick surgeon Bertie Chickering was about to use radiation to treat his mother’s cancer (based on a tip from Algernon Edwards). In the same spirit of constant innovation, Thackery rigged a telephone for use as a metal detector to find shrapnel in the body of a subway worker — a nurse held the receiver to her ear and when she heard static, Thackery pulled out a nail from deep within the man’s body.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/12/arts/13THEKNICK/13THEKNICK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Knick’ Season 2, Episode 5: Rapid Progress', 'kicker': 'The Knick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Knick (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T04:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b993154-2506-5b00-95df-d88c93b9ec9b', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b993154-2506-5b00-95df-d88c93b9ec9b'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks let their lead slip from their grasp, as the Cavaliers came back once again to win, 90-84, on Friday at Madison Square Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/14/sports/basketball/cleveland-cavaliers-beat-new-york-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks let their lead slip from their grasp, as the Cavaliers came back once again to win, 90-84, on Friday at Madison Square Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seconds remained in the first half when Carmelo Anthony started sizing up Tristan Thompson along the right sideline, near the Knicks’ bench. Hunched over, Anthony braided low, hypnotizing dribbles between his legs, back and forth across his body. Then, midstep, he rose and slung a parabolic 3-pointer that splashed through the net.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/14/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'article