s from more than a dozen countries agreed Saturday to press forward on an ambitious timetable to engineer a political transition and cease-fire in Syria, but remained deeply divided on major issues after a round of talks that gained intensity following the terrorist attacks in Paris.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attacks in Paris Add Urgency to Talks on Ending Syria War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talks on Syrian Truce and Transition Take On New Urgency After Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T14:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d7e6065-a28f-578a-84ee-35b9e7430c4a', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d7e6065-a28f-578a-84ee-35b9e7430c4a'}, {'abstract': 'This week: A co-op board steers clear of a squabble