sing questions about American leadership in the world and national security, will most likely bolster Hillary Rodham Clinton’s strengths in Saturday’s debate, according to a focus group of undecided Iowa Democrats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1503, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/us/15FD-clinton/15FD-clinton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Attacks Could Bolster Hillary Clinton’s Support, Focus Group Indicates', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T21:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cec6b14b-6f01-5f3e-a8b3-da459f33998c', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cec6b14b-6f01-5f3e-a8b3-da459f33998c'}, {'abstract': 'We don’t like flip-floppers, but we should consider voting for them anyway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/the-virtue-of-contradicting-ourselves.html', 'snippet': 'We don’t like flip-floppers, but we should consider voting for them anyway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you’re a politician, there may be something worse than being called a liar, a cheater, a jerk or a wimp. In America, you don’t want to be known as a flip-flopper. Jeb Bush and Hillary Rodham Clinton have both been criticized for changing their positions from yes to no on invading Iraq. A decade earlier, flip-flopping was one of the biggest knocks against John Kerry. In a JibJab video gone viral, an animated George W. Bush mocked Mr. Kerry: “You have more waffles than a house of pancakes.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15grant/15grant-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge',