': 'Many educators believe that children need to learn emotional intelligence to reach their full academic potential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR years, there has been a steady stream of headlines about the soaring mental health needs of college students and their struggles with anxiety and lack of resilience.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 757}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1955, 'width': 1550, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15scelfo/15scelfo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Peace in Elementary School', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teaching Peace in Elementary School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scelfo, Julie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T22:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Scelfo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scelfo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5846f5c-8731-5b73-876e-8c9e8e0e3f9f', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5846f5c-8731-5b73-876e-8c9e8e0e3f9f'}, {'abstract': 'We conveniently forget that a third of the immigrants who came here a century ago didn’t like what they found — and went back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/america-the-not-so-promised-land.html', 'snippet': 'We conveniently forget that a third of the immigrants who came here a century ago didn’t like what they found — and went back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the great myths Americans have about their country is that everyone wants to come here. Advocates and enemies of immigration share this assumption, which dates at least as far back as the turn of the 20th century. As reports of “American fever” circulated in Eastern Europe, one Polish economist, Leopold Caro, claimed that entire villages were becoming ghost towns. “Many houses stood empty, and in many others only old women and small children remained behind. In some villages the entire young generation left home.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1239, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/opinion/sunday/15zafra/15zafra-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America, the Not So Promised Land', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America, the Not So Promised Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n