 families continued to struggle to find information about missing loved ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the world joined Parisians in mourning for the people killed in Friday’s terrorist attacks, the identities of the victims, who included a young lawyer, a music critic and an American college student, slowly began to emerge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out for Fun on a Friday Night, Victims Are Mostly Young', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out for Pleasure on a Friday Night, Victims Are Mostly Young', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bataclan (Paris, France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-14T23:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37dc871c-e876-5608-8139-a5b2500d2126', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37dc871c-e876-5608-8139-a5b2500d2126'}, {'abstract': 'The Islamic State emerged from a group of militants in Iraq to take over large portions of Iraq and Syria, and now threatens other countries in Europe and elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/11/14/world/middleeast/isis-expansion.html', 'snippet': 'The Islamic State emerged from a group of militants in Iraq to take over large portions of Iraq and Syria, and now threatens other countries in Europe and els