: '2015-11-15T22:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14890896-788a-5264-a822-fbbcdf273a99', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14890896-788a-5264-a822-fbbcdf273a99'}, {'abstract': 'The Washington National Opera presents a revised version of Philip Glass and Christopher Hampton’s opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/arts/music/review-appomattox-at-the-kennedy-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Washington National Opera presents a revised version of Philip Glass and Christopher Hampton’s opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Eight years ago, the composer Philip Glass unveiled a new opera, “Appomattox,” at the San Francisco Opera. Set to a libretto by Christopher Hampton, it centered on the gentlemanly negotiations between Generals Grant and Lee at a rural Virginia home that effectively brought the Civil War to a close in 1865. But the appearance of a chorus of civil rights protesters signaled that the opera’s true subject was race relations in America.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16APPOMATTOX/16APPOMATTOX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16APPOMATTOX/16APPOMATTOX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16APPOMATTOX/16APPOMATTOX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16APPOMATTOX/16APPO