'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7930d3ee-b9c5-52ef-b9a2-6d4d3c107a3d', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7930d3ee-b9c5-52ef-b9a2-6d4d3c107a3d'}, {'abstract': 'Cooder-White-Skaggs conveyed a sense of rare, joyous occasion during Rosanne Cash’s Perspectives series at Carnegie Hall on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/arts/music/review-ry-cooder-ricky-skaggs-and-the-whites-a-roots-music-celebration.html', 'snippet': 'Cooder-White-Skaggs conveyed a sense of rare, joyous occasion during Rosanne Cash’s Perspectives series at Carnegie Hall on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ry Cooder began the first encore at Zankel Hall on Saturday night with a shadowy, droning solo on electric bouzouki, in no hurry to settle on a tempo. After a few moments, Ricky Skaggs joined him on mandolin, and their searching interplay coalesced into a slow processional. Only as Mr. Cooder started singing, with a light husk in his baritone, did the shape of a song become clear.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16COODER/16COODER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ry Cooder, Ricky Skaggs and the Whites, a Roots-Music Celebration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harmonizing on a Path to Heaven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whites, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Rosanne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Sharon (1953- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skaggs, Ricky', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooder, Ry', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-15T22:46:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/25917790-3a38-5956-b1fd-3e9c3166c2c3', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25917790-3a38-5956-b1fd-3e9c3166c2c3'}, {'abstract': 'The performance shifts between dancers onstage and doll-house-scale arrangements in live video, in Shuji Onodera’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/arts/dance/review-spectator-at-the-japan-society.html', 'snippet': 'The performance shifts between dancers onstage and doll-house-scale arrangements in live video, in Shuji Onodera’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a friend heard I was going to a production at the Japan Society, he guessed I would see one of the traditional Japanese genres — Noh, Kabuki, Bunraku — and said at once, “Interesting.” My visit on Friday, however, was for Shuji Onodera’s “Spectator,” which, certainly interesting, was new in Tokyo in 2013.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SPECTATOR/16SPECTATOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':