 Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Attacks Shift Europe’s Migrant Focus to Security', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attacks Change Europe&#8217;s Migrant Focus From Compassion to Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyman, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-15T22:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Lyman and Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84dbfee3-f2c3-563f-8703-239a4531df0c', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84dbfee3-f2c3-563f-8703-239a4531df0c'}, {'abstract': 'Subtitled “The American Odyssey of George Herbert Walker Bush,” Jon Meacham’s biography reveals the ambition that lay behind a president often seen as ineffectual.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/books/review-in-destiny-and-power-george-hw-bush-epitomizes-a-vanishing-gop.html', 'snippet': 'Subtitled “The American Odyssey of George Herbert Walker Bush,” Jon Meacham’s biography reveals the ambition that lay behind a president often seen as ineffectual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For better or for worse, George Herbert Walker Bush has been enshrined in collective memory as a series of caricatures, all of them evoking ineffectuality. He was the effete Yale man and the blue blood wimp; the awkward statesman who, when called upon to speak, diced the English language into an uneven and mysterious julienne. It didn’t help that his face was generally a fresco of befuddlement. The last thing one would have expected of him was tigerish ambition. Unlike so many politicians who thrust their way into the Oval Office — TheodoreRoosevelt, Lyndon B. Johnson, Bill Clinton — there seemed nothing overtly appetitive about him.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16BOOKMEACHAM/16BOOKMEACHAM-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16BOOKMEACHAM/16BOOKMEACHAM-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16BOOKMEACHAM/16BOOKMEACHAM-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 689, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16BOOKMEACHAM/16BOOKMEACHAM-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1377, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16BOOKMEACHAM/16BOOKMEACHAM-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS