on of Doom,” the set was not quite finished, the music was temporary and the sound designer was not even due to begin work until after the curtain call. “I have no idea what’s going to happen tonight,” said the director, Joel Schumacher, before the show. But he was not sweating it. “I don’t mind anything, except the Republican debates,” he said breezily.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1105, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16SCHUMACHER/16SCHUMACHER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joel Schumacher, Directing ‘Neighborhood 3,’ Gets an Education', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Curtain Calls Instead of ‘Cut!’  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumacher, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flea Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Neighborhood 3: Requisition of Doom (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-15T23:22:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd0ba060-cb1c-5d7a-9ca1-0172a16133ad', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd0ba060-cb1c-5d7a-9ca1-0172a16133ad'}, {'abstract': 'As many as 50 of its more than 200 employees will be affected.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/15/lay-offs-coming-at-weinstein-company-mostly-in-film-division/', 'snippet': 'As many as 50 of its more than 200 employees will be affected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Weinstein Company on Sunday confirmed that it will lay off as many as 50 of its more than 200 employees, mostly in its film division. The layoffs were first reported by Variety. Weinstein has been shifting much of its focus toward television, but continues to work on future films, including “The Six Billion Dollar Man,” planned for 2017, and has high-profile films set for release this year. Those include a pair of likely awards contenders, Todd Haynes’s “Carol” and Quentin Tarantino’s “The Hateful Eight.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u