id Hare looks back on his experience and his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/books/review/the-blue-touch-paper-a-memoir-by-david-hare.html', 'snippet': 'The playwright David Hare looks back on his experience and his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Hare was a child, nothing excited him more than getting lost. From the outset of his adult professional life, however, he knew very well where he was — and how to get from there to where he wanted to be. With his singular combination of talent and tenacity, he always found himself at the center of wherever theatrical daring and excellence were recruited. In 1974, with “Knuckle,” Hare broke through to the West End, among the first of his generation of Oxbridge Young Turks to do so. As a resident dramatist, he ascended the food chain of British theater: from disputatious bouts at the Royal Court to the Nottingham Playhouse during Richard Eyre’s brilliant regime and all the way up to the National Theater, where by 1984 he was an associate director, co-creating the influential Joint Stock Company along the way.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/22BROWN/22BROWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 502, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/22BROWN/22BROWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 502}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/22BROWN/22BROWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/22BROWN/22BROWN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1713, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'sup