html', 'snippet': 'While it’s not an opportunity to “dress like Cookie,” the clothing line may signal a new stage in pop culture/designer partnerships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days the high fashion designer/fast fashion collaboration has become so ubiquitous (Balmain x H&M, Lilly Pulitzer for Target, the North Face for J. Crew) that it is starting to feel like a calculated formula guaranteed to milk the most from a marketing budget. So it’s nice to see one based on an entirely different premise: fandom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/fashion/16OTR-COMBO/16OTR-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Collaborations 3.0: Lee Daniels’s ‘Empire’ and Hood by Air Make a Fashion Statement', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hood by Air', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Empire (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliver, Shayne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T13:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c92e934-c1c4-5ecb-bc97-06c5df9148e0', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c92e934-c1c4-5ecb-bc97-06c5df9148e0'}, {'abstract': 'Jesse Tyler Ferguson will star in the one man show “Fully Committed,” a comedy about foodie culture.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/jesse-tyler-ferguson-returns-to-broadway-in-fully-committed/', 'snippet': 'Jesse Tyler Ferguson will star in the one man show “Fully Committed,” a comedy about foodie culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jesse Tyler Ferguson plays one half of one of television’s most memorable couples on “Modern Family.” But when he returns to Broadway in April, he’ll be all alone. Mr. Ferguson will star in the one-man show “Fully Committed,” a comedy about foodie culture by Becky Mode, starting April 2 at the Lyceum Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 1964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/16artsbeat-ferguson/16artsbeat-ferguson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jesse Tyler Ferguson Returns to Broadway in ‘Fully Committed’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jesse Tyler Ferguson Returning to Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T14:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e9d10d-3ade-5b01-8053-1b5a1803b3fa', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e9d10d-3ade-5b01-8053-1b5a1803b3fa'}, {'abstract': 'Jazzmeia Horn, a 23-year-old singer originally from Dallas, is the winner of the 2015 Thelonious Monk Institute International Jazz Competition.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/jazzmeia-horn-wins-thelonious-monk-institute-international-jazz-competition/', 'snippet': 'Jazzmeia Horn, a 23-year-old singer originally from Dallas, is the winner of the 2015 Thelonious Monk Institute International Jazz Competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The winner of the 2015 Thelonious Monk Institute International Jazz Competition is Jazzmeia Horn. Originally from Dallas, Ms. Horn, 23, is a singer with a smart, steadfast connection to the jazz-vocal tradition, as defined by predecessors like Betty Carter and Sarah Vaughan. Since moving to New York in 2009 to attend the New School for Jazz and Contemporary Music, she has been a regular presence on the club scene, often with her band, the Artistry of Jazz Horn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazzmeia Horn Wins Thelonious Monk Institute International Jazz Competition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jazzmeia Horn Wins Monk Jazz Competition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monk, Thelonious', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T14:11:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31838796-17f9-5731-aba2-ce194b4646d7', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31838796-17f9-5731-aba2-ce194b4646d7'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The revolution in Honduras ends violently in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/1890-honduras-slays-her-traitors/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The revolution in Honduras ends violently in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — The Honduras revolution has ended, and General Sanchez and all his principal leaders have been shot. Yesterday morning General Bogran opened fire on the barrack to which the insurgents had retreated. Sanchez and his comrades, knowing that death awaited them, fought desperately; but it was a hopeless struggle from the start. Bogran’s soldiers charged and soon all the rebels remaining alive were prisoners. Without the formality of a court-martial Sanchez and the leading officers were taken to one of the principal squares in the city, blindfolded and stood in line in the presence of hundreds of citizens. The word was given to the firing party, and a crash of musketry rang the death-knell of the revolution.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, November 17, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Honduras Slays Her Traitors', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T14:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f80047-d6e7-5a3c-a3c4-04b943bd28ce', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f80047-d6e7-5a3c-a3c4-04b943bd28ce'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans will almost certainly press their criticism on foreign policy, but forecasts of “game changers” tend to be wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/upshot/why-the-paris-attacks-probably-wont-change-the-elections-outcome.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans will almost certainly press their criticism on foreign policy, but forecasts of “game changers” tend to be wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until last week, the threat from terrorism had received little attention from candidates or voters during the 2016 campaign. In one poll, just 3 percent of Americans rated it the most important problem facing the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/upshot/17UP-France-Effect/17UP-France-Effect-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/17/upshot/17UP-France-Effect/17UP-France-Effect-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/upshot/17UP-France-Effect/17UP-France-Effect-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/upshot/17UP-France-Effect/17UP-France-Effect-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's