te', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Kimba M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T16:54:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be6c6e68-94b3-58ca-b0d9-a26aa37fdb74', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be6c6e68-94b3-58ca-b0d9-a26aa37fdb74'}, {'abstract': 'The American ambassador in Bogotá discusses Colombia-U.S. relations, cocaine production and the accuracy of the show “Narcos.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/taking-stock-of-the-10-billion-washington-spent-on-colombias-war/', 'snippet': 'The American ambassador in Bogotá discusses Colombia-U.S. relations, cocaine production and the accuracy of the show “Narcos.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States has spent more than $10 billion dollars beefing up Colombia’s security forces, supporting development and backing reform of the judicial system in an effort known as Plan Colombia. After playing an instrumental role in giving the Colombian government the upper hand in its decades-long war against the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia, or FARC, a Marxist guerrilla group, Washington has turned its attention to peacemaking. I talked with\xa0Kevin Whitaker, the American ambassador in Bogotá, by email about this evolution and Washington’s decision to sit down with leaders who are under indictment in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/13/opinion/13whitakerWeb/13whitakerWeb-articleLarge.jpg'