', 'snippet': 'Jane Mayer’s “Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right,” explores how conservatives like the Kochs are seeking to reshape American politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a 2010 profile of the billionaire industrialist brothers Charles and David Koch, the New Yorker writer Jane Mayer described how, from 2005 to 2008, the brothers had vastly outspent ExxonMobil in financing organizations that fight legislation aimed at curbing climate change. Their company, the conglomerate Koch Industries, was also listed as one of the top 10 air polluters in the country, she wrote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Book Looks at the Koch Brothers’ Role in Politics', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T17:47:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e531d6cb-7307-5ed1-a148-d67913d202cc', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e531d6cb-7307-5ed1-a148-d67913d202cc'}, {'abstract': 'A legal review found no evidence to support allegations that Mr. Gillinson, its executive and artistic director, had tried to undermine the oversight of Mr. Perelman, its former chairman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/arts/music/carnegie-hall-stands-behind-clive-gillinson-after-review-of-ronald-perelmans-complaints.html', 'snippet': 'A legal review found no evidence to support allegations that Mr. Gillinson, its executive and artistic director, had tried to undermine the oversight of Mr. Perelman, its former chairman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carnegie Hall — whose former chairman, Ronald O. Perelman, stepped down last month after clashing with its executive and artistic director, Clive Gillinson — announced on Monday that a legal review that it commissioned had found no evidence to support allegations that Mr. Gillinson had tried to undermine Mr. Perelman’s oversight responsibilities.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/arts/17CARNEGIE/17CARNEGIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie Hall Stands Behind Clive Gillinson After Review of Ronald Perel