ith the staff address the anxieties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanksgiving came early this year to the Modern. Not the holiday of turkey and cranberry sauce, but the custom of family members lovingly and contentiously coming together to talk (and talk) about the things that unite and divide them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/dining/18TIPPING1SUB/18TIPPING1SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danny Meyer’s Team Faces a No-Tipping World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Tipping, the Danny Meyer Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tips and Tipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union Square Hospitality Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Danny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waiters and Waitresses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Modern, The (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T20:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c98384-de8d-55b0-87d7-d4d99d49577e', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c98384-de8d-55b0-87d7-d4d99d49577e'}, {'abstract': 'How a half-decade of grim surprises have made Europe’s future look considerably more difficult than it once did.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/europes-darkened-future/', 'snippet': 'How a half-decade of grim surprises have made Europe’s future look considerably more difficult than it once did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before we talk about fighting ISIS, let’s talk about the state of Europe. The first time I wrote about the European encounter with Islam in this newspaper was in December of 2009, around the publication of Christopher Caldwell’s “Reflections on the Revolution in Europe,”\xa0and the Swiss referendum banning minarets.\xa0In that column I wrote critically about the half-thought-out, deliberately un-democratic\xa0immigration policies the continent’s leaders had pursued since the 1960s, but I also expressed skepticism\xa0about the scenarios of dhimmitude and “Eurabia” floated, long before Michel Houellebecq’s “Submission,” by certain voices on the American and European right. From where I stood, neither\xa0demographic projections nor existing patterns of assimilation nor the continent’s ideological currents seemed to support a vision of a Europe\xa0where “Shariah has as much clout as liberalism” by, say, 2045.\xa0Instead, I argued that the European future would probably be like the present, only more so:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Darkened Future', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T20:10:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742d8709-c172-5f4e-9366-dccfc8b5b036', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742d8709-c172-5f4e-9366-dccfc8b5b036'}, {'abstract': 'The Ludwig and Rosy Fischer collection was one of the most important collections of Expressionist art assembled in pre-Nazi Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/museum-of-modern-art-returns-german-artwork-to-heirs-of-jewish-collector/', 'snippet': 'The Ludwig and Rosy Fischer collection was one of the most important collections of Expressionist art assembled in pre-Nazi Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A German Expressionist painting by Ernst Ludwig Kirchner at the Museum of Modern Art will be returned to the heirs of the German art collector Max Fischer, the museum announced Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Modern Art R