tworks, films and people who have influenced his work, from Buñuel to Travis Bickle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/t-magazine/16tmag-gaspar-portrait/16tmag-gaspar-portrait-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seven Things That Inspire Gaspar Noé', 'kicker': 'Under the Influence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noe, Gaspar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kubrick, Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T20:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ad7e063-cf2c-571d-afae-a929545a5c98', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ad7e063-cf2c-571d-afae-a929545a5c98'}, {'abstract': 'Le Labo’s popular scent began as an antidote to mass-market scents — and ironically ended up, to the discerning nose, all over the place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/t-magazine/perfume-santal-33-ds-durga-aesop.html', 'snippet': 'Le Labo’s popular scent began as an antidote to mass-market scents — and ironically ended up, to the discerning nose, all over the place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2011, when the fragrance industry saw a rise in celebrity scents and relied on the allure of glossy marketing, the independent perfumery Le Labo proposed an antidote to the obsession with hype: quietly releasing its fifth fragrance in five years — completely unaware of the impact its new unisex perfume would have on a certain set (and generation) of style-conscious women. Like an under-the-radar It bag prized for its unidentifiable features and nondescript branding, Santal 33 quickly became a sort of cult secret, whispered through wafts of sandalwood and cedar, only detected by those in the know.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'ca