 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa6e65a-cf7e-5945-bf76-752d7af0e84f'}, {'abstract': 'We explore the lives of newly wired consumers and the consequences, good and bad, that arise from our increasing reliance on trackers, monitors, guides and a vast array of other devices to better our health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/16/special-section-wired-well/', 'snippet': 'We explore the lives of newly wired consumers and the consequences, good and bad, that arise from our increasing reliance on trackers, monitors, guides and a vast array of other devices to better our health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once personal health technology meant little more than bathroom scales, thermometers and electric toothbrushes. Now, these devices and apps are everywhere: on our wrists, in our phones, the bedroom, the kitchen, even on our children and pets. In this special issue of Science Times, we explore the lives of newly wired consumers and the consequences, good and bad, that arise from our increasing reliance on trackers, monitors, guides and a vast array of other devices to better our health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/science/wellcover/wellcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/17/science/wellcover/wellcover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 759}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/science/wellcover/wellcover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/science/wellcover/wellcover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', '