ork Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Paris Attacks, ‘La Marseillaise’ Echoes Around the World in Solidarity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Since Paris Attacks, Solidarity Can Be Heard in a Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Anthems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-16T23:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e2d1e52-0d09-5432-accf-7cb1e1dd3d13', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e2d1e52-0d09-5432-accf-7cb1e1dd3d13'}, {'abstract': 'The troubled television star will appear on the “Today” show Tuesday after reports that he is HIV-positive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/arts/television/2015-11-17-arts-charlie-sheen-plans-revealing-personal-announcementhtml.html', 'snippet': 'The troubled television star will appear on the “Today” show Tuesday after reports that he is HIV-positive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — As tabloid reports proliferated on Monday that the troubled television star Charlie Sheen plans to soon reveal his HIV-positive status, one of Hollywood’s top crisis public relations experts confirmed that representatives for Mr. Sheen had in recent months sought his assistance in disclosing the diagnosis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ran