he local news media said Mr. Clark was handcuffed at the time of the shooting, but the authorities said he was not. The Minneapolis police, who have not publicly named Mr. Clark, said the man was a suspect in an assault who disrupted paramedics treating his victim and then fought with officers. The shooting prompted protests. Federal officials did not immediately issue a public response to Ms. Hodges’s request.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minnesota: Federal Inquiry Sought Into Shooting ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Minnesota: Federal Inquiry Sought Into Shooting ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T01:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/446fa990-337b-592e-814c-074313843184', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/446fa990-337b-592e-814c-074313843184'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Tennis Association contends that Eugenie Bouchard did not follow protocol and refused offers of medical attention after she fell and injured her head.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/sports/tennis