n the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/word-of-the-day-quiz-floe/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 13 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'floe • \\ˈflo\\ • noun ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day + Quiz | floe', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T05:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0a9f3c9-df39-586c-8294-af6be77f22bd', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0a9f3c9-df39-586c-8294-af6be77f22bd'}, {'abstract': 'The tornado, one of four that touched down in the area, caused a chemical leak but no immediate reports of injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/us/texas-tornado-rips-through-halliburton-plant.html', 'snippet': 'The tornado, one of four that touched down in the area, caused a chemical leak but no immediate reports of injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tornado ripped through a Halliburton plant an hour northeast of Amarillo on Monday, causing a chemical leak that emergency crews were working to contain, the authorities said. The Gray County Sheriff’s Office said two deputies who were exposed to the chemical, which was unspecified, refused medical treatment. There were no reports of injuries. Lt. Zach Kidd said no one was inside the building, in Pampa, Tex., when the tornado struck, and several vehicles parked outside were unoccupied. Radioactive material housed at the site was not affected, he said. The tornado was one of four that touched down in the county as a severe weather system moved across the region, according to the sheriff’s office. Two homes and several businesses sustained damage ranging from minor to severe, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Tornado Rips Through Halliburton Plant ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Tornado Rips Through Halliburton Plant ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Halliburton Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMARILLO (TEX)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T05:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/62989f7b-4f2d-5667-b195-6acb5e6ae7a3', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62989f7b-4f2d-5667-b195-6acb5e6ae7a3'}, {'abstract': 'A deputy foreign minister said that President Bashar al-Assad should remain in power and be included in elections as part of any diplomatic negotiation aimed at ending the civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/world/middleeast/syria-iran-reaffirms-a-role-for-assad.html', 'snippet': 'A deputy foreign minister said that President Bashar al-Assad should remain in power and be included in elections as part of any diplomatic negotiation aimed at ending the civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Iranian official said Monday that President Bashar al-Assad of Syria should remain in power and be included in elections as part of any diplomatic negotiation aimed at ending the civil war. The statement, by Hossein Amir Abdollahian, a deputy foreign minister, was not a new position for Iran, Mr. Assad’s regional ally. But it reinforced the deep divide that remains over Mr. Assad’s future in the international talks on Syria, even as pressure has intensified for a solution. Diplomats participating in the talks in Vienna over the weekend represented more than a dozen countries, including the United States, which has said Mr. Assad cannot be part of any final settlement. Mr. Abdollahian was quoted by Iran’s Fars News Agency as saying Iran ensured that a statement issued at the meeting’s conclusion excluded any language that would limit Mr. Assad’s role in a postwar government.  ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Iran Reaffirms a Role for Assad', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Syria: Iran Reaffirms a Role for Assad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T05:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/232b3d9a-70fd-54a7-a192-886427f8ec31', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/232b3d9a-70fd-54a7-a192-886427f8ec31'}, {'abstract': 'Dick Wolf adds more Windy City bluster to the Tuesday night lineup, “Frontline” visits 