g nowhere in the wake of the assaults last Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Syrian refugees are not the only possible new arrivals that Republicans want to keep out of the United States. The terror detainees remaining at the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, are also not welcome, and Republicans say the Paris attacks will keep them that way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo/16firstdraftnl-guantanamo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Attacks Complicate Obama’s Guantánamo Plans', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed, Khalid Shaikh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T11:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f709489-c52f-52dd-8e6c-7014668480e1', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f709489-c52f-52dd-8e6c-7014668480e1'}, {'abstract': 'Governments have spent trillions of dollars helping the poor, without finding a foreign-aid strategy that works. What if they learned to invest more nimbly?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/magazine/saving-the-world-startup-style.html', 'snippet': 'Governments have spent trillions of dollars helping the poor, without finding a foreign-aid strategy that works. What if they learned to invest more nimbly?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, not long after the earthquake hit Haiti, I was about an hour north of Port-au-Prince, standing under a mango tree. Its owner, a woman named Jelen, was telling me that she had two daughters but could afford to send only one to school. She knew this meant the other would be poor, like her, for the rest of her life. She said she was choosing the younger one because she was smarter. She then pointed at her mango tree. It was huge, bigger than a family home, and grew hundreds of mangoes each year. She knew that those mangoes could sell for several dollars each in America, but there was no easy way to get them there. So she sold most of them down the road at a local market for pennies. If she could find a good way to get those mangoes down the highway to the capital and then on a ship to America, she was confident that she could make enough money to send both her girls to school.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 508}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1735, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22onmoney1/22mag-22onmoney-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving the World, Startup-Style', 'kicker': 'On Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving the World, Startup-Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T12:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/613f75dc-603f-5ff2-ab3e-371757ca87f5', 'word_count': 1295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/613f75dc-603f-5ff2-ab3e-371757ca87f5'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times/CBS News poll released before the attacks in Paris found that Americans were unhappy with the president’s approach to the radical Islamist group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/17/poll-watch-public-unease-with-isis-strategy-even-before-paris/', 'snippet': 'A New York Times/CBS News poll released before the attacks in Paris found that Americans were unhappy with the president’s approach to the radical Islamist group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The terrorist attacks in Paris last week have renewed criticism of President Obama for his strategy in fighting the Islamic State. But a New York Times/CBS News poll released just before the attacks found that Americans were already unhappy with the president’s approach to the radical Islamist group, also known as ISIS or ISIL.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/us/16firstdraft-obama2/16firstdraft-obama2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Watch: U.S. Public Uneasy With ISIS Strategy Even Before Paris Attacks', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T12:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Thee-Brenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thee-Brenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/927f9a71-3411-5274-bcb5-dfd404316d25', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/927f9a71-3411-5274-bcb5-dfd404316d25'}, {'abstract': 'The word implies that a sacrifice is being made for transgender students. But what is being given up?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/magazine/making-bathrooms-more-accommodating.html', 'snippet': 'The word implies that a sacrifice is being made for transgender students. But what is being given up?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The clearest visual markers of sex difference many of us see in the course of the day are the signs on public bathroom entrances: MEN on one door, WOMEN on the other. Restrooms are public conveniences, freely available in most places and in principle open to all, but the terms for entering them have been fixed. They’re fundamentally fraught spaces, where we undress and obey the dictates of our bodies and therefore feel vulnerable. If people think you’ve confused male and female and walked through the wrong door, you risk discomfort, or even real trouble. This can lead to the spectacle of women standing in line for what feels like forever while the men’s room is empty. Now transgender people, most prominently, are asking society to rethink all of this, from signs to design to who gets to enter where.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 1417, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/magazine/22firstwords/22mag-22firstwords-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '