ese financial firm has sought to build its team in the region, which still generates the largest amount of investment banking fees worldwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Japanese financial firm Nomura has hired yet more deal makers for the Americas, as it continues to push for a share of the investment banking pie in the region.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nomura Hires Six Bankers in Effort to Expand in Americas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nomura Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T14:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/002f9f20-a9fe-5411-aa41-849b3447fe5b', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/002f9f20-a9fe-5411-aa41-849b3447fe5b'}, {'abstract': 'When terrorists strike, television networks respond, sometimes sensitively and other times perhaps unnecessarily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/18/arts/television/after-bloodshed-tv-can-be-cathartic-or-insensitive.html', 'snippet': 'When terrorists strike, television networks respond, sometimes sensitively and other times perhaps unnecessarily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Must the show go on? After Friday’s terrorist massacre in Paris, as often happens after violent tragedies, a few shows didn’t. CBS announced that it would replace scheduled Monday episodes of “Supergirl” (whose plot concerned a series of urban bombings), and “NCIS: Los Angeles” (involving a possible terrorist recruitment scheme). TNT, likewise, pulled a Monday episode of the F.B.I. drama “Legends,” which reportedly depicted a terrorist shooting in Paris.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/16/arts/18CRISISTV/15HOMELAND2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When TV Turns Itself Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Terror Strikes Close to Your TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violence (Media and Entertainment)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '24 (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mr Robot (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'NCIS: Los Angeles (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Homeland (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T14:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d10a0865-57e5-5a15-833a-499524df4b47', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d10a0865-57e5-5a15-833a-499524df4b47'}, {'abstract': 'The security of Microsoft’s products was once a sore spot for the company. Now its executives are giving other people tips on how to keep out the bad guys.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/daily-report-microsoft-finds-its-security-groove/', 'snippet': 'The security of Microsoft’s products was once a sore spot for the company. Now its executives are giving other people tips on how to keep out the bad guys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a given in the technology industry for many years that if you wanted to find a company that excelled at computer security, you ought not look for it in Redmond, Wash., the home of Microsoft.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u