y has raised questions among some public health groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama’s nominee to lead the Food and Drug Administration, Dr. Robert M. Califf, coasted through a confirmation hearing on Tuesday, with most members of a Senate committee — including some who have been skeptical about his ties to the pharmaceutical industry — seeming set to support his candidacy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/science/18Califf/18Califf-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Califf, F.D.A. Nominee, Queried on Industry Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Panel Questions Nominee to Lead F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Califf, Robert M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T14:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe38cd8-a5ef-5c80-bfb9-341298d908b8', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe38cd8-a5ef-5c80-bfb9-341298d908b8'}, {'abstract': 'Caeden, a wearable tech start-up, hopes to attract consumers with a smart bracelet that looks more like a piece of jewelry than a gadget.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/caeden-a-wearable-tech-start-up-introduces-a-smart-bracelet/', 'snippet': 'Caeden, a wearable tech start-up, hopes to attract consumers with a smart bracelet that looks more like a piece of jewelry than a gadget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just about every major tech company, like Apple and Microsoft, has some sort of wearable computer. Caeden, a wearable\xa0tech start-up, thinks that with most of these smartwatches and fitness accessories, an important first step was skipped: They don’t look like something you\xa0would\xa0want to wear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/technology/17bits-caeden/17bits-caeden-articleL