his crime show, which keeps finding ways to stay on the air, has a new home, A&E.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/arts/television/unforgettable-apparently-forever.html', 'snippet': 'This crime show, which keeps finding ways to stay on the air, has a new home, A&E.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Plenty of decent television shows don’t survive for one reason or another — bad time slot, wrong network, lackluster promotional effort. It’s too bad more of them don’t have the resilience of “Unforgettable,” a good crime show that keeps finding ways to stay on the air. For its fourth season, which begins Friday, Nov. 27, that has meant moving to a new network, A&E.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Unforgettable,’ Apparently Forever', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; It’s Still ‘Unforgettable’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARTS & ENTERTAINMENT NETWORK', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Unforgettable (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montgomery, Poppy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-17T20:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ebd86f-1328-5f81-bc5e-757398a71a2b', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ebd86f-1328-5f81-bc5e-757398a71a2b'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. John Kasich conceded that while Ohio did not have the authority to reject Syrian refugees, he urged President Obama to stop accepting them until the United States can ensure that terrorists are not coming in, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/17/john-kasich-urges-obama-to-not-accept-syrian-refugees-for-now/', 'snippet': 'Gov. John Kasich conceded that while Ohio did not have the authority to reject Syrian refugees, he urged President Obama to stop accepting them until the United States can ensure that terrorists are not coming in, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. John Kasich of Ohio conceded Tuesday that he did not have the power to block the flow of Syrian refugees into his state, but he still urged President Obama to stop accepting them until the United States can ensure that terrorists are not making their way into the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-kasich/17firstdraft-kasich-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'th