7-4634ba01b06c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4c0ac866-d8ba-599a-9b97-4634ba01b06c'}, {'abstract': 'The term lets politicians distance themselves from the fact that they’re calling for sending young Americans into battle.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/17/lets-kick-boots-on-the-ground-to-the-curb/', 'snippet': 'The term lets politicians distance themselves from the fact that they’re calling for sending young Americans into battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the aftermath of the Paris terror attacks, “boots on the ground,” Vietnam-era shorthand for ground troops, has become the rhetorical equivalent of camouflage fashion. Tossing out the term gives politicians a battle-toughened air, while distancing them from the fact that they’re calling for the United States to send young Americans into battle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/opinion/17williamsonWEB2/17williamsonWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/17/opinion/17williamsonWEB2/17williamsonWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/opinion/17williamsonWEB2/17williamsonWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/opinion/17williamsonWEB2/17williamsonWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/17/opinion/17williamsonWEB2/17williamsonWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width