/0ec5b230-6212-51f1-8c54-623c528b2489', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec5b230-6212-51f1-8c54-623c528b2489'}, {'abstract': 'The Estefans’ musical “On Your Feet!” and the HBO documentary “The Latin Explosion” overlook what else was going on with Latinos in pop at the time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/18/arts/music/estefan-and-la-bamba-cover-only-part-of-americas-latin-culture-in-the-1980s.html', 'snippet': 'The Estefans’ musical “On Your Feet!” and the HBO documentary “The Latin Explosion” overlook what else was going on with Latinos in pop at the time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My favorite sound to come out of the Miami Sound Machine goes something like this: Hhhwoo! That happens toward the end of the chorus for “Rhythm Is Gonna Get You,” which kicked off the second side of the band’s album “Let It Loose.” It was 1987, and most of us had to flip something over — an LP, a cassette — to hear it. The song stalked summer radio back then.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/arts/18ESTEFAN/18ESTEFAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/arts/18ESTEFAN/18ESTEFAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/arts/18ESTEFAN/18ESTEFAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/arts/18ESTEFAN/18ESTEFAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '