 they would start an inquiry into whether the shooting of an unarmed black man by the police violated civil rights laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/18/us/minnesota-us-will-investigate-police-shooting-of-unarmed-man.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Department officials said they would start an inquiry into whether the shooting of an unarmed black man by the police violated civil rights laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justice Department officials said Tuesday that they would start an inquiry into whether the shooting of an unarmed black man by the Minneapolis police violated civil rights laws. The man, Jamar Clark, 24, who was shot Sunday, died Monday night. The police said that Mr. Clark was an assault suspect and that he had been shot after interfering with paramedics trying to treat his victim and fighting with two officers. The police have disputed witness accounts that said Mr. Clark was handcuffed when he was shot. Though no police camera captured the confrontation, other cameras showed parts of it, said Superintendent Drew Evans of the Minnesota Bureau of Criminal Apprehension, which is investigating the case. Superintendent Evans said releasing that footage now could compromise the investigation. Protesters, including dozens who were arrested Monday night for blocking highway traffic, have demanded the release of video evidence and the names of the officers. The protesters and Mayor Betsy Hodges requested the Justice Department investigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minnesota: U.S. Will Investigate Police Shooting of Unarmed Man ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Minnesota: U.S. Will Investigate Police Shooting of Unarmed Man ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Jamar (d 2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-18T03:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f5aefd5-1b67-5f90-b13a-3c799b440819', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f5aefd5-1b67-5f90-b13a-3c799b440819'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mommsen, a scholar of the Holocaust, was commissioned by Volkswagen to explore the company’s complicity in the crimes of the Third Reich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/18/world/europe/hans-mommsen-studied-volkswagens-role-in-nazi-era-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mommsen, a scholar of the Holocaust, was commissioned by Volkswagen to explore the company’s complicity in the crimes of the Third Reich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hans Mommsen, considered the leading German historian of the Third Reich, whose work encompassed the origins of the Holocaust as well as a widely publicized report documenting Volkswagen’s wartime use of slave labor, died in Tutzing, near Munich, on Nov. 5, his 85th birthday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/world/18mommsen-obit/18mommsen-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/world/18mommsen-obit/18mommsen-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non