, 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b43b0171-8d3e-5c9b-abd1-590f203d4d51', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b43b0171-8d3e-5c9b-abd1-590f203d4d51'}, {'abstract': 'How the “most shocking moment in football history” looks, 30 years later.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/18/rewatching-the-theismann-injury/', 'snippet': 'How the “most shocking moment in football history” looks, 30 years later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has perhaps never been a more memorable play in football — or even all of American sports — than the one that ended the career of the Washington Redskins quarterback Joe Theismann, 30 years ago today. Since that play, N.F.L. quarterbacks have attempted nearly half a million passes, and we have never again seen (or heard) such skeletal trauma.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-privatelives/opinionator-pog-privatelives-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-privatelives/opinionator-pog-privatelives-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-privatelives/opinionator-pog-privatelives-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-privatelives/opinionator-pog-privatelives-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 