k': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-18T15:31:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da6af4fe-4c5d-5b9c-902c-ea9ac0de4a56', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da6af4fe-4c5d-5b9c-902c-ea9ac0de4a56'}, {'abstract': 'The scoring and offensive rebounding of Porzingis, the 7-foot-3 rookie, have so far outweighed negatives like his shooting percentage and penchant for fouling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/sports/basketball/despite-problems-with-fouls-kristaps-porzingis-has-knicks-fans-believing.html', 'snippet': 'The scoring and offensive rebounding of Porzingis, the 7-foot-3 rookie, have so far outweighed negatives like his shooting percentage and penchant for fouling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After suffering through a miserable 17-win season by the Knicks last season, Madison Square Garden fans are getting excited again, thanks in large part to the play of Kristaps Porzingis. When a 7-foot-3 Latvian rookie comes to town, you might expect him to be a novelty act, beloved by fans but unproductive. But it is starting to look as if Porzingis is actually going to be good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/sports/19PORZINGISweb/19PORZINGISweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristaps Porzingis Looks Good, Despite Problems With Fouls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porzingis, Kristaps (1995- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-18T15:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72ac6a17-c593-58fd-aae0-d49ae39554f0', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72ac6a17-c593-58fd-aae0-d49ae39554f0'}, {'abstract': 'Former Gov. Jeb Bush of Florida has been struggling to gain traction in polls in early nominating states, but the speech at the Citadel, aides hope, will allow him to cast himself as a serious candidate for serious times, with a proven record of fixing things.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/18/jeb-bush-cites-paris-attacks-in-calling-for-stronger-military/', 'snippet': 'Former Gov. Jeb Bush of Florida has been struggling to gain traction in polls in early nominating states, but the speech at the Citadel, aides hope, will allow him to cast himself as a serious candidate for serious times, with a proven record of f...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — Jeb Bush plans to use a long-scheduled speech at the Citadel on Wednesday to outline his vision for overhauling the nation’s military and responding to the growing threat of the Islamic State.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/us/18firstdraft-jeb/18firstdraft-jeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/us/18firstdraft-jeb/18firstdraft-jeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/us/18firstdraft-jeb/18firstdraft-jeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/us/18firstdraft-jeb/18firstdraft-jeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 