_paragraph': 'Canadian Pacific Railway will probably have to come up with more than $28.4 billion to keep a Norfolk Southern deal on track. The company justifies its unsolicited bid for its American rival by promoting cost savings worth more than $12 billion. But Canadian Pacific shareholders would keep $5 billion of that amount for themselves. Given antitrust risks, the merger price could use stoking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hurdles for Canadian Pacific-Norfolk Southern Deal', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Pacific Railway Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Norfolk Southern Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T00:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/530e5a06-3b5a-5580-b673-c38138dce7a8', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/530e5a06-3b5a-5580-b673-c38138dce7a8'}, {'abstract': 'United Automobile Workers leaders said voting on a new labor agreement is tight at Ford, leaving the deciding votes in the hands of workers at three big plants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/business/results-of-uaw-vote-show-ford-pact-losing.html', 'snippet': 'United Automobile Workers leaders said voting on a new labor agreement is tight at Ford, leaving the deciding votes in the hands of workers at three big plants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEARBORN, Mich. — Leaders of the United Automobile Workers union said on Wednesday that a slight majority of workers at Ford Motor Company have so far voted against a proposed new labor agreement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Results of U.A.W. Vote Show Ford Pact Losing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Results of U.A.W. Vote Show Ford Pact Losing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T00:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/717130f2-3d2b-5319-8fc7-7816651e294a', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/717130f2-3d2b-5319-8fc7-7816651e294a'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Brown will be chief deputy attorney general responsible for criminal prosecutions, and Janet Sabel will be chief deputy attorney general in charge of affirmative litigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/business/attorney-general-of-ny-picks-top-deputies.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Brown will be chief deputy attorney general responsible for criminal prosecutions, and Janet Sabel wi