late what it charged to service Navy ships across much of the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After nearly two years of settlement talks broke down, the Justice Department announced Wednesday that it was moving forward with a civil fraud lawsuit against one of the ship-supply contractors said to have overcharged the Navy by tens of millions of dollars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. to Sue Contractor It Says Bilked the Navy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. to Sue Contractor It Says Bilked the Navy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inchcape Shipping Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense Contracts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis, Leonard Glenn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T00:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew and Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://ar