87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf346659-6f68-553b-bfd6-a526c8e97afa'}, {'abstract': 'A state court judge in San Francisco on Wednesday ordered the destruction of five frozen embryos after a man challenged his ex-wife’s right to use them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/us/california-judge-orders-frozen-embryos-destroyed.html', 'snippet': 'A state court judge in San Francisco on Wednesday ordered the destruction of five frozen embryos after a man challenged his ex-wife’s right to use them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the first decision in California to address a dispute over the fate of frozen embryos after a couple’s divorce, a state judge in San Francisco on Wednesday ordered the destruction of five embryos after a man challenged his ex-wife’s right to use them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Judge Orders Frozen Embryos Destroyed ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Judge Orders Frozen Embryos Destroyed ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Davis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T03:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9405cd92-0b61-5d99-8574-9885deed44af', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9405cd92-0b61-5d99-8574-9885deed44af'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Birmingham was the author of best sellers about a range of social strata and places like the Dakota apartment building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/nyregion/stephen-birmingham-chronicler-of-the-rich-and-other-elites-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Birmingham was the author of best sellers about a range of social strata and places like the Dakota apartment building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Birmingham, the prolific novelist, purveyor of popular sociology and raconteur of the rich and famous in best-selling books like “ ‘Our Crowd’: The Great Jewish Families of New York” and “The Right People: A Portrait of the American Social Establishment,” died on Sunday at his home in Manhattan. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/arts/19birmingham-obit-1/19birmingham-obit-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen Birmingham, Chronicler of the Rich and Other Elites, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stephen Birmingham Dies; Chronicler of the Wealthy and Other Elites Was 86', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birmingham, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T03:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cf7e6ac-d665-5f32-a123-11a8ae0ec5cf', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cf7e6ac-d665-5f32-a123-11a8ae0ec5cf'}, {'abstract': 'A nasal spray designed to reverse opioid overdoses won approval from the Food and Drug Administration, expanding the options for treating drug overdoses without medical training.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/us/fda-approves-a-nasal-spray-to-combat-opioid-overdose.html', 'snippet': 'A nasal spray designed to reverse opioid overdoses won approval from the Food and Drug Administration, expanding the options for treating drug overdoses without medical training.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A nasal spray designed to reverse opioid overdoses won approval from the Food and Drug Administration on Wednesday, expanding the options for treating drug overdoses without medical training. Until now, all versions of the overdose reversal drug naloxone were injectable. The spray, called Narcan, will make it easier for ordinary people to treat someone who has taken too much oxycodone, morphine or heroin. Adapt Pharma Inc., the company that makes it, said it would offer the spray at a discount to emergency workers, firefighters and the police. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Approves a Nasal Spray to Combat Opioid Overdose', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Approves a Nasal Spray to Combat Opioid Overdose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Naloxone (Drug)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T03:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/75730691-ee6d-5c8c-b1c9-86e4706fca89', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75730691-ee6d-5c8c-b1c9-86e4706fca89'}, {'abstract': 'Government forces and insurgent factions in the Damascus suburbs planned to announce a Russian-brokered deal for a 15-day cease-fire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/world/middleeast/syria-truce-near-damascus-is-planned.html', 'snippet': 'Government forces and insurgent factions in the Damascus suburbs planned to announce a Russian-brokered deal for a 15-day cease-fire.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Syrian antigovernment activists said Wednesday that government forces and insurgent factions in the Damascus suburbs planned to announce a Russian-brokered deal for a 15-day cease-fire that could begin as soon as Thursday. United Nations officials and international negotiators are trying to hammer out a countrywide cease-fire as world leaders gather in Vienna in an effort to renew peace talks, and it was unclear whether the Russian-brokered effort was separate and parallel, or a step toward reaching a more comprehensive agreement. The Russian involvement was seen as a sign that it now had the upper hand — more so than Iran, President Bashar al-Assad’s closest ally. The truce would cover the East Ghouta suburbs that have been cut off from Damascus by the fighting. The truce would open checkpoints into East Ghouta, allowing humanitarian aid to get in and civilians to leave, according to several antigovernment activists reached in the area. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Truce Near Damascus Is Planned', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Syria: Truce Near Damascus Is Planned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_