.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/us/us-investigators-struggle-to-track-homegrown-isis-suspects.html', 'snippet': 'Many in the United States who are believed to have Islamic State ties have never visited Syria, and thwarting them is like trying to prevent a school shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — At least three dozen people in the United States suspected of ties to the Islamic State were under heavy electronic or physical surveillance even before the Paris attacks, senior American officials say. But unlike the attackers in France, the officials say, the majority of those under investigation here never traveled to Syria to fight alongside the Islamic State or receive training from it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/world/19fighters-web/19fighters-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Investigators Struggle to Track Homegrown ISIS Suspects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspects in U.S. Who Don’t Travel to Syria Are Even Harder to Investigate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt, Eric Schmitt and Matt Apuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21cdea14-1e8a-5cca-942b-92e3d69eb249', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21cdea14-1e8a-5cca-942b-92e3d69eb249'}, {'abstract': 'William Coupon’s classic style started out in an chaotic place: the Mudd Club. He slowed things down to the pace of formal portraiture, taking the circus out of the tent.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/punk-portraits-of-new-york/', 'snippet': 'William Coupon’s classic style started out in an chaotic place: the Mudd Club. He slowed things down to the pace of formal portraiture, taking the circus out of the tent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Coupon photographed Ronald Reagan and he photographed Lydia Lunch, both in the same way: against a backdrop of hand-painted Belgian linen, side-lit by a single fixture. For three and a half decades, he has varied little from this method, whether working in the Oval Office or the tribal regions of the Amazon rain forest. “It’s the classic medium shot, chiaroscuro light,” Mr. Coupon, 62, said the other day, describing his method and mission. “I knew if I focused on other subcultures I could hit on a range of people. I thought, I want to photograph everyone in the world.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Punk Portraits of New York', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mudd Club (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b50ecbc-9618-5e2e-a780-047b278731e3', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b50ecbc-9618-5e2e-a780-047b278731e3'}, {'abstract': 'Clint Trickett, a former West Virginia quarterback who was forced to retire because of a number of concussions, is the quarterbacks coach of a top junior college team in Mississippi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/11/18/sports/ncaafootball/a-quarterbacks-new-role.html', 'snippet': 'Clint Trickett, a former West Virginia quarterback who was forced to retire because of a number of concussions, is the quarterbacks coach of a top junior college team in Mississippi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clint Trickett, a former West Virginia quarterback who was forced to retire because of a number of concussions, is the quarterbacks coach of a top junior college team in Mississippi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/sports/ncaafootball/TRICKETT-slide-PH47/TRICKETT-slide-PH47-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/18/sports/ncaafootball/TRICKETT-slide-PH47/TRICKETT-slide-PH47-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/18/sports/ncaafootball/TRICKETT-slide-PH47/TRICKETT-slide-PH47-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '