[{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09141cb3-72e2-5666-a4f6-4d41be980422', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09141cb3-72e2-5666-a4f6-4d41be980422'}, {'abstract': 'For his new “Commencements” series, debuting here, the photographer Ruben Brulat braved 130-degree temperatures at remote African lava lakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/t-magazine/ruben-brulat-african-lava-naked-photographs.html', 'snippet': 'For his new “Commencements” series, debuting here, the photographer Ruben Brulat braved 130-degree temperatures at remote African lava lakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Ruben Brulat was traveling alone through Iceland in 2009 when, in the midst of setting up his camp, he was arrested by the beauty of a rock perched on the mountainside, almost ready to fall from among the clouds seemingly wrapped around its peak. Setting up his camera on a timer, Brulat followed his senses and captured himself lying naked in the primal elements. It was a transformative moment, and it started him on his projects “Primates,” “Paths” and now, seen here for the first time, “Commencements.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Self-Portraits of a Naked Adventurer', 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brulat, Ruben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Djibouti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eritrea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Danakil Desert (Africa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '