_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remixed Signals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkinson, Isabel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Aurel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T20:32:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Wilkinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilkinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/699f41cc-d713-5fa3-9744-24a403c04e14', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/699f41cc-d713-5fa3-9744-24a403c04e14'}, {'abstract': 'On Abbot Kinney Boulevard, local institutions are joined by hip new outposts originally from Oakland, Portland and New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/t-magazine/venice-beach-california-food-coffee-travel.html', 'snippet': 'On Abbot Kinney Boulevard, local institutions are joined by hip new outposts originally from Oakland, Portland and New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just under a mile from Venice Beach and its winding boardwalk, the once-destitute stretch of Abbot Kinney Boulevard has emerged as a buzzy destination with indie shops, luxe fashion boutiques and eateries. Since Gjelina opened there in 2008, its artisanal pizzas have helped draw in a steady crowd of locals, low-key hipsters, fashionable bohos and intrigued out-of-towners. Just this year, the restaurant released a cookbook and introduced Gjusta, an equally popular bakery, deli, smokehouse, coffee and juice bar next door. (Over the summer, the “Top Chef” alum Nyesha Arrington began serving lamb-belly won tons and wakame-cured hamachi out of the new rustic-chic dining room at Leona, on a nearby street. And not far away, and a month later, the charming restaurant-retail storefront Dudley Market opened its doors, selling utilitarian handmade goods, from minimalist ceramics to artistic cutting boards, alongside gourmet pantry offerings.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/t-magazine/19tmag-kinney/19tmag-kinney-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Beach’s Influx of Trendy Outsiders', 'kicker': 'Food 