}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bef79433-81ba-55ff-8e57-409b0f5d1859', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bef79433-81ba-55ff-8e57-409b0f5d1859'}, {'abstract': 'The artist’s first full retrospective in New York, at the Bronx Museum of the Arts, crackles with fervor, desire and coded insider-outsider knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/arts/design/martin-wong-an-urban-visionary-with-a-hungry-eye.html', 'snippet': 'The artist’s first full retrospective in New York, at the Bronx Museum of the Arts, crackles with fervor, desire and coded insider-outsider knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until 1989, the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s late night was Tuesday. It was a good time for a visit; attendance was sparse. So I went a lot. It was also when I’d bump into the artist Martin Wong who briefly, and somewhat improbably, worked as a clerk in the Met’s bookstore. I say improbably because I was accustomed to seeing him in a different setting, on the Lower East Side, where he often dressed like a rodeo cowboy and ran with graffiti artists who were tagging the neighborhood.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20MARTINWONGJP8/20MARTINWONGJP8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Martin Wong, an Urban Visionary With a Hungry Eye', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Urban Visionary With a Hungry Eye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Museum of the Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Martin (1946-99)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T22:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8e2af52-f856-5972-929e-ac7c3a2a3433', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8e2af52-f856-5972-929e-ac7c3a2a3433'}, {'abstract': 'Introvert Shonda Rhimes says “yes” for a year. But (maybe more importantly) she also says no.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/19/saying-yes-and-no-shonda-rhimes-style/', 'snippet': 'Introvert Shonda Rhimes says “yes” for a year. But (maybe more importantly) she also says no.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shonda Rhimes, who is famous for her role as creator, head writer, executive producer and showrunner of “Grey’s Anatomy,” “Private Practice” and “Scandal” and as executive producer of “How to Get Away With Murder,” is an introvert. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherlode-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/19/us/yearofyes-motherlode/yearofyes-motherl