46537b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Fordjour’s unsettling installation at the Robert Blumenthal Gallery draws on memories of prayer rooms and revival meetings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/arts/design/from-derek-fordjour-a-sense-of-abandoned-ritual.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Fordjour’s unsettling installation at the Robert Blumenthal Gallery draws on memories of prayer rooms and revival meetings.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20FORJOURGALLERY1/20FORJOURGALLERY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Derek Fordjour, a Sense of Abandoned Ritual', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Derek Fordjour, a Sense of Abandoned Ritual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blumenthal,  Robert, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fordjour, Derek (1974- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-19T22:19:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4901b7ab-1ce7-5cd7-950a-6d90d710cb91', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4901b7ab-1ce7-5cd7-950a-6d90d710cb91'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Grillo’s raucous, densely composed works are full of apparent pop-culture motifs that are nearly all invented, and Mr. Lewis’s “Badlandz” is a wry zombie formalist installation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/arts/design/joe-grillo-and-zane-lewis-in-separate-shows-at-the-hole.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Grillo’s raucous, densely composed works are full of apparent pop-culture motifs that are nearly all invented, and Mr. Lewis’s “Badlandz” is a wry zombie formalist installation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Grillo, who emerged at the turn of the century as the youngest member of the Dearraindrop collective, has titled his first solo show in New York City, at the Hole, with an implied streak of profanity, “#%@&?!!!.” His raucous, densely composed works are crowded with apparent pop-culture figures and motifs that are nearly all invented. Rendered in saturated colors outlined in black, they operate in an area bounded by painting, cartooning, graffiti and perhaps video games. Mr. Grillo’s efforts bring new energy to the high-low graphic tradition that includes artists like Pierre Alechinsky, William Copley, Keith Haring, Kenny Scharf and Sue Williams. However, a crazed retinal overload tends to distinguish Mr. Grillo’s works from those of his predecessors. He has pop culture in his veins, but his efforts stop short of garishness and mechanical slickness by being visibly improvised by hand.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 528}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLERY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLERY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/20/arts/20GRILLO1GALLERY2/20GRILLO1GALLE