c76d'}, {'abstract': 'The trim — more than $1 billion from last year’s budget — is the first time since the financial crisis that Volkswagen has not increased investment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/21/business/international/volkswagen-emissions-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'The trim — more than $1 billion from last year’s budget — is the first time since the financial crisis that Volkswagen has not increased investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOLFSBURG, Germany — Scarred by an emissions-cheating scandal, Volkswagen on Friday said it would need to cut its budget next year for new technology and research — a reversal after years of increased spending aimed at becoming the world’s biggest carmaker.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'VW Cuts Its R.&D. Budget in Face of Costly Emissions Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Costs Rising in Scandal, VW Makes Budget Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diesel Power', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Emissions (Transportation)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muller, Matthias (1953- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T13:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db263263-c39a-5afc-9124-1ebf873fb756', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db263263-c39a-5afc-9124-1ebf873fb756'}, {'abstract': 'A new commenting system is in the works, and for many, it can’t come fast enough.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/change-needed-for-commenting-that-favors-the-verified/', 'snippet': 'A new commenting system is in the works, and for many, it can’t come fast enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In emails, in online comments and even in that wonder of our time called face-to-face conversation, I hear a lot about Times readers’ frustration with the existence of “verified commenters.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Change Needed for Commenting That Favors the ‘Verified’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T13:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb671ed4-f5c6-5bd6-8159-efe2a53e1aec', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb671ed4-f5c6-5bd6-8159-efe2a53e1aec'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Aldrich and Nicholas Ray were rugged postwar auteurs whose styles flew in the face of assembly-line filmmaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/movies/homevideo/emperor-of-the-north-and-wind-across-the-everglades-fighters-in-nature-and-showbiz.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Aldrich and Nicholas Ray were rugged postwar auteurs whose styles flew in the face of assembly-line filmmaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of those studio directors who, more or less the same age as Orson Welles, began working in movies within a decade of “Citizen Kane” (1941) represent Hollywood’s “greatest generation.” Survivors of the Great Depression and often veterans of World War II, they fought the good war against assembly-line filmmaking. Robert Aldrich (1918-83) and Nicholas Ray (1911-79) were two.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22HOBERMAN/22HOBERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth':