'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VMware Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T14:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Kerstetter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kerstetter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6731439-ee14-5858-a992-90491360fe4b', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6731439-ee14-5858-a992-90491360fe4b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The dead in Coventry are buried in a common grave in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/1940-coventry-lays-dead-to-rest/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The dead in Coventry are buried in a common grave in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COVENTRY, England — Thin wisps of smoke still rose from the ruins of central Coventry today [Nov. 20], and rescuers still were searching for further victims, as a thousand men and women silently watched their loved ones laid to rest in a common grave. The dead — there were 200 — were the victims of German bombs showered ruthlessly and indiscriminately last Thursday night — a night Coventry will never forget. Some of them mothers, some children and some of them the men who manned the factories vital to Great Britain’s prosecution of the war, they now lie in plain pine coffins, placed end to end and tier upon tier in a deep, narrow trench hastily dug by steam shovels borrowed from a construction job.\xa0—\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 21, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Coventry Lays Dead to Rest', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T14:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13374359-8c8b-55a3-b5c4-ca1a70c6c2d3', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13374359-8c8b-55a3-b5c4-ca1a70c6c2d3'}, {'abstract': 'Xi Jinping paid tribute to the 1980s Communist Party leader who helped restore his father’s political career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/world/asia/china-hu-yaobang-birthday-xi-jinping.html', 'snippet': 'Xi Jinping paid tribute to the 1980s Communist Party leader who helped restore his father’s political career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s staunchly traditionalist Communist leader, Xi Jinping, paid tribute on Friday to a predecessor, Hu Yaobang, who was in many ways his opposite in temperament and politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/world/20huyaobang03/20huyaobang02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/world/20huyaobang03/20huyaobang02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 566}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/world/20huyaobang03/20huyaobang02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'ju