is enormous glass-fronted office at the Bastille opera house, one ear clamped to his cellphone, talking at top speed while motioning at a visitor to sit down. “I tell you, it’s nonsense,” he said impatiently into his cell. “We are not taking them off. We are making them removable. It’s entirely different.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 898}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22LISSNER1/22LISSNER1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day (and Night) at the Opera With Stéphane Lissner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Day (and Night) at the Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lissner, Stephane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Moses und Aron (Opera)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schoenberg, Arnold', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/624c0d16-9596-5f90-b7d5-3c72019803e5', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/624c0d16-9596-5f90-b7d5-3c72019803e5'}, {'abstract': 'This show, consisting of more than 70 works, contemplates the future of photography in art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/arts/design/photo-poetics-an-anthology-features-10-artists-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'This show, consisting of more than 70 works, contemplates the future of photography in art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As photography disperses in an ever more granular way into daily life — through phones, social media, ubiquitous screens — artists are hauling the medium back into the studio to see if it can be reconstituted into something more tangible. Sara VanDerBeek once described how she created an object, captured its image and “then, through the process of making a final print, framing it and hanging it on the wall,” rendered the image “an object again.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1003, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1003, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Photo-Poetics: An Anthology’ Features 10 Artists at the Guggenheim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Images as Objects, Objects as Images', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value':