arly Western intellectual tradition in the ancient Greek world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The philosopher Sidney Morgenbesser, beloved by generations of Columbia University students (including me), was known for lines of wit that yielded nuggets of insight. He kept up his instructive shtick until the end, remarking to a colleague shortly before he died: “Why is God making me suffer so much? Just because I don’t believe in him?” For Morgenbesser, nothing worth pondering, including disbelief, could be entirely de-\xadparadoxed.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 241, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 241}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Goldstein/1122-BKS-Goldstein-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'