intage, $17.) In the span of a year, America’s friendly rapport with Chinese leaders devolved into fraught antagonism. Here, Bern\xadstein, a former New York Times correspondent, argues that the longstanding diplomatic strain between the two countries can be traced to China’s political disintegration at the end of World War II.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T16:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joumana Khatib', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khatib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/be75c7ce-bfc7-5a33-99f0-bd96f5510685', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be75c7ce-bfc7-5a33-99f0-bd96f5510685'}, {'abstract': 'Before paying a fee for threat protection, it’s best to do due diligence on the quality of the adviser providing the assessment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/21/your-money/taking-a-rational-look-at-the-risk-of-threats.html', 'snippet': 'Before paying a fee for threat protection, it’s best to do due diligence on the quality of the adviser providing the assessment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE terrorist attacks in Paris last week that killed 130 people and injured hundreds more instilled fear in millions of people who weren’t anywhere near the attacks. That, of course, is the point of terrorism.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre