': 'Kennedy, David M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilmore, Glenda Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sugrue, Thomas J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'These United States: A Nation in the Making, 1890 to the Present (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T17:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b19a5e76-0759-5de7-8ca8-3b20d0248ec5', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b19a5e76-0759-5de7-8ca8-3b20d0248ec5'}, {'abstract': 'One history of ancient Rome and another of the first five Roman emperors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/books/review/mary-beards-spqr-and-tom-hollands-dynasty.html', 'snippet': 'One history of ancient Rome and another of the first five Roman emperors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How on earth did they do it? The Greek historian Polybius, writing in the second century B.C., was the first to ask the question: “Who could be so indifferent or so idle that they did not want to find out how, and under what kind of political organization, almost the whole of the inhabited world was conquered and fell under the sole power of the Romans in less than 53 years?” It was not as if Rome was a promising spot: a swampy piece of ground up a barely navigable river surrounded by scrubby hills, its few thousand inhabitants alternately flooded out and ravaged by malaria.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/15/books/review/