y’s role in overcoming the Great Depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, the international economy came within weeks of catastrophic collapse. Concerted action by the world’s monetary authorities staved off disaster. Although stagnation continues to plague much of the globe, especially Europe, a major depression was avoided.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Money Makers,’ by Eric Rauchway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Bad as Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauchway, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Money Makers: How Roosevelt and Keynes Ended the Depression, Defeated Fascism, and Secured a Prosperous Peace (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T17:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffry Frieden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frieden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2855c4de-37cb-555e-8024-297ff1660f85', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2855c4de-37cb-555e-8024-297ff1660f85'}, {'abstract': 'Magna Carta’s historical importance is still debated, but the story behind it has its own merits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/books/review/magna-carta-the-birth-of-liberty-by-dan-jones.html', 'snippet': 'Magna Carta’s historical importance is still debated, but the story behind it has its own merits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Modern liberal democracy, we hear, began 800 years ago in England on a marshy field near London. Pressed by his aggrieved subjects, a hated king accepted strict new limits on royal power. The pact, named Magna Carta (Great Charter), became entrenched in British law. A bulwark against oppressive rulers, it inspired 17th-century England’s parliamentarians and 18th-century America’s revolutionaries. It remains a founding text of Western constitutional government.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Magna Carta: The Birth of Liberty,’ by Dan Jones', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Block', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Dan (1981- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magna Carta (1215)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Magna Carta: The Birth of Liberty (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T17:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edmund Fawcett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edmund', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fawcett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b20012f-b0af-5bb8-96c7-997f5e02b1ec', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b20012f-b0af-5bb8-96c7-997f5e02b1ec'}, {'abstract': 'Ted Koppel says a cyberattack on the nation’s power sources is likely, and we’re nowhere near ready.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/books/review/lights-out-by-ted-koppel.html', 'snippet': 'Ted Koppel says a cyberattack on the nation’s power sources is likely, and we’re nowhere near ready.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The possibility that terrorists or a hostile foreign state could take down the American power grid either by a cyberattack or by an electromagnetic pulse attack is one of those haunting possibilities that keep strategic planners from sleeping peacefully at night. In “Lights Out: A Cyberattack, a Nation Unprepared, Surviving the Aftermath,” Ted Koppel, one of America’s most experienced and best-known journalists, has attempted to show readers why the danger is real, the degree to which the authorities are unprepared and the steps we can take now to be ready when the power goes down.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/books/review/1122-BKS-Mead/1122-BKS-Mead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lights Out,’ by Ted Koppel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grid Lock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koppel, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lights Out: A Cyberattack, a Nation Unprepared, Surviving the Aftermath (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T17:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walter Russell Mead', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walter', 'middlename': 'Russell', 'lastname': 'Mead', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/da0f17be-086f-5058-9974-8d73797c3eb7', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da0f17be-086f-5058-9974-8d73797c3eb7'}, {'abstract': 'Audio recordings of erotic fiction are a booming business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/books/review/erotic-fiction-audiobooks-are-a-booming-business.html', 'snippet': 'Audio recordings of erotic fiction are a booming business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month I finished recording an audio version of my new book in four days — a full day ahead of schedule — and I was feeling pretty good about it. It helped that the audio technician at \xadDuArt, a film and recording studio in Midtown Manhattan, could hear like a bat and caught every stomach gurgle. As I was about to leave, I jokingly asked the audiobook studio director if he could make the book a runaway audio best seller.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subty