nt’s Hospital campus in the West Village, was filed with the city this past week — a spacious duplex penthouse with a private rooftop terrace that sold for $25,489,849.99 and was the most expensive closed sale, according to public records. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 865}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1422, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/realestate/22TICKET/22TICKET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A West Village Penthouse for $25.49 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Views From the Rooftop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Vivian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Vincent's Hospital Manhattan", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T20:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Marino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/201ae439-1c05-5b6a-87cd-cf4c620774ce', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/201ae439-1c05-5b6a-87cd-cf4c620774ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Police apologized for the behavior of officers who used intimate relationships, one nine years long, to gather intelligence and infiltrate activist groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/21/world/europe/british-police-apologize-for-undercover-officers-intimate-tactics.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Police apologized for the behavior of officers who used intimate relationships, one nine years long, to gather intelligence and infiltrate activist groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — They lived together, traveled abroad on vacation and, for five years, behaved like any other couple. Then one day the man, who called himself Mark Cassidy, disappeared, leading his bewildered ex-partner to eventually discover that she had been living with a married police spy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Police Apologize for Undercover Officers’ Intimate Tactics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Police Apologize for Undercover Officers&#8217; Intimate Infiltration Tactics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T20:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87629c10-13f2-5d56-91c6-6c8fe2335ce2', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87629c10-13f2-5d56-91c6-6c8fe2335ce2'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Eisner opens “Nomad 1957,” a weeklong installation inside the Jean Prouvé structure outside of Maxfield.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/20/t-magazine/lisa-eisner-jewelry-exhibit-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'Lisa Eisner opens “Nomad 1957,” a weeklong installation inside the Jean Prouvé structure outside of Maxfield.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took some convincing to get Tommy Perse, the owner of the L.A. boutique Maxfield, to agree to the jewelry installation “Nomad 1957.” But Lisa Eisner is nothing if not persuasive. A longtime patron of the Los Angeles fashion institution, Eisner, a jewelry designer (and sometime artist, stylist, photographer and publisher), began selling pieces at Maxfield earlier this year. Three months ago, the store approached her to do an out-of-the-box installation with her pieces. Eisner’s first instinct was to ask about Structure Nomade — a large, prefab space designed by the French architect Jean Prouvé in 1957 that sits just outside Maxfield’s entrance, which had never been used for anything.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-eisner-3/20tmag-eisner-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Los Angeles, Jewelry Mingles With Midcentury Design'