ew York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/arts/21UPATREESUB/21UPATREESUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘More Up a Tree,’ Performance Art Through the Looking Glass', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dancer, a Drummer and a Looking Glass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Serpa Soares, Claudia (Dancer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Jim (1962- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-20T22:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ce6d3de-8b7c-5046-b1ce-13255f59a320', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ce6d3de-8b7c-5046-b1ce-13255f59a320'}, {'abstract': 'In interviews around the country, many Americans were sorry about what had happened and fearful of attacks at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/21/us/americans-view-paris-attacks-with-empathy-fear-and-resolve.html', 'snippet': 'In interviews around the country, many Americans were sorry about what had happened and fearful of attacks at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — It made parents worry for their children studying abroad. It sent a shiver of fear into plans for vacations to France. Cafes and nightclubs in Miami and Los Angeles felt newly vulnerable, not so different from the bloody scenes unfolding on people’s phones and televisions. For Americans accustomed to tuning out foreign conflicts, it brought the world crashing in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/21/us/21america-web03SUB/21america-web03SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/21/us/21america-web03SUB/21america-web03SUB-articleLarge