c-a005-0330b2ab2d87'}, {'abstract': 'The sales of The Financial Times and The Economist for about $2 billion cumulatively raise questions about whether the deals will pay off financially for the buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/business/media/pearsons-big-paydays-defy-the-odds-against-print-media.html', 'snippet': 'The sales of The Financial Times and The Economist for about $2 billion cumulatively raise questions about whether the deals will pay off financially for the buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been tough sledding for print media. More than 150 newspapers have closed or converted to digital-only offerings in the last two years. Recently the magazine giants Condé Nast and Time Inc. have both cut employees and closed magazines.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/business/pearsonjump/pearsonjump-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pearson’s Big Paydays Defy the Odds Against Print Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Paydays for Pearson Defy Print Media Odds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohan, William D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economist, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nikkei Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economist Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exor SpA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-22T21:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By William D. Cohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3950da90-93b7-5414-9e6a-c5a60e15e686', 'word_count': 1711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3950da90-93b7-5414-9e6a-c5a60e15e686'}, {'abstract': 'Surveys of voters show that young people, independents and possibly even blacks and Hispanics are not excited about Hillary Rodham Clinton’s candidacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/us/politics/lack-of-enthusiasm-from-supporters-may-undermine-clintons-lead.html', 'snippet': 'Surveys of voters show that young people, independents and possibly even blacks and Hispanics are not excited about Hillary Rodham Clinton’s candidacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s cause for concern in Hillaryland, the constellation of Democratic advisers, supporters and politicians counting on the former secretary of state to lead the party to a sweeping victory next November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/us/23letter-web/23letter-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'