roject, which promotes and commissions classical works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/arts/music/review-jack-quartet-and-anthony-mcgill-perform-a-menu-of-american-delicacies.html', 'snippet': 'This concert at Roulette in Brooklyn was the first New York event for the American Music Project, which promotes and commissions classical works.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Wind in High Places” is a string quartet by John Luther Adams that uses only open strings and natural harmonics. Written in 2011 in memory of a friend and hiking companion, it evokes the glassy stillness of the Alaskan wilderness that for decades was Mr. Adams’s home and inspiration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23MCGILL-SUB/23MCGILL-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: JACK Quartet and Anthony McGill Perform a Menu of American Delicacies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Floating Freely in a Sublime Landscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Geoffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roulette (Brooklyn, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Music Project', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, John Luther', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Earle', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGill, Anthony', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JACK Quartet', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-22T22:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d56be8-7db9-57e0-8d17-15967ecbbd84', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d56be8-7db9-57e0-8d17-15967ecbbd84'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cencic, a countertenor accompanied by this ensemble, sang arias in Italian during a program featuring selections by composers associated with Naples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/arts/music/review-max-emanuel-cencic-and-il-pomo-doro-bring-baroque-to-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cencic, a countertenor accompanied by this ensemble, sang arias in Italian during a program featuring selections by composers associated with Naples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How a singer conveys the text is usually an integral part of a vocal performance, assuming the listener understands the words and story or can rely on subtitles. Deciphering unfamiliar lyrics when syllables are elongated and ornamented can be a challenge in any language: Subtitles are often provided even for English librettos.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Max Emanuel Cencic and Il Pomo D’Oro Bring Baroque to the Met', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vocalist Interprets the Obscure With an Assist From Period Instruments ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Il Pomo D'Oro (Music Group)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cencic, Max Emanuel (1976- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-22T22:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cecb5779-6958-5e91-944c-304bebcc8f82', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cecb5779-6958-5e91-944c-304bebcc8f82'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Barry’s new novel follows an emotionally raw Lennon on a 1978 journey through western Ireland to commune with nature and himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/books/review-in-beatlebone-an-imagined-trip-with-john-lennon.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Barry’s new novel follows an emotionally raw Lennon on a 1978 journey through western Ireland to commune with nature and himself.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Beatlebone,” the strange and exhilarating new novel by the Irish writer Kevin Barry, is about John Lennon — kind of. It follows him closely for around 200 pages, through a few comically calamitous days in 1978, as he travels through western Ireland to an island off its coast, bought on a lark 11 years earlier. He’s nearing 40 here; past drugs, past scream therapy, far past the Beatles, and stripped raw emotionally, tired “but not for sleeping,” full of “large sad warmish feelings.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23BOOKBARR2/23BOOKBARR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 935, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23BOOKBARR2/23BOOKBARR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 935}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23BOOKBARR2/23BOOKBARR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/23/arts/23BOOKBARR2/23BOOKBARR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1315, 'subType': 'superJu