European tour because of the terror attacks in Paris, the Foo Fighters have released a new five-song EP on schedule. A countdown clock on the band’s website hit zero at midnight on Monday, revealing a free download of “Saint Cecilia,” along with a link to donate to victims of the violence in Paris. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foo Fighters Turn Free ‘Saint Cecilia’ EP Into Tribute to Victims of  Paris Attacks', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foo Fighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-23T15:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/136e601e-e1b9-5692-9476-81a38932ecfa', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/136e601e-e1b9-5692-9476-81a38932ecfa'}, {'abstract': 'With the use of tests booming, the administration wants new regulatory powers, and even Republicans in Congress are looking at stricter standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/us/politics/fda-targets-inaccurate-medical-tests-citing-dangers-and-costs.html', 'snippet': 'With the use of tests booming, the administration wants new regulatory powers, and even Republicans in Congress are looking at stricter standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Inaccurate and unreliable medical tests are prompting abortions, promoting unnecessary surgeries, putting tens of thousands of people on unneeded drugs and raising medical costs, the Food and Drug Administration has concluded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/us/24tests-web/24tests-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Targets Inaccurate Medical Tests, Citing Dangers and Costs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Cites Dangers and Costs of Inaccurate Medical Tests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genomic Health Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-23T15:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2328d4d4-8f36-55be-947b-7c0f8dbf9c98', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2328d4d4-8f36-55be-947b-7c0f8dbf9c98'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to holiday entertaining, rough-around-the-edges is not only acceptable, but preferable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/t-magazine/in-praise-of-the-good-enough-holiday.html', 'snippet': 'When it comes to holiday entertaining, rough-around-the-edges is not only acceptable, but preferable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The winter celebrations are upon us, bringing with their glee the return of insecurities like: Is your centerpiece of the right niveau? Should you drape the banisters with balsam fir, or is boxwood more current? Which breed of artificial bird is trending to clamp among the boughs? And will you be able to hold your head up if you have not personally raised from poulthood the turkey that graces the holiday table (as Martha Stewart suggests) or hand-pressed the apple cider with which you braised the brisket?', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '65', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', '