{'abstract': 'Daniil Trifonov plays well with others at Kaufmann Concert Hall in the New York Philharmonic’s festival devoted to the composer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/arts/music/review-rachmaninoff-chemistry-at-the-92nd-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'Daniil Trifonov plays well with others at Kaufmann Concert Hall in the New York Philharmonic’s festival devoted to the composer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was something a bit perverse about the chamber-music program presented by the New York Philharmonic at the 92nd Street Y on Sunday, part of its three-week Rachmaninoff festival. Sure, the promise of the breathtaking pianist Daniil Trifonov joining forces with the violinist Sheryl Staples and the cellist Carter Brey in the seething “Trio Élégiaque” (Op. 9) was all it took to fill the Kaufmann Concert Hall. But to round out the program with two unfinished string quartets — works that Rachmaninoff abandoned, surely with good reason — when there is a luscious, masterly cello sonata begging to be played?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Rachmaninoff Chemistry at the 92nd Street Y', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Passion, Desolation and Chemistry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rachmaninoff, Sergei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trifonov, Daniil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-23T21:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60ae32ab-b50c-5f9d-b884-6e93b958138a', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60ae32ab-b50c-5f9d-b884-6e93b958138a'}, {'abstract': 'Breast milk may provide the ideal nourishment for an infant, but two recent studies are putting a different spin on the bottle-versus-breast debate.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/breast-feeding-is-good-for-mothers-not-just-babies/', 'snippet': 'Breast milk may provide the ideal nourishment for an infant, but two recent studies are putting a different spin on the bottle-versus-breast debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breast milk may provide the ideal nourishment for an infant, but two recent studies are putting a different spin on the bottle-versus-breast debate, suggesting it is mothers, and not just babies, who may have much to gain from breast-feeding. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/science/24wellbreast/24wellbreast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/24/science/24wellbreast/24wellbreast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/science/24wellbreast/24wellbreast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/science/24wellbreast/24well