 which means that hens live in housing that allows them to spend much of their day in open pasture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRESCENT CITY, Calif. — A decade ago, a couple running a dairy business in Northern California visited a Mennonite farm where the owner had used a flock of laying hens to teach his children business principles and instill values like responsibility and care for nature.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting the Chicken Before the Egg', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting the Chicken Before the Egg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alexandre Family EcoDairy Farms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-23T22:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68db1e87-fdae-5ad8-a219-13a97a880bd6', 'word_count': 1621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68db1e87-fdae-5ad8-a219-13a97a880bd6'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/23/nytnow/your-monday-evening-briefing-brussels-pfizer-david-cameron.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you n