e': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Tobias', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tobias', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77d726ba-1aa0-5026-8225-dcb24ffae296', 'word_count': 1313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77d726ba-1aa0-5026-8225-dcb24ffae296'}, {'abstract': 'The deaths came eight days after Egyptian border guards were accused in the fatal shootings of at least 15 Sudanese migrants trying to cross the frontier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/world/middleeast/egypt-forces-kill-5-sudanese-at-border.html', 'snippet': 'The deaths came eight days after Egyptian border guards were accused in the fatal shootings of at least 15 Sudanese migrants trying to cross the frontier.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Egyptian security forces on Monday shot and killed at least five Sudanese migrants who were trying to cross the border from Egypt into Israel, the military said in a statement.\xa0 \xa0The deaths came eight days after Egyptian border guards were accused in the fatal shootings of at least 15 Sudanese migrants trying to cross the frontier.\xa0 Human rights groups have for years criticized the Egyptian authorities as resorting too quickly to lethal force against migrants and asylum seekers, mostly from East Africa, who travel through the Sinai Peninsula to reach Israel.\xa0 In the latest episode, the military said the border guards fired warning shots and were moving to arrest the migrants when the Egyptian guards came under fire.\xa0 In addition to the five migrants who were killed, six others were injured, the statement said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Forces Kill 5 Sudanese at Border', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Egypt: Forces Kill 5 Sudanese at Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-24T04:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/366f2b58-726b-5ef4-90e3-ffd03a9ffacd', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366f2b58-726b-5ef4-90e3-ffd03a9ffacd'}, {'abstract': 'The Education Department said that students receiving subsidized lunches would be given admissions priority for half the seats at a Brooklyn school that is the subject of a contested rezoning proposal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/nyregion/admissions-quota-proposed-in-brooklyn-school-rezoning.html', 'snippet': 'The Education Department said that students receiving subsidized lunches would be given admissions priority for half the seats at a Brooklyn school that is the subject of a contested rezoning proposal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to concerns that a plan to redraw two Brooklyn school zones would fill an elementary school with affluent white children that currently serves mostly low-income minority children, Education Department staff members said on Monday that