ordon J. Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gordon', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e86db3d1-8ce8-50e8-8039-42643b3dd10c', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e86db3d1-8ce8-50e8-8039-42643b3dd10c'}, {'abstract': 'The $160 billion deal to combine Pfizer and Allergan does not appear to be illegal, but it should be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/24/opinion/pfizers-big-breakthrough-global-tax-avoidance.html', 'snippet': 'The $160 billion deal to combine Pfizer and Allergan does not appear to be illegal, but it should be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The $160 billion deal to combine Pfizer and Allergan, the maker of Botox, does not appear to be illegal. But it should be. This merger is a tax-dodging maneuver that enriches shareholders and executives while shortchanging the public and robbing the Treasury of money that would pay for a host of government programs — including education, scientific research and other services that also benefit corporations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/opinion/24tue1/24tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/24/opinion/24tue1/24tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/opinion/24tue1/24tue1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/24/opinion/24tue1/24tue1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 968,