nal': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85c19775-0856-5be1-913d-5e6974605905', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85c19775-0856-5be1-913d-5e6974605905'}, {'abstract': 'Tours include visits to Slovenia and Croatia, or to Macedonia and Montenegro, sampling home-cooked meals and street food and traveling to markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/22/travel/travel-deals-food-tours-of-eastern-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Tours include visits to Slovenia and Croatia, or to Macedonia and Montenegro, sampling home-cooked meals and street food and traveling to markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intrepid Travel is expanding its food tour offerings into Eastern Europe in 2016 with its “Real Food Adventures,” introducing travelers to home-cooked meals, street food and local food markets in four countries. The first trip,  to Slovenia and Croatia, leaves May 29 (from $2,119) and the second, to Montenegro and Macedonia, on June 9 (from $1,647), destinations where “slow food” is a way of life. Both 10-day tours include culinary and cultural highlights.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/travel/22HORIZON/22HORIZON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/22/travel/22HORIZON/22HORIZON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/22/travel/22HORIZON/22HORIZON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub