rd_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcc1a7b4-000e-5cfb-bcab-207198c7f6ae'}, {'abstract': 'This film, starring James McAvoy and Daniel Radcliffe, recasts a ghoulish story into something of a buddy movie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/movies/review-victor-frankenstein-recasts-a-tale-that-keeps-on-giving.html', 'snippet': 'This film, starring James McAvoy and Daniel Radcliffe, recasts a ghoulish story into something of a buddy movie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You cannot keep a good monster down, especially when there’s franchise money to be made. This doubtless explains “Victor Frankenstein,” a pop romp that exhumes Mary Shelley’s famous monster-maker for a jaunty bromance with his bestie, Igor. It’s a hyperventilated resurrection that owes less to Shelley (or most Frankenstein flicks) than to Guy Ritchie’s Sherlock Holmes diversions, which turned Holmes (Robert Downey Jr.) and Dr. Watson (Jude Law) into 19th-century action heroes complete with cheerfully deployed violence and self-regarding smiles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25VICTOR/25VICTOR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Victor Frankenstein’ Recasts a Tale That Keeps On Giving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Igor and His Boss, Recast in a 19th-Century Tale That Keeps On Giving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGuigan, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAvoy, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radcliffe, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landis, Max (1985- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Victor Frankenstein (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-24T22:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1b68f6e-6f6a-5c61-b739-9266db95389d', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1b68f6e-6f6a-5c61-b739-9266db95389d'}, {'abstract': 'Homo sapiens and giant reptiles co-exist in this animated, alternate universe version of Earth history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/movies/review-the-good-dinosaur-pixar-human-and-apatosaurus.html', 'snippet': 'Homo sapiens and giant reptiles co-exist in this animated, alternate universe version of Earth history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blink and you may miss the sly joke that sets “The Good Dinosaur” on its enchantingly eccentric way. It begins with a near apocalypse 65 million years ago and an asteroid racing toward Earth. And while that’s around the time, more or less, that science hypothesizes the dinosaurs bit the dust, the wizards at Pixar have forged another creation story. Instead of crashing, the space rock zips past the big blue marble. Fast forward a few million years to what looks like the American Northwest, where two apatosaurs are farming the land, tilling the soil with honest sweat and giant noses.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 237, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 237}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/arts/25GOODDINO/25GOODDINO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The Good Dinosaur,’ a Reptile Tends to His Human Pet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '…\xa0And a Reptile Tends to His Human Pet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sohn, Peter (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Sam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Good Dinosaur (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-24T22:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42584b2-c844-5baa-bcb0-8df270338077', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42584b2-c844-5baa-bcb0-8df270338077'}, {'abstract': 'Video does exist of people celebrating after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks, but the cheering took place in the Middle East, not in New Jersey, as Donald J. Trump has asserted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/24/the-video-of-celebrations-that-was-broadcast-on-911/', 'snippet': 'Video does exist of people celebrating after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks, but the cheering took place in the Middle East, not in New Jersey, as Donald J. Trum