: 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-25T03:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/f55c590d-71e5-51f6-b83a-0407176b5a02', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f55c590d-71e5-51f6-b83a-0407176b5a02'}, {'abstract': 'Several cabinet ministers said that only 10,000 of the planned 25,000 refugees would arrive by the end of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/world/americas/canada-syrians-arrival-is-delayed-and-officials-cite-need-to-prepare.html', 'snippet': 'Several cabinet ministers said that only 10,000 of the planned 25,000 refugees would arrive by the end of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Canada’s new Liberal government has delayed its plan to bring 25,000 Syrian refugees into the country by the end of the year. At a news conference\xa0on Tuesday, several cabinet ministers said that only 10,000 would arrive by the original deadline, with the balance coming by the end of February. “We want to bring them in fast, but we also want to do it right,” said John McCallum, the immigration minister. Mr. McCallum said the delay was not caused by security concerns after the recent attacks in Paris. Rather, he said, it related to preparing housing and services for the refugees, who will become permanent residents upon entry. Government officials said the selection process would favor families, women who are at risk and gay, lesbian bisexual and transgender people. Single men will be admitted only if they fall under the sexual orientation categories or if they travel with their parents. About 36 cities have agreed to accept Syrian refugees who are to be flown to Canada by the military, which will also provide temporary accommodations for about 6,000 people at some of its bases.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Syrians’ Arrival Is Delayed, and Officials Cite Need to Prepare', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Americas; Canada: Syrians’ Arrival Is Delayed, and Officials Cite Need to Prepare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-25T03:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5224a359-fb6a-599b-b943-5d7c460aa29b', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5224a359-fb6a-599b-b943-5d7c460aa29b'}, {'abstract': 'Henry Ellenson had a team-high 18 points and 11 rebounds in the Legends Classic tournament championship game, an overtime win over Arizona State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/sports/ncaabasketball/freshman-standout-propels-marquette-to-a-title.html', 'snippet': 'Henry Ellenson had a team-high 18 points and 11 rebounds in the Legends Classic tournament championship game, an overtime win over Arizona State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, most of the nation’s top college basketball coaches traveled to tiny Rice Lake, Wis., trying to persuade Henry Ellenson to join their programs. Kentucky’s John Calipari, Duke’s Mike Krzyzewski, North Carolina’s Roy Williams and Michigan State’s Tom Izzo were among those who showed up in the town of 8,000 to woo the 6-foot-10 Ellenson, a forward with guard skills.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/sports/CITY-FANDUEL/CITY-FANDUEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Freshman Standout Propels Marquette to a Title', 'kicker': 'Marquette 78, Arizona State 73, Overtime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freshman Standout Propels Marquette to a Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marquette University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-25T04:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Casey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc1a9fb9-9919-5634-8424-2c161ef84fb2', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc1a9fb9-9919-5634-8424-2c161ef84fb2'}, {'abstract': 'The honor that Princeton bestowed on an unrepentant racist decades ago should be rescinded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/opinion/the-case-against-woodrow-wilson-at-princeton.html', 'snippet': 'The honor that Princeton bestowed on an unrepentant racist decades ago should be rescinded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Student protesters at Princeton performed a valuable public service last week when they demanded that the administration acknowledge the toxic legacy of Woodrow Wilson, who served as university president and New Jersey governor before being elected to the White House. He was an unapologetic racist whose administration rolled back the gains that African-Americans achieved just after the Civil War, purged black workers from influential jobs and transformed the government into an instrument of white supremacy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed1web/25wed1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case Against Woodrow Wilson at Princeton', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Case Against Woodrow Wilson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Woodrow', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, John Abraham (1862-1928)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-25T04:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecacb9d1-5072-5e7d-ac58-66bb9be31f26', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecacb9d1-5072-5e7d-ac58-66bb9be31f26'}, {'abstract': 'Readers share stories about how the former President’s racist policies affected their families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/opinion/readers-weigh-in-woodrow-wilson-cost-my-grandfather-too.html', 'snippet': 'Readers share stories about how the former President’s racist policies affected their families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordon J. Davis’s Nov. 24th Op-Ed, “What Woodrow Wilson Cost My Grandfather,” recounted the story of his grandfather, John Abraham Davis, an African-American man whose prestigious career in the Government Printing Office was destroyed after President Wilson segregated the government in 1913. In recent weeks, students at Princeton — where Woodrow Wilson also served as president — have demanded that his name be removed from university facilities. Below are some highlights from the hundreds of reader comments on the article.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 485}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1655, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wilson-commentsWeb/25wilson-commentsWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodrow Wilson Cost My Grandfather Too', 'kicker': 'Readers Weigh In', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Woodrow', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'