on', 'byline': {'original': 'By Héctor Tobar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Héctor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tobar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf729bc-43c6-545a-95bc-b8613d8fde0c', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf729bc-43c6-545a-95bc-b8613d8fde0c'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s downing of a Russian fighter jet added new uncertainty to an already complicated Syrian civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/opinion/one-jet-closer-to-a-wider-confrontation.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s downing of a Russian fighter jet added new uncertainty to an already complicated Syrian civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turkey’s downing of a Russian fighter jet on Tuesday is just the kind of volatile incident that has been feared since Moscow’s military intervention added new uncertainty to the already complicated Syrian civil war. The attack adds to tensions between Ankara and Moscow, which support different factions in Syria, and threatens to worsen relations between Russia and Turkey’s NATO allies, which have been going downhill since Russia invaded Ukraine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed2/25wed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed2/25wed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 484}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/25/opinion/25wed2/25wed2-jumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015