351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f34b34a0-c8ab-5f7b-9a38-e630510103c3'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain expects aid from U.S. in the form of credits, warplanes, ships and munitions in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/25/1940-britain-expects-aid-from-u-s/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain expects aid from U.S. in the form of credits, warplanes, ships and munitions in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Marquess of Lothian, British Ambassador, who said on his return from London Saturday that the British were nearing the end of their cash resources, had long talks with President Roosevelt and Secretary of State Cordell Hull this afternoon [Nov. 25], after which he told reporters that Great Britain expected substantial aid from the United States next year in the form of credits, warplanes, ships and munitions. However, he said the President had made no promises. —\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 26, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Britain Expects Aid from U.S.', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-25T11:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':