. Simon divorced James Taylor, but covers her upbringing, the early stages of her singing career and her romances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carly Simon would like to correct the notion that she is any kind of bourgeois princess, even if one of the first things she did after marrying in 1972 was to change her Bloomingdale’s charge card to read “Mrs. James Taylor.” Her upbringing as a privileged daughter of Richard L. Simon, a founder of Simon & Schuster, used to be held against her. In her bohemian days — that is, when she wore bohemian clothes — it may even have hurt her professionally. Albert Grossman, the manager whose clients included Bob Dylan, called her “a nine out of a perfect 10,” docked one point because of her prosperous background. It’s rare for managers to take offense at money.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/arts/26BOOKSIMONJP/26BOOKSIMONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/26/arts/26BOOKSIMONJP/26BOOKSIMONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/arts/26BOOKSIMONJP/26BOOKSIMONJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/arts/26BOOKSIMONJP/26BOOKSIMONJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/arts/26BOOKSIMONJP/26BOOKSIMONJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS