l', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c387c220-1d8a-52ee-8d86-52fbc851bd05', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c387c220-1d8a-52ee-8d86-52fbc851bd05'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PENELOPE FITZGERALD: A Life, by Hermione Lee. (Vintage, $17.95.) Elusive and eccentric, Fitzgerald (1916-2000) published her first book, a biography, when she was 58 and went on to win the Man Booker Prize with her third novel a few years later. Lee, a veteran biographer of literary figures (including Edith Wharton and Virginia Woolf), approaches her subject with surgical precision in this volume, one of the Book Review’s 10 Best of 2014.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T01:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joumana Khatib', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khatib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/170a5d21-2f20-553f-8984-20ee25720ef3', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/170a5d21-2f20-553f-8984-20ee25720ef3'}, {'abstract': 'The university reported only 14 of 113 cases of student-reported rape to the federal government because many of the reported assaults occurred off-campus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/26/sports/ncaafootball/fsu-reported-few-rape-cases-to-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'The university reported only 14 of 113 cases of student-reported rape to the federal government because many of the reported assaults occurred off-campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In court papers that Florida State University fought to keep confidential, the former director of the school’s Victim Advocate Office testified that in 2014, a total of 113 students reported being sexually battered, which is the same as rape in Florida. But the college reported only 14 cases to the federal government, records show.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.S.U. Reported Few Rape Cases to the U.S. ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Official Says F.S.U. Reported Few Rapes ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bogdanich, Walt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T01:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walt Bogdanich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bogdanich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a3f00cd-1694-58c6-983b-44bedf233b45', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a3f00cd-1694-58c6-983b-44bedf233b45'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPQR: A History of Ancient Rome, by Mary Beard. (Liveright, $35.) Like New Yorkers, Romans were aggressive and acquisitive and came from somewhere else; Beard’s wonderfully concise history unpacks the secrets of the city’s success.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T01:21:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25eb6279-0c28-5cc2-84ef-3b4ce1179e6a', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25eb6279-0c28-5cc2-84ef-3b4ce1179e6a'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio unveiled a citywide initiative to tackle mental illness and addiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/26/opinion/treating-mental-illness-in-new-york-from-all-angles.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio unveiled a citywide initiative to tackle mental illness and addiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As too many people know only too well, mental health is a world of unmet needs and untold suffering. Society’s ability to identify and treat emotional ailments and addiction is painfully inadequate. Families, left to themselves, struggle and fail. They often lack the resources to confront problems or don’t try: two things in plentiful supply are ignorance and denial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 968, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/26/opinion/26thu2/26thu2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Treating Mental Illness in New York, From All Angles ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treating Mental Illness, From All Angles  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T01:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 