brings back a classic chronograph.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/26/t-magazine/a-1950s-era-timepiece-reborn.html', 'snippet': 'The venerable Swiss brand Vacheron Constantin brings back a classic chronograph.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the time chronograph technology started to catch on in the late 1800s until the middle of the 20th century, the venerable Swiss brand Vacheron Constantin produced highly coveted timepieces. But in 1955, it stopped making the wristwatches, which had become too elaborately wonkish to suit changing tastes. Although the company began gingerly reintroducing chronographs in the late 1980s, the final ’50s-era model, the Cornes de Vache, continued to obsess collectors. Only 36 were ever made: 26 in yellow gold, eight in rose gold and two in platinum. Now the company has reinterpreted the design. The Historiques Cornes de Vache 1955, available only in platinum, is, like the original, a sober classic distinguished by its cow-horn-shaped lugs. But a slightly wider face gives the watch a more modern, balanced look and feel. With its raised Roman numerals, midnight-blue alligator strap, sapphire-hued tachometric dial and clear crystal back, it makes keeping track of time an immeasurable pleasure.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '98', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/06/t-magazine/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0/06tmag-13qual_thing_watch-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A 1950s-Era Timepiece, Reborn', 'kicker': 'Watch Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Thing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hass, Nancy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vacheron Constantin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Hass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6aa38ef-d8f5-50fe-a00f-d2d9744e557e', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6aa38ef-d8f5-50fe-a00f-d2d9744e557e'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Tension ends in Italy as the Axis powers meet in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/26/1940-italy-breathes-easier-after-pact/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Tension ends in Italy as the Axis powers meet in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The diplomatic offensive launched by the Axis powers against Great Britain after the meeting between Benito Mussolini and Fuehrer Adolf Hitler at Brenner Pass is believed here tonight [Nov. 27] to have ended for the time being. Tension in Rome over a possible imminent spread of war in the Balkans also has passed suddenly. In the highest diplomatic circles, it was said today that no signing of any agreement by either of the Axis powers with Bulgaria was likely soon. Turkey, armed to the teeth under martial law and moving up fresh divisions toward the Bulgarian border, may also be expected to remain out of the war for some time.\xa0—\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 27, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/blogs/27iht-oldnov27-musso/27iht-oldnov27-musso-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/blogs/27iht-oldnov27-musso/27iht-oldnov27-musso-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/blogs/27iht-oldnov27-musso/27iht-oldnov27-musso-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSta