1823447-70ac-5bd9-986a-6f1f90166d78', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31823447-70ac-5bd9-986a-6f1f90166d78'}, {'abstract': 'The photography exhibition “ADSVMVS ABSVMVS” is a mordantly wacky, show-and-tell stand-up routine on mortality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/arts/design/hollis-framptons-singular-sensibility.html', 'snippet': 'The photography exhibition “ADSVMVS ABSVMVS” is a mordantly wacky, show-and-tell stand-up routine on mortality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker, photographer, essayist, poet, teacher, fabulist and proto-digital pioneer Hollis Frampton (1936-1984) eased off on producing photography after the 1960s but came back to it at the end of his too-short life. His final work in the medium, a portfolio of 14 pictures with the curious title “ADSVMVS ABSVMVS,” makes up this exhibition, which is also — but how can this be? — his New York gallery solo debut.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 726}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 847, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1693, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1/27FRAMPTON1GALLERY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollis Frampton’s Singular Sensibility', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hollis Frampton’s Singular Sensibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frampton, Hollis (1936-84)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T21:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/95fd14e0-6905-5ad0-926a-cc7e9735bd89', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95fd14e0-6905-5ad0-926a-cc7e9735bd89'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary recounts the emotional wounds Janis Joplin sustained growing up as the antithesis of the all-American prom-queen ideal in Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/movies/review-in-janis-little-girl-blue-exploring-joplins-demons.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary recounts the emotional wounds Janis Joplin sustained growing up as the antithesis of the all-American prom-queen ideal in Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Amy Berg’s documentary “Janis: Little Girl Blue,” the sound that erupts from Janis Joplin singing the ’60s R&B classic “Cry Baby” comes as close as I’ve heard to a grown-up singer capturing a baby’s primal squall. Heard today, this raw, insistent scream, from Joplin’s posthumously released 1971 album, “Pearl,” is as disturbing and powerful as ever.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27JANIS1/27JANIS1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Janis: Little Girl Blue,’ Exploring Joplin’s Demons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take Another Little Piece of Her Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berg, Amy (1970- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blues Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joplin, Janis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Janis: Little Girl Blue (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T21:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5d0ee2-6656-5f10-ae17-ff499538f7b9', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5d0ee2-6656-5f10-ae17-ff499538f7b9'}, {'abstract': 'A number of galleries are showcasing works by women at the annual art fair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/arts/design/art-basel-miami-beach-a-focus-on-female-artists.html', 'snippet': 'A number of galleries are showcasing works by women at the annual art fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may come a day when having a critical mass of women featured in an art fair is no longer noteworthy, but we’re not there yet. So it’s worth noting that Art Basel Miami Beach, which starts next week, has a significant number of female artists.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1627, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27INSIDERART1/27INSIDERART1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Basel Miami Beach: A Focus on Female Artists', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women in Focus in Miami Beach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art Basel Miami Beach', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major':