astasia Lin, Miss World Canada (and Rights Advocate)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Bars a Rights Activist Who Wields a Tiara and Sash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Contests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Anastasia (1990- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miss World Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Falun Gong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T22:05:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b525191-90ba-507f-87d3-d1b72c178f97', 'word_count': 1503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b525191-90ba-507f-87d3-d1b72c178f97'}, {'abstract': 'In Tom Hooper’s new film, Eddie Redmayne and Alicia Vikander portray the 1920s artists Einar and Gerda Wegener as Einar became Lili Elbe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/movies/review-the-danish-girl-about-a-transgender-pioneer.html', 'snippet': 'In Tom Hooper’s new film, Eddie Redmayne and Alicia Vikander portray the 1920s artists Einar and Gerda Wegener as Einar became Lili Elbe.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Danish Girl,” Tom Hooper’s new film, is a story of individual struggle that is also a portrait of a marriage. In this respect and others it resembles “The King’s Speech,” Mr. Hooper’s earlier historical drama, a multiple Oscar winner a few years ago. In that case, the union of George VI and Elizabeth, the Queen Mother, was the foundation on which the tale of George’s elocutionary striving was built. Here, the marriage is bohemian rather than aristocratic, but the stakes, while personal, are every bit as profound and consequential as the matters of state that drove the monarch to the microphone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1053, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27DANISHGIRL/27DANISHGIRL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Danish Girl,’ About a Transgender Pioneer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Emotional Transformation for a Man and a Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hooper, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redmayne, Eddie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schoenaerts, Matthias', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elbe, Lili (1882-1931)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vikander, Alicia (1988- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Danish Girl (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T22:07:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60616522-bef7-53fa-a2d5-8931f3f7f540', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60616522-bef7-53fa-a2d5-8931f3f7f540'}, {'abstract': 'David Morales choreographs and stars in this work that centers on the Spanish poet Federico García Lorca and his last affair with a man, Juan Ramírez de Lucas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/arts/dance/review-lorca-madly-in-love-portrays-a-forbidden-romance-through-flamenco.html', 'snippet': 'David Morales choreographs and stars in this work that centers on the Spanish poet Federico García Lorca and his last affair with a man, Juan Ramírez de Lucas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the great Spanish poet and playwright Federico García Lorca was assassinated during the Spanish Civil War, his homosexuality was concealed and suppressed for decades. In contemporary Spain, the truth is now widely acknowledged, but for an artist to treat the subject frankly, especially in the tradition-bound world of flamenco, as David Morales does in his show “Lorca Madly in Love,” still counts as taboo-breaking and bold.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 671}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1976, 'width': 1768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/arts/27LORCA/27LORCA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Lorca Madly in Love’ Portrays a Forbidden Romance Through Flamenco', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tale of a Forbidden Affair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamenco (Dance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Lorca, Federico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morales, David (1971- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-26T22:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a4f5ed9-3183-5700-893f-fe80d908d69b', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a4f5ed9-3183-5700-893f-fe80d908d69b'}, {'abstract': 'Today, even some critics of Ralph Nader’s 1965 book acknowledge its impact on the auto industry and safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/automobiles/50-years-ago-unsafe-at-any-speed-shook-the-auto-world.html', 'snippet': 'Today, even some critics of Ralph Nader’s 1965 book acknowledge its impact on the auto industry and safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FEW DRIVERS could imagine owning a car these days that did not come with airbags, antilock brakes and seatbelts. But 50 years ago motorists went without such basic safety features.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/27/business/27WHEELS1/27WHEELS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/27/business/27WHEELS1/27WHEELS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheig