love, sex and death.” He keeps those ideas in his back pocket, as he captures stark black-and-white photos on film of simple New York moments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pictures suggest a murder mystery, or at least a thickening plot. But the truth is far more innocent. These photographs were taken by Jason Langer, who lives in Portland, Ore., when he was visiting friends in New York City.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding the Noir Without Looking', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding the Noir Without Looking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-27T08:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab454a8b-2a40-5148-965f-f9a8ac704ddc', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab454a8b-2a40-5148-965f-f9a8ac704ddc'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican front-runner has outlined a series of measures that would make the United States an authoritarian nightmare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/27/opinion/donald-trumps-police-state.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican front-runner has outlined a series of measures that would make the United States an authoritarian nightmare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Plot Against America,” the novelist Philip Roth imagines an alternative history at the dawn of World War II. Charles A. Lindbergh, aviator hero and crypto-fascist, defeats Franklin D. Roosevelt in 1940. Rather than go to war against Nazi Germany