 the World Boxing Association’s middleweight champion. Before that, he was a cancer survivor. Mr. Jacobs, 28, learned he had osteosarcoma in 2011, which could have ended his career. Instead, after surgery and radiation, he returned to the ring 19 months later and has been undefeated since. He is set to defend his title against Peter Quillin at Barclays Center next Saturday. In the months before a fight, Mr. Jacobs lives and trains on Long Island, leaving only to spend Sundays in Brooklyn with his partner, Natalie Stevens, 28, a makeup artist, and their son, Nathaniel Jacobs, 6. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE1/29ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 