minine Persuasion: Ann Hampton Callaway Celebrates Women Songwriters.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ann Hampton Callaway belongs to the school of gifted pop singers for whom majestic vocal display is not enough. Along with Barbra Streisand and Celine Dion, to name two obvious examples, Ms. Callaway uses pyrotechnics as a platform for conveying inspirational messages of peace and hope. And the opening-night performance of her new show at Feinstein’s/54 Below, “Feminine Persuasion: Ann Hampton Callaway Celebrates Women Songwriters,” often had a sticky undertone of sentimentality.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ann Hampton Callaway Honors Her Predecessors at Feinstein’s/54 Below', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Her Body Now Swings With Her Voice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callaway, Ann Hampton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-27T20:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7aca77-5ad2-5ccd-95fe-85ff2c444fc2', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7aca77-5ad2-5ccd-95fe-85ff2c444fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities responded to an “active shooter” near a Planned Parenthood clinic in Colorado Springs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/11/27/us/colorado-springs-shooting-map.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities responded to an “active shooter” near a Planned Parenthood clinic in Colorado Springs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Authorities responded to an “active shooter” near a Planned Parenthood clinic in Colorado Springs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting in Planned Parenthood Clinic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-27T20:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b8f609b8-b5ad-5411-9181-3ad427643143', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b8f609b8-b5ad-5411-9181-3ad427643143'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike its domestic peers, the Spanish bank didn’t lend to the teetering engineering group. Nor did it invest in Bankia’s failed I.P.O. or Spain’s bad bank, Sareb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/28/business/dealbook/the-pain-in-spain-falls-mainly-away-from-bbva.html', 'snippet': 'Unlike its domestic peers, the Spanish bank didn’t lend to the teetering engineering group. Nor did it invest in Bankia’s failed I.P.O. or Spain’s bad bank, Sareb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BBVA, Spain’s second-largest bank, is often seen as more conservative than its Spanish peers. That reputation now looks deserved. The bank is the only major domestic player that does not have exposure to Abengoa, the Spanish engineering company seeking protection from its creditors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pain in Spain Falls Mainly Away From BBVA', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-27T21:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fiona Maharg-Bravo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fiona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maharg-Bravo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58f7b384-b5a6-56a3-9e2b-02de80acaefd', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58f7b384-b5a6-56a3-9e2b-02de80acaefd'}, {'abstract': 'The Harrison restaurant lists more than 40 kinds of pie, such as margherita and meatball, and sweet variations like Nutella and vanilla bean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/nyregion/restaurant-review-porta-napoli-offers-pizza-for-every-palate.html', 'snippet': 'The Harrison restaurant lists more than 40 kinds of pie, such as margherita and meatball, and sweet variations like Nutella and vanilla bean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early September, Porta Napoli in Harrison took the place of Rue des Crepes, known for its theatrical Parisian décor and its neatly folded buckwheat crepes. It is Naples, not Paris, that the new proprietors hope to bring to mind. “Authenticity” is the catchword. Wood embers glow in a fire-engine-red pizza oven, which spreads cheer like a giant emoji. Menu headings are in Italian (sfizi, insalate, pizze rossi, pizze bianche). The flour in the supple pizza dough is “00” (doppio zero), as required by the Associazione Verace Pizza Napoletana. The wine list covers regions from Sicily to the Alps but never strays beyond Italy’s borders.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 522, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 522}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1781, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINEWE3/29DINEWE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Porta Napoli Offers Pizza for Every Palate', 'kicker': 'Dining | Hudson Valley', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '<p>A Place for Pizza, From Savory to Sweet</p>', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrison (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pizza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porta Napoli (Harrison, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-27T21:11:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8a21baa-ba6a-56b2-ba82-0b907d608f31', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8a21baa-ba6a-56b2-ba82-0b907d608f31'}, {'abstract': 'At Taberna, the food is traditional Portuguese as seen through the eyes of an imaginative, skilled chef. But this sharp focus does not mean monotony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/travel/london-restaurant-review-taberna-do-mercado.html', 'snippet': 'At Taberna, the food is traditional Portuguese as seen through the eyes of an imaginative, skilled chef. But this sharp focus does not mean monotony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the chef Nuno Mendes was born in Lisbon and trained mostly in the United States, it’s his London restaurants — Chiltern Firehouse, for example — that have gained attention. His latest is Taberna do Mercado in East London’s Old Spitalfields Market. The informal, tightly packed 40-seat restaurant (with additional tables and a charcoal grill outside) looks like a sleek version of a Portuguese tavern: nothing fancy, but with plenty of attention to materials and details (including seating that is all too authentic: Some of the wooden chairs are really too small for grown-ups). The atmosphere is convivial; we had fun at the tiny concrete-topped bar, drinking and watching sausages being sliced.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/travel/29BITES/29BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'imag