e': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/768a9942-c62f-5e1c-a886-ca4140efe159', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/768a9942-c62f-5e1c-a886-ca4140efe159'}, {'abstract': 'Good looks aside, for Long Islanders the draw at Sandbar is Guy Reuge, the award-winning Frenchman who opened Mirabelle Restaurant in St. James in 1983.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/nyregion/restaurant-review-at-sandbar-familiar-french-hands-behind-the-menu.html', 'snippet': 'Good looks aside, for Long Islanders the draw at Sandbar is Guy Reuge, the award-winning Frenchman who opened Mirabelle Restaurant in St. James in 1983.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sandbar, a sparkling new restaurant that opened in Cold Spring Harbor in late September, is a beauty. Diners enter through a bar with a soaring glass ceiling and emerge into an elegant dining room with plenty of windows, 11 chandeliers and pale, sand-colored walls. The light, bright room nonetheless has a subdued nautical look, with antique mahogany half hulls lining the walls, along with lovely paintings of the harbor by local artists.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINELI3/29DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINELI3/29DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/29DINELI3/29DINELI3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio