itorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Affordable Housing vs. Gentrification  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-28T02:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/754f41c4-2cc4-5f99-9bdd-63630b561dee', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/754f41c4-2cc4-5f99-9bdd-63630b561dee'}, {'abstract': 'Parisians won’t admit that they go to the gym, let alone that they’re scared of terrorists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/28/opinion/frances-cult-of-fearlessness.html', 'snippet': 'Parisians won’t admit that they go to the gym, let alone that they’re scared of terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris — SINCE the attacks two weeks ago, I’ve been avoiding supermarkets — which seem like potential targets — and doing most of my shopping at a minimarket. The cashier there, a young man from Mali, keeps telling me not to be afraid.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank