ajor league team’s minor league affiliate based in Havana, but its first mission is to build good will.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAVANA — A minibus of Americans rumbled through a city in transformation, past the run-down housing and round-the-clock construction, the sparsely stocked bodegas and chic new restaurants, to a reception at the residence of the American chargés d’affaires. The hint of change teased the November night.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/sports/CUBANBASEBALL-1/CUBANBASEBALL-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pitch Is Framed by Diplomacy in Cuba', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pitch Framed by Diplomacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwechheimer, Lou (1955- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caribbean Baseball Initiative', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minor Leagues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-28T17:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efdd8b57-e8a2-5b9d-996d-3d60a7e30e45', 'word_count': 2547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efdd8b57-e8a2-5b9d-996d-3d60a7e30e45'}, {'abstract': 'Hicks good, Friedman/Phelps not so much.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/28/demand-supply-and-macroeconomic-models/', 'snippet': 'Hicks good, Friedman/Phelps not so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m supposed to do a presentation next week about “shifts in economic models,” which has me trying to systematize my thought about what the crisis and aftermath have and haven’t changed my understanding of macroeconomics. And it seems to me that there is an important theme here: it’s the supply side, stupid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demand, Supply, and Macroeconomic Models', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'c