.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alberto Serrano has declared war on the shock troops of gentrification: hipsters. He has chosen as his front line a part of the Bronx, specifically a stretch along Walton Avenue in the Mount Hope neighborhood, which — for now — is free from goofy bars, twee crochet sculptures and overpriced cafes. His weapon? A huge mural depicting a grand comic-strip battle of the hip versus the hopeful.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/nyregion/30SIDE/30SIDE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Wall in the West Bronx, a Gentrification Battle Rages', 'kicker': 'Side Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking a Battle Over Gentrification to a Wall in the Bronx ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrano, Alberto (Artist)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-29T15:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bbca0d8-95c7-56ee-9dc8-1e23b06261c8', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bbca0d8-95c7-56ee-9dc8-1e23b06261c8'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy says it has brought the Greek advance to a standstill in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/29/1940-rome-declares-counterattack-has-halted-foe/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy says it has brought the Greek advance to a standstill in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Stiff counter-attacks by reinforced and reorganized Italian troops were said here tonight [Nov. 29] to have brought the Greek advance in Albania to a standstill. As the high command announced a turn for the better in the tide of battle, Gen. Ubaldo Soddu, who went to Albania recently to take command at the front, received promotion by royal decree. Greek efforts to advance yesterday, the high command said, were stopped by a counter-attack of the Ferrara, Siena and Centauro divisions of the 11th Army Corps. In the Koritza sector of the 9th Army Corps, all was reported quiet. Authoritative quarters were denied reports that the Greeks had captured Argyrokastron, one of the Italian bases in Albania, and that Gen. Pietro Badoglio had taken up headquarters in Tirana. Badoglio is in Rome, it was said, and Soddu is in supreme command at the front.\xa0—\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, November 30, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Rome Declares Counterattack Has Halted Foe', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-29T16:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b22e3758-b16b-5da1-8a63-93a362b45066', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b22e3758-b16b-5da1-8a63-93a362b45066'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Stephen G. Breyer suggests the court should check abroad for guidance because about 20 percent of cases are affected by what happens outside the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/us/politics/breyer-sees-value-in-us-supreme-courts-looking-to-foreign-law.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Stephen G. Breyer suggests the court should check abroad for guidance because about 20 percent of cases are affected by what happens outside the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Justice Stephen G. Breyer, a progressive force on the United States Supreme Court for more than two decades, advocates the courts taking into account foreign law. That’s the stuff of a good debate, befitting a justice who got to the bench courtesy of former President Ronald Reagan and the archconservative Senator Strom Thurmond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 747}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1645, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/us/30letter-web/30letter-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': 