maginable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s enough truth to the glaring streak of self-loathing that runs throughout the seventh episode of “Jessica Jones” to make it both palatable and believable. That’s no small feat for an episode that encourages viewers to forgive Jones, but never forces her to confront the demons that she’s courting. Instead of accepting and confronting the guilt she feels over killing Reva Connors, Jones yo-yos between steps two and four of the five stages of grief: anger and depression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/29/arts/jessicajones7/jessicajones7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 1