, 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T08:33:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9987c977-84bf-51f8-b33e-14023f4ab8cd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9987c977-84bf-51f8-b33e-14023f4ab8cd'}, {'abstract': 'The only thing keeping the country in the digital dark ages is the government’s fear of a more open society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/opinion/time-to-bring-cuba-online.html', 'snippet': 'The only thing keeping the country in the digital dark ages is the government’s fear of a more open society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of Cuban citizens could have affordable access to the Internet in a matter of months. The only thing keeping the island in the digital Dark Ages is a lack of political will. Cuban officials have long blamed the American embargo for their nation’s obsolete telecommunications systems. They no longer have that excuse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Bring Cuba Online', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Bring Cuba Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T09:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/25e694af-6741-5d5c-ad43-ac5f99538936', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25e694af-6741-5d5c-ad43-ac5f99538936'}, {'abstract': 'Lo único que impide que millones de cubanos tengan acceso a Internet a un precio razonable es la falta de voluntad política.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/opinion/es-hora-de-conectar-a-cuba-a-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Lo único que impide que millones de cubanos tengan acceso a Internet a un precio razonable es la falta de voluntad política.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millones de cubanos podrían tener acceso a Internet a un precio moderado en cuestión de meses. Lo único que mantiene a Cuba en las tinieblas en plena era digital es la falta de voluntad política. Desde hace mucho tiempo, los líderes cubanos han dicho que el deplorable estado de la infraestructura de telecomunicaciones en la isla es culpa del embargo de Estados Unidos. Ya no tienen esa excusa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/opinion/30mon1/30mon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Es hora de conectar a Cuba a Internet', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 