, {'abstract': 'Do you believe in mind reading? Try this experiment in clairvoyance with the late recreational mathematician, Martin Gardner.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/gardner-impromptu/', 'snippet': 'Do you believe in mind reading? Try this experiment in clairvoyance with the late recreational mathematician, Martin Gardner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Gardner was a giant in the recreational math world — many of the puzzles we take on\xa0each week here at Numberplay are direct descendants of the many counter-intuitive conundra\xa0that Gardner curated\xa0in the\xa020th century. He was such a significant force in math puzzles that we forget — or have a hard time really believing — that he had other lives, including that of a popular and influential magician. This week I’m pleased to present a book that captures this magical life: Martin Gardner’s Impromptu. The book is absolutely gorgeous: beautifully designed and full of detail, with\xa0hundreds of pages of original notes and sketches by Martin Gardner (the book itself is over 800 pages long). Click\xa0here to enjoy selections from the color section of the book, and here for an introduction to MiniTrix, a series of short videos featuring Martin Gardner performing various impromptu tricks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martin Gardner’s Impromptu', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magic and Magicians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carroll, Lewis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardner, Martin (1914-2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'valu