ncies on Monday, a milestone decision by the International Monetary Fund that underscores the country’s rising financial and economic heft.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Renminbi Is Approved by I.M.F. as a Main World Currency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.M.F. Adds China’s Currency to Elite Global Financial Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T17:21:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26c60767-320e-5e50-a724-6d91ee32c7b7', 'word_count': 1691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26c60767-320e-5e50-a724-6d91ee32c7b7'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Vincent T. DeVita Jr. provides a rare view of the struggle to move cancer treatment into the modern age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/12/01/science/review-science-and-politics-collide-in-the-death-of-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Vincent T. DeVita Jr. provides a rare view of the struggle to move cancer treatment into the modern age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scene is a wild cocktail party in Washington at the tail end of the Kennedy administration. Our innocent young narrator, new to the rituals of power, watches in fascination as one of his superiors dances by with a half-undressed woman slung over a shoulder. By the end of the evening, he has helped hoist another of his bosses, dead drunk, out of a bathtub.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 874}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 704, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1407, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/science/01SCIBOOK/01SCIBOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Science and Politics Collide in ‘The Death of Cancer’', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unbowed Warrior', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeVita, Vincent T Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Cancer Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemotherapy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mastectomy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death of Cancer (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T17:21:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.d', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba3c57d-4fe2-55c3-9d4c-1b158bb5a8e7', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba3c57d-4fe2-55c3-9d4c-1b158bb5a8e7'}, {'abstract': 'The investment bank may have no problem continuing business as usual after the Petrobras scandal. But that’s not always how banking works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/12/01/business/dealbook/btg-pactual-has-strengths-but-they-may-not-be-enough.html', 'snippet': 'The investment bank may have no problem continuing business as usual after the Petrobras scandal. But that’s not always how banking works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BTG Pactual, Brazil’s No. 1 investment bank, may do fine without André Esteves, who quit as chairman and chief executive on Sunday. But that will depend on the bank retaining the trust of trading partners and customers through the crisis caused by Mr. Esteves’s arrest as part of Brazil’s wide-ranging investigation into corruption at the national oil giant Petrobras.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BTG Pactual Has Strengths, but They May Not Be Enough', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BTG Pactual', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esteves, Andre Santos (1969- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T17:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d961710-9220-5ccf-b473-c530bb45a979', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d961710-9220-5ccf-b473-c530bb45a979'}, {'abstract': 'The Times is dropping “Rodham” from its references to Hillary Clinton, reflecting how the Democratic candidate for president refers to herself these days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/30/times-drops-rodham-in-referring-to-hillary-clinton/', 'snippet': 'The Times is dropping “Rodham” from its references to Hillary Clinton, reflecting how the Democratic candidate for president refers to herself these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Bill Clinton lost the governor’s seat in Arkansas in 1980, Hillary Rodham (reluctantly) took the name Clinton. “I learned the hard way that some voters in Arkansas were seriously offended by the fact that I kept my maiden name,” she wrote years later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur