s://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/t-magazine/molly-crabapple-drawing-blood-book.html', 'snippet': 'Molly Crabapple’s new memoir, “Drawing Blood,” charts the artist and writer’s progress from sketching club founder to political correspondent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Molly Crabapple made her name in 2005 as the founder of Dr. Sketchy’s Anti-Art School — a sketching club with scores of chapters around the world where the nude models were the stars — then as house artist for the Box nightclub, where she lined the New York demi-monde in a style recalling both Aubrey Beardsley and Toulouse-Lautrec. Recently, however, Crabapple has reinvented herself as a political reporter, returning dispatches from places like Guantanamo Bay, the Gaza Strip and Syrian refugee camps for publications like the Guardian, Vanity Fair and Vice, where she’s a contributing editor. Her new memoir, “Drawing Blood” ($30, out Dec. 1 from Harper Collins) chronicles this transformation, and, fittingly, it’s the first book Crabapple is releasing as a writer rather than an illustrator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/t-magazine/30tmag-crabapple-1/30tmag-crabapple-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/30/t-magazine/30tmag-crabapple-1/30tmag-crabapple-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/t-magazine/30tmag-crabapple-1/30tmag-crabapple-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/t-magazine/30tmag-crabapple-1/30tmag-crabapple-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1566, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJu