Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34b049d0-f045-547b-bac0-cecb9febd162', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34b049d0-f045-547b-bac0-cecb9febd162'}, {'abstract': 'The unorthodox exchange was a public hint of the behind-the-scenes tumult that has surrounded Tribune Publishing in recent months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/12/01/business/media/tweet-from-rupert-murdoch-about-sale-brings-a-denial-from-tribune.html', 'snippet': 'The unorthodox exchange was a public hint of the behind-the-scenes tumult that has surrounded Tribune Publishing in recent months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday morning, Los Angeles Times employees were greeted with an unusual message from their corporate parent company, Tribune Publishing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/01/business/01latimes-web1/01latimes-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tweet From Rupert Murdoch About Sale Brings a Denial From Tribune', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tribune Counters Rumor Los Angeles Times Is for Sale ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Publishing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Tribune', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broad, Eli', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T20:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d163ed6f-6077-5f82-92c4-92cf8b0a9076', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d163ed6f-6077-5f82-92c4-92cf8b0a9076'}, {'abstract': 'Things changed around 1990.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/hyperglobalization-and-global-inequality/', 'snippet': 'Things changed around 1990.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve mentioned before that I’m a big fan of work by my CUNY colleague Branko Milanovic showing that if you look at income growth by percentile of the whole world population for the past 25 years, you see “twin peaks”: rapid growth near the middle, representing China’s middle class, and at the top, representing the global elite, with a sag in the region representing the OECD working class. But was it always thus? I asked Branko what a similar picture looked like for the previous generation — and he has obliged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hyperglobalization and Global Inequality', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-11-30T20:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/514dce52-8aeb-5f9c-9561-b03d2aa37e31', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514dce52-8aeb-5f9c-9561-b03d2aa37e31'}, {'abstract': 'Should we be surprised when the language of brutality and violence boils over into the real thing?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/11/30/magazine/planned-parenthood-and-the-tinderbox-of-abortion-rhetoric.html', 'snippet': 'Should we be surprised when the language of brutality and violence boils over into the real thing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abortion opponents have been quick to distance themselves from the Nov. 27 shooting at a Planned Parenthood clinic in Colorado Springs, which left three people dead. The anti-abortion groups lining up to condemn the violence included the Center for Medical Progress, which released videos in July accusing Planned Parenthood of selling fetal parts and tissue. Planned Parenthood denied making sales, saying one of its 700 health centers was being reimbursed for supplying fetal tissue to researchers, who have used fetal cells to produce lifesaving vaccines and treatments. But the doctor caught on camera spoke in graphic medical terms while sipping wine over lunch, and the videos prompted five separate congressional investigations into Planned Parenthood’s practices. Testifying before a House committee in October, the group’s president, Cecile Richards, said it would continue facilitating the tissue donations, with patients’ consent, but stop accepting reimbursements. The Center for Medical Progress called this “an admission of guilt.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/magazine/30mag-abortion-1/30mag-abortion-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/30/magazine/30mag-abortion-1/30mag-abortion-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/magazine/30mag-abortion-1/30mag-abortion-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/magazine/30mag-abortion-1/30mag-abortion-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/30/magazine/30mag-abortion-1/30mag-abortion-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':